      וְלֹא תִתְחַתֵּן בָּם בִּתְּךָ לֹא־תִתֵּן לִבְנוֹ וּבִתּוֹ לֹא־תִקַּח לִבְנֶֽךָ׃
    → And do not give them to your children. Do not give them to your sons, and do not take them as your own children.
    Deuteronomy 7:4
      כִּֽי־יָסִיר אֶת־בִּנְךָ מֵֽאַחֲרַי וְעָבְדוּ אֱלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים וְחָרָה אַף־יְהוָה בָּכֶם וְהִשְׁמִידְךָ מַהֵֽר׃
    → For he will take away your throne from you, and others will worship other gods instead. Then Jehovah will also reject you, and he will destroy you quickly.
    Deuteronomy 7:5
      כִּֽי־אִם־כֹּה תַעֲשׂוּ לָהֶם מִזְבְּחֹתֵיהֶם תִּתֹּצוּ וּמַצֵּבֹתָם תְּשַׁבֵּרוּ וַאֲשֵֽׁירֵהֶם תְּגַדֵּעוּן וּפְסִילֵיהֶם תִּשְׂרְפוּן בָּאֵֽשׁ׃
    → For if you do these things for them, then their altars will be destroyed, and their places of worship will be torn down. Their offerings will be burned, and their idols will be destroyed by fire.
    Deuteronomy 7:6
      כִּי עַם קָדוֹשׁ אַתָּה לַיהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ בְּךָ בָּחַר ׀ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לִהְיוֹת לוֹ לְעַם סְגֻלָּה מִכֹּל הָֽעַמִּים אֲשֶׁר עַל־פְּנֵי הָאֲדָמָֽה׃
    → For you, O Holy One, are chosen by Jehovah your God to be His people, a people of choice among all the nations that lie before the earth.
    Deuteronomy 7:7
      לֹא מֵֽרֻבְּכֶם מִכָּל־הָֽעַמִּים חָשַׁק יְהוָה בָּכֶם וַיִּבְחַר בָּכֶם כִּֽי־אַתֶּם הַמְעַט מִכָּל־הָעַמִּֽים׃
    → You are not the most important people among all nations. Yet Jehovah has chosen you, because you are the least important among all nations.
    Deuteronomy 7:8
      כִּי מֵֽאַהֲבַת יְהוָה אֶתְכֶם וּמִשָּׁמְרוּ אֶת־הַשְּׁבֻעָה אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶם הוֹצִיא יְהוָה אֶתְכֶם בְּיָד חֲזָקָה וַֽיִּפְדְּךָ מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים מִיַּד פַּרְעֹה מֶֽלֶךְ־מִצְרָֽיִם׃
    → For Jehovah loves you, and he has kept the covenant that was made with your ancestors. Therefore, Jehovah has brought you forth with strength, and he has saved you from being slaves under the rule of Pharaoh, the king of Egypt.
    Deuteronomy 7:9
      וְיָדַעְתָּ כִּֽי־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הָֽאֱלֹהִים הָאֵל הַֽנֶּאֱמָן שֹׁמֵר הַבְּרִית וְהַחֶסֶד לְאֹהֲבָיו וּלְשֹׁמְרֵי מִצְוֺתָיו לְאֶלֶף דּֽוֹר׃
    → And you shall know that Jehovah your God is the true God who keeps the covenant and the mercy for those who love Him, and who protects His commandments for ever.
    Deuteronomy 7:10
      וּמְשַׁלֵּם לְשֹׂנְאָיו אֶל־פָּנָיו לְהַאֲבִידוֹ לֹא יְאַחֵר לְשֹׂנְאוֹ אֶל־פָּנָיו יְשַׁלֶּם־לֽוֹ׃
    → And he will repay those who hate him with their own hands. He will take them away from their homes; no one else will be able to harm them. He will repay those who hate him with their own hands.
    Deuteronomy 7:11
      וְשָׁמַרְתָּ אֶת־הַמִּצְוָה וְאֶת־הַֽחֻקִּים וְאֶת־הַמִּשְׁפָּטִים אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם לַעֲשׂוֹתָֽם׃
    → And you have kept the commandments, and the laws, and the judgments that I command you to carry out today.
    Deuteronomy 7:12
      וְהָיָה ׀ עֵקֶב תִּשְׁמְעוּן אֵת הַמִּשְׁפָּטִים הָאֵלֶּה וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְשָׁמַר יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְךָ אֶֽת־הַבְּרִית וְאֶת־הַחֶסֶד אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → And because you heard these laws and kept them, and obeyed them, then Jehovah your God will fulfill to you the covenant and the blessings that were promised to your ancestors.
    Deuteronomy 7:13
      וַאֲהֵבְךָ וּבֵרַכְךָ וְהִרְבֶּךָ וּבֵרַךְ פְּרִֽי־בִטְנְךָ וּפְרִֽי־אַדְמָתֶךָ דְּגָנְךָ וְתִֽירֹשְׁךָ וְיִצְהָרֶךָ שְׁגַר־אֲלָפֶיךָ וְעַשְׁתְּרֹת צֹאנֶךָ עַל הָֽאֲדָמָה אֲשֶׁר־נִשְׁבַּע לַאֲבֹתֶיךָ לָתֶת לָֽךְ׃
    → And I will love you, bless you, and multiply your crops and the fruits of your land. Your cattle and your livestock will increase greatly. All your possessions on this land will be blessed to you, just as your ancestors were blessed.
    Deuteronomy 7:14
      בָּרוּךְ תִּֽהְיֶה מִכָּל־הָעַמִּים לֹא־יִהְיֶה בְךָ עָקָר וַֽעֲקָרָה וּבִבְהֶמְתֶּֽךָ׃
    → May it be blessed among all nations; there shall be no poverty or destitution in you.
    Deuteronomy 7:15
      וְהֵסִיר יְהוָה מִמְּךָ כָּל־חֹלִי וְכָל־מַדְוֵי מִצְרַיִם הָרָעִים אֲשֶׁר יָדַעְתָּ לֹא יְשִׂימָם בָּךְ וּנְתָנָם בְּכָל־שֹׂנְאֶֽיךָ׃
    → And Jehovah will remove from you all your diseases and all the evil things of Egypt that you knew would not be beneficial to you. He will give them over to those who hate you.
    Deuteronomy 7:16
      וְאָכַלְתָּ אֶת־כָּל־הָֽעַמִּים אֲשֶׁר יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ לֹא־תָחֹס עֵֽינְךָ עֲלֵיהֶם וְלֹא תַעֲבֹד אֶת־אֱלֹהֵיהֶם כִּֽי־מוֹקֵשׁ הוּא לָֽךְ׃
    → And you shall eat all the nations that Yahweh your God gives you. Do not look at them with contempt, and do not worship their gods, for that would be too difficult for you.
    Deuteronomy 7:17
      כִּי תֹאמַר בִּלְבָבְךָ רַבִּים הַגּוֹיִם הָאֵלֶּה מִמֶּנִּי אֵיכָה אוּכַל לְהוֹרִישָֽׁם׃
    → For if you say in your heart, “These nations are better than me; how can I possibly defeat them?”
    Deuteronomy 7:18
      לֹא תִירָא מֵהֶם זָכֹר תִּזְכֹּר אֵת אֲשֶׁר־עָשָׂה יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְפַרְעֹה וּלְכָל־מִצְרָֽיִם׃
    → Do not be afraid of them. Remember what Jehovah your God has done for Pharaoh and for all the Egyptians.
    Deuteronomy 7:19
      הַמַּסֹּת הַגְּדֹלֹת אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וְהָאֹתֹת וְהַמֹּֽפְתִים וְהַיָּד הַחֲזָקָה וְהַזְּרֹעַ הַנְּטוּיָה אֲשֶׁר הוֹצִֽאֲךָ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ כֵּֽן־יַעֲשֶׂה יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְכָל־הָעַמִּים אֲשֶׁר־אַתָּה יָרֵא מִפְּנֵיהֶֽם׃
    → The great miracles that your eyes have seen, and the strong hands and arms, and the branches that Jehovah your God has brought forth from the vineyard. Thus will Jehovah your God do for all the nations who fear you.
    Deuteronomy 7:20
      וְגַם אֶת־הַצִּרְעָה יְשַׁלַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ בָּם עַד־אֲבֹד הַנִּשְׁאָרִים וְהַנִּסְתָּרִים מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃
    → And also, Jehovah your God will send plagues upon them, until all those who remain behind and are hidden from your sight are destroyed.
    Deuteronomy 7:21
      לֹא תַעֲרֹץ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּֽי־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ בְּקִרְבֶּךָ אֵל גָּדוֹל וְנוֹרָֽא׃
    → Do not be afraid of them, for the LORD your God is in your midst. He is a great and powerful God.
    Deuteronomy 7:22
      וְנָשַׁל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֶת־הַגּוֹיִם הָאֵל מִפָּנֶיךָ מְעַט מְעָט לֹא תוּכַל כַּלֹּתָם מַהֵר פֶּן־תִּרְבֶּה עָלֶיךָ חַיַּת הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃
    → And Jehovah your God will scatter those nations from before you, little by little. They won’t be able to stand against you anymore. Then, the death penalty will fall upon them.
    Deuteronomy 7:23
      וּנְתָנָם יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְפָנֶיךָ וְהָמָם מְהוּמָה גְדֹלָה עַד הִשָּׁמְדָֽם׃
    → And Jehovah your God will give them to you before your eyes. And they will be used for great purposes, even until they are used up completely.
    Deuteronomy 7:24
      וְנָתַן מַלְכֵיהֶם בְּיָדֶךָ וְהַאֲבַדְתָּ אֶת־שְׁמָם מִתַּחַת הַשָּׁמָיִם לֹֽא־יִתְיַצֵּב אִישׁ בְּפָנֶיךָ עַד הִשְׁמִֽדְךָ אֹתָֽם׃
    → And they shall be given into your hands. You will destroy their names from under heaven. No one shall stand before you until you have destroyed them completely.
    Deuteronomy 7:25
      פְּסִילֵי אֱלֹהֵיהֶם תִּשְׂרְפוּן בָּאֵשׁ לֹֽא־תַחְמֹד כֶּסֶף וְזָהָב עֲלֵיהֶם וְלָקַחְתָּ לָךְ פֶּן תִּוָּקֵשׁ בּוֹ כִּי תוֹעֲבַת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הֽוּא׃
    → May their idols be burned in fire, so that they may not be able to taste gold or silver. And take them for yourself, so that you won’t be burdened by them, because this is the punishment from your God, your Lord.
    Deuteronomy 7:26
      וְלֹא־תָבִיא תֽוֹעֵבָה אֶל־בֵּיתֶךָ וְהָיִיתָ חֵרֶם כָּמֹהוּ שַׁקֵּץ ׀ תְּשַׁקְּצֶנּוּ וְתַעֵב ׀ תְּֽתַעֲבֶנּוּ כִּי־חֵרֶם הֽוּא׃
    → And do not bring any burden to your home. Then you will be as guilty as those who are punished. They will punish you and treat you with cruelty, for they are guilty themselves.
  Deuteronomy 7 [en]: 26 vv, 4s
    Deuteronomy 8:1
      כָּל־הַמִּצְוָה אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם תִּשְׁמְרוּן לַעֲשׂוֹת לְמַעַן תִּֽחְיוּן וּרְבִיתֶם וּבָאתֶם וִֽירִשְׁתֶּם אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־נִשְׁבַּע יְהוָה לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃
    → All the commandments that I command you today, you must keep. This is so that you may live, multiply, and inherit the land which Jehovah has promised to your ancestors.
    Deuteronomy 8:2
      וְזָכַרְתָּ אֶת־כָּל־הַדֶּרֶךְ אֲשֶׁר הֹלִֽיכֲךָ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ זֶה אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָה בַּמִּדְבָּר לְמַעַן עַנֹּֽתְךָ לְנַסֹּֽתְךָ לָדַעַת אֶת־אֲשֶׁר בִּֽלְבָבְךָ הֲתִשְׁמֹר מִצְוֺתָיו אִם־לֹֽא׃
    → And you remember all the paths that Jehovah your God led you along during those forty years in the wilderness. This was so that you could test yourself and see whether the commandments of Jehovah were truly obeyed by you.
    Deuteronomy 8:3
      וַֽיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּֽאֲכִֽלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְתָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן הוֹדִֽעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ יִחְיֶה הָֽאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא פִֽי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָֽם׃
    → And He will satisfy your hunger, and He will give you food that you do not know. Your ancestors also did not know this, so that they might know that man does not live solely on bread alone. For man lives on everything that God creates.
    Deuteronomy 8:4
      שִׂמְלָתְךָ לֹא בָֽלְתָה מֵֽעָלֶיךָ וְרַגְלְךָ לֹא בָצֵקָה זֶה אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָֽה׃
    → Your clothes have not fallen off you, and your feet are not torn. These are forty years.
    Deuteronomy 8:5
      וְיָדַעְתָּ עִם־לְבָבֶךָ כִּי כַּאֲשֶׁר יְיַסֵּר אִישׁ אֶת־בְּנוֹ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ מְיַסְּרֶֽךָּ׃
    → And you shall know with your heart that when Jehovah your God takes away a man’s son, it is because He wants to take away you as well.
    Deuteronomy 8:6
      וְשָׁמַרְתָּ אֶת־מִצְוֺת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לָלֶכֶת בִּדְרָכָיו וּלְיִרְאָה אֹתֽוֹ׃
    → And you have kept the commandments of the LORD your God, to walk in His ways and to fear Him.
    Deuteronomy 8:7
      כִּי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ מְבִֽיאֲךָ אֶל־אֶרֶץ טוֹבָה אֶרֶץ נַחֲלֵי מָיִם עֲיָנֹת וּתְהֹמֹת יֹצְאִים בַּבִּקְעָה וּבָהָֽר׃
    → For Jehovah your God will bring you into a good land, a land of valleys and hills, with rivers flowing through it.
    Deuteronomy 8:8
      אֶרֶץ חִטָּה וּשְׂעֹרָה וְגֶפֶן וּתְאֵנָה וְרִמּוֹן אֶֽרֶץ־זֵית שֶׁמֶן וּדְבָֽשׁ׃
    → A land of wheat and barley, vines and fig trees, and olive trees. It’s also a land of figs and dates.
    Deuteronomy 8:9
      אֶרֶץ אֲשֶׁר לֹא בְמִסְכֵּנֻת תֹּֽאכַל־בָּהּ לֶחֶם לֹֽא־תֶחְסַר כֹּל בָּהּ אֶרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אֲבָנֶיהָ בַרְזֶל וּמֵהֲרָרֶיהָ תַּחְצֹב נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃
    → A land where one can eat bread without any worries. There’s never a shortage of anything there. It’s a land whose stones are made of iron, and from its hills, thorns can be cut down.
    Deuteronomy 8:10
      וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵֽרַכְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָֽתַן־לָֽךְ׃
    → And you ate and drank, and you praised the LORD your God on this good land that He has given you.
