    Psalms 18:8
      וַתִּגְעַשׁ וַתִּרְעַשׁ ׀ הָאָרֶץ וּמוֹסְדֵי הָרִים יִרְגָּזוּ וַיִּתְגָּֽעֲשׁוּ כִּי־חָרָה לֽוֹ׃
    → And the earth became restless and noisy. The rulers of the mountains became angry and agitated, because they were in pain.
    Psalms 18:9
      עָלָה עָשָׁן ׀ בְּאַפּוֹ וְאֵשׁ־מִפִּיו תֹּאכֵל גֶּחָלִים בָּעֲרוּ מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃
    → Smoke rose up from his mouth, and fire from his eyes. He would eat the flesh of those who were destroyed by him.
    Psalms 18:10
      וַיֵּט שָׁמַיִם וַיֵּרַד וַעֲרָפֶל תַּחַת רַגְלָֽיו׃
    → And he took the heavens and descended, and the clouds covered his feet.
    Psalms 18:11
      וַיִּרְכַּב עַל־כְּרוּב וַיָּעֹף וַיֵּדֶא עַל־כַּנְפֵי־רֽוּחַ׃
    → And he mounted the ark, and he fell, and he lay on the wings of the wind.
    Psalms 18:12
      יָשֶׁת חֹשֶׁךְ ׀ סִתְרוֹ סְבִֽיבוֹתָיו סֻכָּתוֹ חֶשְׁכַת־מַיִם עָבֵי שְׁחָקִֽים׃
    → It was filled with darkness; its surroundings were dark as if they were covered with water. It was a place of thick darkness.
    Psalms 18:13
      מִנֹּגַהּ נֶגְדּוֹ עָבָיו עָבְרוּ בָּרָד וְגַֽחֲלֵי־אֵֽשׁ׃
    → From there, they passed through the thickets and the flames of fire.
    Psalms 18:14
      וַיַּרְעֵם בַּשָּׁמַיִם ׀ יְֽהוָה וְעֶלְיוֹן יִתֵּן קֹלוֹ בָּרָד וְגַֽחֲלֵי־אֵֽשׁ׃
    → And the heavens shall tremble, and Jehovah will give his voice in the form of wind and fire.
    Psalms 18:15
      וַיִּשְׁלַח חִצָּיו וַיְפִיצֵם וּבְרָקִים רָב וַיְהֻמֵּֽם׃
    → And he sent forth his four wings, and scattered them everywhere. In great numbers, they were spread out across the land.
    Psalms 18:16
      וַיֵּרָאוּ ׀ אֲפִיקֵי מַיִם וַֽיִּגָּלוּ מוֹסְדוֹת תֵּבֵל מִגַּעֲרָתְךָ יְהוָה מִנִּשְׁמַת רוּחַ אַפֶּֽךָ׃
    → And the waters saw your power; the foundations of the sea were shaken by your wrath, O LORD! From the spirit of your wind.
    Psalms 18:17
      יִשְׁלַח מִמָּרוֹם יִקָּחֵנִי יַֽמְשֵׁנִי מִמַּיִם רַבִּֽים׃
    → From the midst of his anger, he will send me away; my days will be taken from me in many waters.
    Psalms 18:18
      יַצִּילֵנִי מֵאֹיְבִי עָז וּמִשֹּׂנְאַי כִּֽי־אָמְצוּ מִמֶּֽנִּי׃
    → Save me from my enemies, those who are cruel and hateful, for they have risen up against me.
    Psalms 18:19
      יְקַדְּמוּנִי בְיוֹם־אֵידִי וַֽיְהִי־יְהוָה לְמִשְׁעָן לִֽי׃
    → May they honor me on this day. May Jehovah be my refuge.
    Psalms 18:20
      וַיּוֹצִיאֵנִי לַמֶּרְחָב יְחַלְּצֵנִי כִּי חָפֵֽץ בִּֽי׃
    → And He brought me out into the wilderness, to be rescued from my suffering. For He loved me.
    Psalms 18:21
      יִגְמְלֵנִי יְהוָה כְּצִדְקִי כְּבֹר יָדַי יָשִׁיב לִֽי׃
    → May the LORD reward me with justice, as He always has done. May He restore me to my rightful place.
    Psalms 18:22
      כִּֽי־שָׁמַרְתִּי דַּרְכֵי יְהוָה וְלֹֽא־רָשַׁעְתִּי מֵאֱלֹהָֽי׃
    → For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and I have not sinned against Him.
    Psalms 18:23
      כִּי כָל־מִשְׁפָּטָיו לְנֶגְדִּי וְחֻקֹּתָיו לֹא־אָסִיר מֶֽנִּי׃
    → For all his judgments are against me, and his laws do not restrain me.
    Psalms 18:24
      וָאֱהִי תָמִים עִמּוֹ וָאֶשְׁתַּמֵּר מֵעֲוֺנִֽי׃
    → And Jehovah was with him, and I will be saved from my troubles.
