    → The fruits of the earth will die, and their seeds will be destroyed by human hands.
    Psalms 21:12
      כִּי־נָטוּ עָלֶיךָ רָעָה חָֽשְׁבוּ מְזִמָּה בַּל־יוּכָֽלוּ׃
    → For we have suffered a great loss from you. Think about it carefully before you act rashly.
    Psalms 21:13
      כִּי תְּשִׁיתֵמוֹ שֶׁכֶם בְּמֵֽיתָרֶיךָ תְּכוֹנֵן עַל־פְּנֵיהֶֽם׃
    → For they will be destroyed when you are among your people. They will be punished in front of their own faces.
    Psalms 21:14
      רוּמָה יְהוָה בְּעֻזֶּךָ נָשִׁירָה וּֽנְזַמְּרָה גְּבוּרָתֶֽךָ׃
    → May the Lord be praised through your power; may your greatness be celebrated and honored.
  Psalms 21 [en]: 14 vv, 2s
    Psalms 22:1
      לַמְנַצֵּחַ עַל־אַיֶּלֶת הַשַּׁחַר מִזְמוֹר לְדָוִֽד׃
    → A song for David, to be sung over the black string.
    Psalms 22:2
