    → From his throne, he watched over all the inhabitants of the earth.
    Psalms 33:15
      הַיֹּצֵר יַחַד לִבָּם הַמֵּבִין אֶל־כָּל־מַעֲשֵׂיהֶֽם׃
    → He united their hearts, so that they could understand all his actions.
    Psalms 33:16
      אֵֽין־הַמֶּלֶךְ נוֹשָׁע בְּרָב־חָיִל גִּבּוֹר לֹֽא־יִנָּצֵל בְּרָב־כֹּֽחַ׃
    → The king who is not righteous cannot be saved through great strength.
    Psalms 33:17
      שֶׁקֶר הַסּוּס לִתְשׁוּעָה וּבְרֹב חֵילוֹ לֹא יְמַלֵּֽט׃
    → The false horse cannot be ridden; with its large army, it cannot move forward.
    Psalms 33:18
      הִנֵּה עֵין יְהוָה אֶל־יְרֵאָיו לַֽמְיַחֲלִים לְחַסְדּֽוֹ׃
    → Now, let the eyes of Jehovah be open to those who fear Him, so that He may show them His kindness.
    Psalms 33:19
      לְהַצִּיל מִמָּוֶת נַפְשָׁם וּלְחַיּוֹתָם בָּרָעָֽב׃
    → To save their souls from death and to keep them alive during famine.
    Psalms 33:20
      נַפְשֵׁנוּ חִכְּתָה לַֽיהוָה עֶזְרֵנוּ וּמָגִנֵּנוּ הֽוּא׃
    → Our souls waited for Jehovah’s help. He saved us from harm.
    Psalms 33:21
      כִּי־בוֹ יִשְׂמַח לִבֵּנוּ כִּי בְשֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ בָטָֽחְנוּ׃
    → For in him our hearts shall rejoice, for in his holy name we have placed our trust.
    Psalms 33:22
      יְהִֽי־חַסְדְּךָ יְהוָה עָלֵינוּ כַּאֲשֶׁר יִחַלְנוּ לָֽךְ׃
    → May your kindness be upon us, O LORD, as we begin to serve you.
  Psalms 33 [en]: 22 vv, 3s
    Psalms 34:1
      לְדָוִד בְּשַׁנּוֹתוֹ אֶת־טַעְמוֹ לִפְנֵי אֲבִימֶלֶךְ וַֽיְגָרֲשֵׁהוּ וַיֵּלַֽךְ׃
    → In his twenties, David changed his ways before Abimelech. Then he drove him away and went his own way.
    Psalms 34:2
      אֲבָרֲכָה אֶת־יְהוָה בְּכָל־עֵת תָּמִיד תְּֽהִלָּתוֹ בְּפִֽי׃
    → Bless God at all times, always with praise in my mouth.
    Psalms 34:3
      בַּיהוָה תִּתְהַלֵּל נַפְשִׁי יִשְׁמְעוּ עֲנָוִים וְיִשְׂמָֽחוּ׃
    → In the LORD, my soul shall be healed; it will hear the cries of those who are in need and rejoice.
    Psalms 34:4
      גַּדְּלוּ לַיהוָה אִתִּי וּנְרוֹמְמָה שְׁמוֹ יַחְדָּֽו׃
    → Let us grow in the Lord, and let His name be praised together.
    Psalms 34:5
      דָּרַשְׁתִּי אֶת־יְהוָה וְעָנָנִי וּמִכָּל־מְגוּרוֹתַי הִצִּילָֽנִי׃
    → I have sought refuge in Jehovah; He saved me from all my troubles and from every danger.
    Psalms 34:6
      הִבִּיטוּ אֵלָיו וְנָהָרוּ וּפְנֵיהֶם אַל־יֶחְפָּֽרוּ׃
    → Look at him, and flee from him; turn away from him.
    Psalms 34:7
      זֶה עָנִי קָרָא וַיהוָה שָׁמֵעַ וּמִכָּל־צָרוֹתָיו הוֹשִׁיעֽוֹ׃
    → He cried out in need, and Jehovah heard him. From all his troubles, he was saved.
    Psalms 34:8
      חֹנֶה מַלְאַךְ־יְהוָה סָבִיב לִֽירֵאָיו וַֽיְחַלְּצֵֽם׃
    → HONE, the servant of Jehovah, surrounded his followers and saved them.
    Psalms 34:9
      טַעֲמוּ וּרְאוּ כִּי־טוֹב יְהוָה אַֽשְׁרֵי הַגֶּבֶר יֶחֱסֶה־בּֽוֹ׃
    → They tasted and saw that it was good from the Lord, for He showed them His kindness.
    Psalms 34:10
      יְראוּ אֶת־יְהוָה קְדֹשָׁיו כִּי־אֵין מַחְסוֹר לִירֵאָֽיו׃
    → Let them see that Jehovah is holy; for there is no one who can protect those who fear Him.
    Psalms 34:11
      כְּפִירִים רָשׁוּ וְרָעֵבוּ וְדֹרְשֵׁי יְהוָה לֹא־יַחְסְרוּ כָל־טֽוֹב׃
    → May they be filled with wisdom and have no hunger; may the servants of the LORD have nothing lacking in all that is good.
    Psalms 34:12
      לְֽכוּ־בָנִים שִׁמְעוּ־לִי יִֽרְאַת יְהוָה אֲלַמֶּדְכֶֽם׃
    → Let the children listen to me; let them fear the LORD.
    Psalms 34:13
      מִֽי־הָאִישׁ הֶחָפֵץ חַיִּים אֹהֵב יָמִים לִרְאוֹת טֽוֹב׃
    → Who is this man who desires life, who loves to see good things?
    Psalms 34:14
      נְצֹר לְשׁוֹנְךָ מֵרָע וּשְׂפָתֶיךָ מִדַּבֵּר מִרְמָֽה׃
    → May your words be different from evil, and may your speech be free from lies.
    Psalms 34:15
      סוּר מֵרָע וַעֲשֵׂה־טוֹב בַּקֵּשׁ שָׁלוֹם וְרָדְפֵֽהוּ׃
    → Avoid evil and do good. Seek peace, and pursue it.
    Psalms 34:16
      עֵינֵי יְהוָה אֶל־צַדִּיקִים וְאָזְנָיו אֶל־שַׁוְעָתָֽם׃
    → The eyes of the LORD are upon the righteous, and His ears are attentive to their prayers.
    Psalms 34:17
      פְּנֵי יְהוָה בְּעֹשֵׂי רָע לְהַכְרִית מֵאֶרֶץ זִכְרָֽם׃
    → The face of the LORD will be against those who do evil, so that they may be destroyed from the earth.
    Psalms 34:18
      צָעֲקוּ וַיהוָה שָׁמֵעַ וּמִכָּל־צָרוֹתָם הִצִּילָֽם׃
    → They cried out, and Jehovah heard them. From all their troubles, He saved them.
    Psalms 34:19
      קָרוֹב יְהוָה לְנִשְׁבְּרֵי־לֵב וְֽאֶת־דַּכְּאֵי־רוּחַ יוֹשִֽׁיעַ׃
    → YHWH is close to those whose hearts are pure, and He saves those whose spirits are true.
    Psalms 34:20
      רַבּוֹת רָעוֹת צַדִּיק וּמִכֻּלָּם יַצִּילֶנּוּ יְהוָֽה׃
    → May the many evils of the wicked be removed from us, and may Jehovah save us from them all.
    Psalms 34:21
      שֹׁמֵר כָּל־עַצְמוֹתָיו אַחַת מֵהֵנָּה לֹא נִשְׁבָּֽרָה׃
    → He keeps all his possessions together; none of them is left behind.
    Psalms 34:22
      תְּמוֹתֵת רָשָׁע רָעָה וְשֹׂנְאֵי צַדִּיק יֶאְשָֽׁמוּ׃
    → The wicked will be punished, and the righteous will be blessed.
    Psalms 34:23
      פּוֹדֶה יְהוָה נֶפֶשׁ עֲבָדָיו וְלֹא יֶאְשְׁמוּ כָּֽל־הַחֹסִים בּֽוֹ׃
    → May the Lord have mercy on His servants, and may they not be punished for all their sins.
  Psalms 34 [en]: 23 vv, 3s
    Psalms 35:1
      לְדָוִד ׀ רִיבָה יְהוָה אֶת־יְרִיבַי לְחַם אֶת־לֹֽחֲמָֽי׃
    → To David, the LORD will fight against his enemies for him. He will avenge his wounds.
    Psalms 35:2
      הַחֲזֵק מָגֵן וְצִנָּה וְקוּמָה בְּעֶזְרָתִֽי׃
    → The strong one will protect and defend, and stand firm with my help.
    Psalms 35:3
      וְהָרֵק חֲנִית וּסְגֹר לִקְרַאת רֹדְפָי אֱמֹר לְנַפְשִׁי יְֽשֻׁעָתֵךְ אָֽנִי׃
    → And let the enemy be shut in, so that he cannot see my pursuers. I say to my soul: “Your salvation is near.”
    Psalms 35:4
      יֵבֹשׁוּ וְיִכָּלְמוּ מְבַקְשֵׁי נַפְשִׁי יִסֹּגוּ אָחוֹר וְיַחְפְּרוּ חֹשְׁבֵי רָעָתִֽי׃
    → They will be deceived and misled by those who seek to harm my soul. They will be defeated, and their evil thoughts will be revealed.
    Psalms 35:5
      יִֽהְיוּ כְּמֹץ לִפְנֵי־רוּחַ וּמַלְאַךְ יְהוָה דּוֹחֶֽה׃
    → They shall be like smoke before the wind, and the Lord will fill them with glory.
    Psalms 35:6
      יְֽהִי־דַרְכָּם חֹשֶׁךְ וַחֲלַקְלַקּוֹת וּמַלְאַךְ יְהוָה רֹדְפָֽם׃
    → May their path be dark and difficult, and may Jehovah pursue them relentlessly.
    Psalms 35:7
