      יְקוּמוּן עֵדֵי חָמָס אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְתִּי יִשְׁאָלֽוּנִי׃
    → They arose to perform a task that I did not know about.
    Psalms 35:12
      יְשַׁלְּמוּנִי רָעָה תַּחַת טוֹבָה שְׁכוֹל לְנַפְשִֽׁי׃
    → May evil be replaced by good, so that all my thoughts may be filled with goodness.
    Psalms 35:13
      וַאֲנִי ׀ בַּחֲלוֹתָם לְבוּשִׁי שָׂק עִנֵּיתִי בַצּוֹם נַפְשִׁי וּתְפִלָּתִי עַל־חֵיקִי תָשֽׁוּב׃
    → And I am in their suffering; I hold my heart tightly closed. My prayers are on my lips, and they will be answered.
    Psalms 35:14
      כְּרֵֽעַ־כְּאָח לִי הִתְהַלָּכְתִּי כַּאֲבֶל־אֵם קֹדֵר שַׁחֽוֹתִי׃
    → As a companion to my brother, I walked along the path of sorrow. But Koder was always there to comfort me.
    Psalms 35:15
      וּבְצַלְעִי שָׂמְחוּ וְֽנֶאֱסָפוּ נֶאֶסְפוּ עָלַי נֵכִים וְלֹא יָדַעְתִּי קָֽרְעוּ וְלֹא־דָֽמּוּ׃
    → And in their hearts they rejoiced. They gathered around me, those who were sick. I didn’t know that they had been broken and destroyed.
    Psalms 35:16
      בְּחַנְפֵי לַעֲגֵי מָעוֹג חָרֹק עָלַי שִׁנֵּֽימוֹ׃
    → In the depths of despair, I am filled with sorrow and pain.
    Psalms 35:17
      אֲדֹנָי כַּמָּה תִּרְאֶה הָשִׁיבָה נַפְשִׁי מִשֹּׁאֵיהֶם מִכְּפִירִים יְחִידָתִֽי׃
    → Adonai, how many times will I see this return of my soul from those who deceive me?
    Psalms 35:18
      אוֹדְךָ בְּקָהָל רָב בְּעַם עָצוּם אֲהַֽלְלֶֽךָּ׃
    → Hail you in a large crowd, among a whole people who praise you.
    Psalms 35:19
      אַֽל־יִשְׂמְחוּ־לִי אֹיְבַי שֶׁקֶר שֹׂנְאַי חִנָּם יִקְרְצוּ־עָֽיִן׃
    → May my enemies rejoice, for they are false and hateful. They will be punished for their actions.
    Psalms 35:20
      כִּי לֹא שָׁלוֹם יְדַבֵּרוּ וְעַל רִגְעֵי־אֶרֶץ דִּבְרֵי מִרְמוֹת יַחֲשֹׁבֽוּן׃
    → For it is not right for them to speak, and in the moments of time on earth, to say things that are false and misleading.
    Psalms 35:21
      וַיַּרְחִיבוּ עָלַי פִּיהֶם אָמְרוּ הֶאָח ׀ הֶאָח רָאֲתָה עֵינֵֽינוּ׃
    → And they spread their mouths wide over me. They said, “Oh, what a sight we have seen!”
    Psalms 35:22
      רָאִיתָה יְהוָה אַֽל־תֶּחֱרַשׁ אֲדֹנָי אֲל־תִּרְחַק מִמֶּֽנִּי׃
    → The LORD has seen that you are still faithful to me, and that you do not stray from me.
    Psalms 35:23
      הָעִירָה וְהָקִיצָה לְמִשְׁפָּטִי אֱלֹהַי וַֽאדֹנָי לְרִיבִֽי׃
    → The city rose up and went to court before the judgments of God and my Lord, in order to settle disputes.
    Psalms 35:24
      שָׁפְטֵנִי כְצִדְקְךָ יְהוָה אֱלֹהָי וְאַל־יִשְׂמְחוּ־לִֽי׃
    → Judge me according to your righteousness, O LORD God. May no one rejoice over me.
    Psalms 35:25
      אַל־יֹאמְרוּ בְלִבָּם הֶאָח נַפְשֵׁנוּ אַל־יֹאמְרוּ בִּֽלַּעֲנֽוּהוּ׃
    → Let them not say in their hearts, “Our souls are safe.” Let them not say, “We are secure.”
    Psalms 35:26
      יֵבֹשׁוּ וְיַחְפְּרוּ ׀ יַחְדָּו שְׂמֵחֵי רָעָתִי יִֽלְבְּשׁוּ־בֹשֶׁת וּכְלִמָּה הַֽמַּגְדִּילִים עָלָֽי׃
    → They will dig and search together, to uncover the secrets of my misfortune. They will plow through everything that increases my suffering.
    Psalms 35:27
      יָרֹנּוּ וְיִשְׂמְחוּ חֲפֵצֵי צִדְקִי וְיֹאמְרוּ תָמִיד יִגְדַּל יְהוָה הֶחָפֵץ שְׁלוֹם עַבְדּֽוֹ׃
    → Let them rejoice and be glad, those who seek righteousness. Let them always say, “May the LORD increase His glory! He desires peace for His servants.”
    Psalms 35:28
      וּלְשׁוֹנִי תֶּהְגֶּה צִדְקֶךָ כָּל־הַיּוֹם תְּהִלָּתֶֽךָ׃
    → And let your righteousness be revealed today, your glory forever.
  Psalms 35 [en]: 28 vv, 4s
    Psalms 36:1
      לַמְנַצֵּחַ ׀ לְעֶֽבֶד־יְהוָה לְדָוִֽד׃
    → To serve the LORD, to David.
    Psalms 36:2
      נְאֻֽם־פֶּשַׁע לָרָשָׁע בְּקֶרֶב לִבִּי אֵֽין־פַּחַד אֱלֹהִים לְנֶגֶד עֵינָֽיו׃
    → The wicked will be punished by God, but in my eyes, there is no fear of God in their hearts.
