    → My heart would ache like bread, day and night. Every day, they said to me, “Who is your God?”
    Psalms 42:5
      אֵלֶּה אֶזְכְּרָה ׀ וְאֶשְׁפְּכָה עָלַי ׀ נַפְשִׁי כִּי אֶֽעֱבֹר ׀ בַּסָּךְ אֶדַּדֵּם עַד־בֵּית אֱלֹהִים בְּקוֹל־רִנָּה וְתוֹדָה הָמוֹן חוֹגֵֽג׃
    → These memories come back to me, and my soul is filled with sorrow. I walk through the streets, carrying blood with me, until I reach God’s house, with a voice of praise and worship.
    Psalms 42:6
