    → Day and night, they suffer under their hardships; they endure sorrow and toil.
    Psalms 55:12
      הַוּוֹת בְּקִרְבָּהּ וְֽלֹא־יָמִישׁ מֵרְחֹבָהּ תֹּךְ וּמִרְמָֽה׃
    → They are close to her, but not far from her. They are both inside and outside of her.
    Psalms 55:13
      כִּי לֹֽא־אוֹיֵב יְחָֽרְפֵנִי וְאֶשָּׂא לֹֽא־מְשַׂנְאִי עָלַי הִגְדִּיל וְאֶסָּתֵר מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃
    → For he will not harm me, nor will he despise me. He will increase my strength and give me courage from within.
    Psalms 55:14
      וְאַתָּה אֱנוֹשׁ כְּעֶרְכִּי אַלּוּפִי וּמְיֻדָּֽעִי׃
    → And you are a man who is wise and knowledgeable.
    Psalms 55:15
      אֲשֶׁר יַחְדָּו נַמְתִּיק סוֹד בְּבֵית אֱלֹהִים נְהַלֵּךְ בְּרָֽגֶשׁ׃
    → When they walk together in the house of God, they walk with joy.
    Psalms 55:16
      יַשִּׁי מָוֶת עָלֵימוֹ יֵרְדוּ שְׁאוֹל חַיִּים כִּֽי־רָעוֹת בִּמְגוּרָם בְּקִרְבָּֽם׃
    → May death fall upon them! May the living creatures descend upon them, as if they were trapped in their own homes.
    Psalms 55:17
      אֲנִי אֶל־אֱלֹהִים אֶקְרָא וַיהוָה יוֹשִׁיעֵֽנִי׃
    → I will cry out to God, and Jehovah will save me.
    Psalms 55:18
      עֶרֶב וָבֹקֶר וְצָהֳרַיִם אָשִׂיחָה וְאֶהֱמֶה וַיִּשְׁמַע קוֹלִֽי׃
    → In the evening, at noon, and in the morning, I will sacrifice. I will make offerings. They will hear my voice.
    Psalms 55:19
      פָּדָה בְשָׁלוֹם נַפְשִׁי מִקֲּרָב־לִי כִּֽי־בְרַבִּים הָיוּ עִמָּדִֽי׃
    → May my soul be freed from distress, for there were many who stood against me.
    Psalms 55:20
