    → Let them return to their tracks, those words that were spoken by the one who said “Oh!”
    Psalms 70:5
      יָשִׂישׂוּ וְיִשְׂמְחוּ ׀ בְּךָ כָּֽל־מְבַקְשֶׁיךָ וְיֹאמְרוּ תָמִיד יִגְדַּל אֱלֹהִים אֹהֲבֵי יְשׁוּעָתֶֽךָ׃
    → May they be blessed and rejoice in you. May they always say, “May God bless you, my friends who bring salvation to me.”
    Psalms 70:6
      וַאֲנִי ׀ עָנִי וְאֶבְיוֹן אֱלֹהִים חֽוּשָׁה־לִּי עֶזְרִי וּמְפַלְטִי אַתָּה יְהוָה אַל־תְּאַחַֽר׃
    → I am poor and needy; may God help me. Please, do not leave me alone. You, LORD, do not abandon me.
  Psalms 70 [en]: 6 vv, 1s
    Psalms 71:1
