    → And I will always be concerned and attentive to all your words.
    Psalms 71:15
      פִּי ׀ יְסַפֵּר צִדְקָתֶךָ כָּל־הַיּוֹם תְּשׁוּעָתֶךָ כִּי לֹא יָדַעְתִּי סְפֹרֽוֹת׃
    → I will recount your righteousness all day long; your salvation will be known forever. For I do not know how many times you have been saved.
    Psalms 71:16
      אָבוֹא בִּגְבֻרוֹת אֲדֹנָי יְהוִה אַזְכִּיר צִדְקָתְךָ לְבַדֶּֽךָ׃
    → I will come in great glory, O God of Israel. Then I will remember your righteousness only for yourself.
    Psalms 71:17
      אֱֽלֹהִים לִמַּדְתַּנִי מִנְּעוּרָי וְעַד־הֵנָּה אַגִּיד נִפְלְאוֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → God has taught me from my youth, and until now I will always speak of your wonders.
    Psalms 71:18
      וְגַם עַד־זִקְנָה ׀ וְשֵׂיבָה אֱלֹהִים אַֽל־תַּעַזְבֵנִי עַד־אַגִּיד זְרוֹעֲךָ לְדוֹר לְכָל־יָבוֹא גְּבוּרָתֶֽךָ׃
    → And even in old age, and when I’m gone, God will not let me be left alone. He will make my descendants live for generations to come, as a sign of Your greatness.
    Psalms 71:19
      וְצִדְקָתְךָ אֱלֹהִים עַד־מָרוֹם אֲשֶׁר־עָשִׂיתָ גְדֹלוֹת אֱלֹהִים מִי כָמֽוֹךָ׃
    → And your righteousness, O God, is beyond all praise. You have done great things, O God! Who else can compare to you?
    Psalms 71:20
      אֲשֶׁר הִרְאִיתַנִי ׀ צָרוֹת רַבּוֹת וְרָעוֹת תָּשׁוּב תְּחַיֵּינִי וּֽמִתְּהֹמוֹת הָאָרֶץ תָּשׁוּב תַּעֲלֵֽנִי׃
    → May they see that I suffer great hardships and evils. May the destruction of my life be reversed, and may the land be restored to its former state.
    Psalms 71:21
      תֶּרֶב ׀ גְּֽדֻלָּתִי וְתִסֹּב תְּֽנַחֲמֵֽנִי׃
    → Let my greatness increase, and let me be comforted.
