    → And he led his people like a flock of sheep, and he guided them through the wilderness.
    Psalms 78:53
      וַיַּנְחֵם לָבֶטַח וְלֹא פָחָדוּ וְאֶת־אוֹיְבֵיהֶם כִּסָּה הַיָּֽם׃
    → And they were at ease and not afraid, and their enemies were covered by the sea.
    Psalms 78:54
      וַיְבִיאֵם אֶל־גְּבוּל קָדְשׁוֹ הַר־זֶה קָנְתָה יְמִינֽוֹ׃
    → And he brought them to the holy land of Mount Zeh. There, his right hand was acquired.
    Psalms 78:55
