    Psalms 78:64
      כֹּהֲנָיו בַּחֶרֶב נָפָלוּ וְאַלְמְנֹתָיו לֹא תִבְכֶּֽינָה׃
    → Their priests fell in the battle, and their prophets were not mourned.
    Psalms 78:65
      וַיִּקַץ כְּיָשֵׁן ׀ אֲדֹנָי כְּגִבּוֹר מִתְרוֹנֵן מִיָּֽיִן׃
    → And he stretched out his hand as if it were a weapon, like a mighty ruler who can do anything he wants.
    Psalms 78:66
      וַיַּךְ־צָרָיו אָחוֹר חֶרְפַּת עוֹלָם נָתַן לָֽמוֹ׃
    → And his enemies were subjected to eternal shame and disgrace.
    Psalms 78:67
      וַיִּמְאַס בְּאֹהֶל יוֹסֵף וּֽבְשֵׁבֶט אֶפְרַיִם לֹא בָחָֽר׃
    → And he lay down in Joseph’s tent, and in Ephraim’s camp, without choosing a place.
    Psalms 78:68
      וַיִּבְחַר אֶת־שֵׁבֶט יְהוּדָה אֶֽת־הַר צִיּוֹן אֲשֶׁר אָהֵֽב׃
    → And he chose the tribe of Judah to be located on Mount Zion, which he loved.
    Psalms 78:69
      וַיִּבֶן כְּמוֹ־רָמִים מִקְדָּשׁוֹ כְּאֶרֶץ יְסָדָהּ לְעוֹלָֽם׃
    → And he created them like mountains from his holy place, as if they were land established for eternity.
    Psalms 78:70
      וַיִּבְחַר בְּדָוִד עַבְדּוֹ וַיִּקָּחֵהוּ מִֽמִּכְלְאֹת צֹֽאן׃
    → And David chose his servant, and took him from the flocks of the sheep.
    Psalms 78:71
      מֵאַחַר עָלוֹת הֱבִיאוֹ לִרְעוֹת בְּיַעֲקֹב עַמּוֹ וּבְיִשְׂרָאֵל נַחֲלָתֽוֹ׃
    → After his rise, he brought it down upon Jacob’s people and upon Israel’s land.
    Psalms 78:72
      וַיִּרְעֵם כְּתֹם לְבָבוֹ וּבִתְבוּנוֹת כַּפָּיו יַנְחֵֽם׃
    → And his heart was filled with sorrow, and his hands trembled.
