  Psalms 92 [en]: 16 vv, 2s
    Psalms 93:1
      יְהוָה מָלָךְ גֵּאוּת לָבֵשׁ לָבֵשׁ יְהוָה עֹז הִתְאַזָּר אַף־תִּכּוֹן תֵּבֵל בַּל־תִּמּֽוֹט׃
    → YHWH, King of Glory, let the sea be filled with blood. YHWH, mighty and powerful, even if Egypt is destroyed, it will not be defeated.
    Psalms 93:2
      נָכוֹן כִּסְאֲךָ מֵאָז מֵֽעוֹלָם אָֽתָּה׃
    → May your throne remain stable from all eternity.
    Psalms 93:3
      נָשְׂאוּ נְהָרוֹת ׀ יְֽהוָה נָשְׂאוּ נְהָרוֹת קוֹלָם יִשְׂאוּ נְהָרוֹת דָּכְיָֽם׃
    → Let the rivers carry away the sins of Jehovah. Let them carry away the sins of His people.
    Psalms 93:4
      מִקֹּלוֹת ׀ מַיִם רַבִּים אַדִּירִים מִשְׁבְּרֵי־יָם אַדִּיר בַּמָּרוֹם יְהוָֽה׃
    → From the depths of great waters, from the depths of the sea, there comes a great power from the depths of the sea. It is the power of Jehovah.
    Psalms 93:5
      עֵֽדֹתֶיךָ ׀ נֶאֶמְנוּ מְאֹד לְבֵיתְךָ נַאֲוָה־קֹדֶשׁ יְהוָה לְאֹרֶךְ יָמִֽים׃
    → May our prayers be accepted by you, O holy house of God. May the Lord bless you for ever.
  Psalms 93 [en]: 5 vv, 1s
    Psalms 94:1
      אֵל־נְקָמוֹת יְהוָה אֵל נְקָמוֹת הוֹפִֽיַע׃
    → It is the vengeance of Jehovah; it is His way of retribution.
    Psalms 94:2
      הִנָּשֵׂא שֹׁפֵט הָאָרֶץ הָשֵׁב גְּמוּל עַל־גֵּאִֽים׃
    → The judge who ruled over the land now sits on a throne over the people.
    Psalms 94:3
      עַד־מָתַי רְשָׁעִים ׀ יְהוָה עַד־מָתַי רְשָׁעִים יַעֲלֹֽזוּ׃
    → Until the day they die, those wicked people will be punished by God. Those wicked people will be brought down to hell.
    Psalms 94:4
      יַבִּיעוּ יְדַבְּרוּ עָתָק יִֽתְאַמְּרוּ כָּל־פֹּעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן׃
    → They shall speak in a grand manner; they shall say everything that happens.
    Psalms 94:5
      עַמְּךָ יְהוָה יְדַכְּאוּ וְֽנַחֲלָתְךָ יְעַנּֽוּ׃
    → Your people will be destroyed, and your land will be laid waste.
    Psalms 94:6
      אַלְמָנָה וְגֵר יַהֲרֹגוּ וִֽיתוֹמִים יְרַצֵּֽחוּ׃
    → Almanya and Ger Yaharogu will be destroyed, and they will be punished.
    Psalms 94:7
      וַיֹּאמְרוּ לֹא יִרְאֶה־יָּהּ וְלֹא־יָבִין אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹֽב׃
    → And they said, “May Jehovah not see him, and may the God of Jacob not understand him.”
    Psalms 94:8
      בִּינוּ בֹּעֲרִים בָּעָם וּכְסִילִים מָתַי תַּשְׂכִּֽילוּ׃
    → In midst of storms and among the foolish people, they will be destroyed.
    Psalms 94:9
      הֲנֹטַֽע אֹזֶן הֲלֹא יִשְׁמָע אִֽם־יֹצֵֽר עַיִן הֲלֹא יַבִּֽיט׃
    → He who is deaf cannot hear, and he who is blind cannot see.
    Psalms 94:10
      הֲיֹסֵר גּוֹיִם הֲלֹא יוֹכִיחַ הַֽמְלַמֵּד אָדָם דָּֽעַת׃
    → The ignorant people cannot truly understand what knowledge is.
    Psalms 94:11
      יְֽהוָה יֹדֵעַ מַחְשְׁבוֹת אָדָם כִּי־הֵמָּה הָֽבֶל׃
    → YHWH knows the thoughts of man, for he is all-knowing.
    Psalms 94:12
      אַשְׁרֵי ׀ הַגֶּבֶר אֲשֶׁר־תְּיַסְּרֶנּוּ יָּהּ וּֽמִתּוֹרָתְךָ תְלַמְּדֶֽנּוּ׃
    → Let us learn from the teachings of your Torah.
    Psalms 94:13
      לְהַשְׁקִיט לוֹ מִימֵי רָע עַד יִכָּרֶה לָרָשָׁע שָֽׁחַת׃
    → To clear him from the waters of evil, until he is recognized as a good person.
    Psalms 94:14
      כִּי ׀ לֹא־יִטֹּשׁ יְהוָה עַמּוֹ וְנַחֲלָתוֹ לֹא יַעֲזֹֽב׃
    → For Jehovah will not bring his people and their land back.
    Psalms 94:15
      כִּֽי־עַד־צֶדֶק יָשׁוּב מִשְׁפָּט וְאַחֲרָיו כָּל־יִשְׁרֵי־לֵֽב׃
    → For justice will be restored through judgment, and after that, all those who are evil will be punished.
    Psalms 94:16
      מִֽי־יָקוּם לִי עִם־מְרֵעִים מִֽי־יִתְיַצֵּב לִי עִם־פֹּעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן׃
    → Who will stand with me against my enemies? Who will be my ally in times of trouble?
    Psalms 94:17
      לוּלֵי יְהוָה עֶזְרָתָה לִּי כִּמְעַט ׀ שָֽׁכְנָה דוּמָה נַפְשִֽׁי׃
    → May the LORD help me, as my soul longs for it.
    Psalms 94:18
      אִם־אָמַרְתִּי מָטָה רַגְלִי חַסְדְּךָ יְהוָה יִסְעָדֵֽנִי׃
    → If I say, “Turn my feet towards your mercy, O LORD!” then you will hear me.
    Psalms 94:19
      בְּרֹב שַׂרְעַפַּי בְּקִרְבִּי תַּנְחוּמֶיךָ יְֽשַׁעַשְׁעוּ נַפְשִֽׁי׃
    → In many times of sorrow and distress, your words of comfort will heal my soul.
    Psalms 94:20
      הַֽיְחָבְרְךָ כִּסֵּא הַוּוֹת יֹצֵר עָמָל עֲלֵי־חֹֽק׃
    → May you be like Shem, who was created through great labor.
    Psalms 94:21
      יָגוֹדּוּ עַל־נֶפֶשׁ צַדִּיק וְדָם נָקִי יַרְשִֽׁיעוּ׃
    → May they praise the soul of the righteous and the pure blood that will inherit them.
    Psalms 94:22
      וַיְהִי יְהוָה לִי לְמִשְׂגָּב וֵאלֹהַי לְצוּר מַחְסִֽי׃
    → And Jehovah became my refuge, and my God became my shield.
    Psalms 94:23
      וַיָּשֶׁב עֲלֵיהֶם ׀ אֶת־אוֹנָם וּבְרָעָתָם יַצְמִיתֵם יַצְמִיתֵם יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃
    → And He shall sit upon them, and in their pain they will cry out to our God.
  Psalms 94 [en]: 23 vv, 3s
    Psalms 95:1
      לְכוּ נְרַנְּנָה לַיהוָה נָרִיעָה לְצוּר יִשְׁעֵֽנוּ׃
    → Let us go, O Lord, and seek Your help for our salvation.
    Psalms 95:2
      נְקַדְּמָה פָנָיו בְּתוֹדָה בִּזְמִרוֹת נָרִיעַֽ לֽוֹ׃
    → His face was turned toward us, in praise of the songs of Nari’loh.
    Psalms 95:3
      כִּי אֵל גָּדוֹל יְהוָה וּמֶלֶךְ גָּדוֹל עַל־כָּל־אֱלֹהִֽים׃
    → For Jehovah is a great God, and He is a great King over all gods.
    Psalms 95:4
      אֲשֶׁר בְּיָדוֹ מֶחְקְרֵי־אָרֶץ וְתוֹעֲפוֹת הָרִים לֽוֹ׃
    → Who has the power to explore the lands and navigate through the mountains?
    Psalms 95:5
      אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ הַיָּם וְהוּא עָשָׂהוּ וְיַבֶּשֶׁת יָדָיו יָצָֽרוּ׃
    → To whom the sea belongs; and he created it, and his hands shaped it into its form.
    Psalms 95:6
      בֹּאוּ נִשְׁתַּחֲוֶה וְנִכְרָעָה נִבְרְכָה לִֽפְנֵי־יְהוָה עֹשֵֽׂנוּ׃
    → Let us bow and fall down, in worship before the LORD our God.
    Psalms 95:7
      כִּי הוּא אֱלֹהֵינוּ וַאֲנַחְנוּ עַם מַרְעִיתוֹ וְצֹאן יָדוֹ הַיּוֹם אִֽם־בְּקֹלוֹ תִשְׁמָֽעוּ׃
    → For he is our God, and we are His people. Today, if you listen to Him, then you will be saved.
    Psalms 95:8
      אַל־תַּקְשׁוּ לְבַבְכֶם כִּמְרִיבָה כְּיוֹם מַסָּה בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃
    → Do not make it difficult for yourselves to forgive each other, as it is the right thing to do in times of conflict.
    Psalms 95:9
      אֲשֶׁר נִסּוּנִי אֲבוֹתֵיכֶם בְּחָנוּנִי גַּם־רָאוּ פָעֳלִֽי׃
    → Those who tried to tempt me, your ancestors did so in their sins. But they also saw my works.
    Psalms 95:10
      אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָה ׀ אָקוּט בְּדוֹר וָאֹמַר עַם תֹּעֵי לֵבָב הֵם וְהֵם לֹא־יָדְעוּ דְרָכָֽי׃
    → Forty years passed, and I said to them, “My people, they do not know the ways of God.”
    Psalms 95:11
      אֲשֶׁר־נִשְׁבַּעְתִּי בְאַפִּי אִם־יְבֹאוּן אֶל־מְנוּחָתִֽי׃
    → I will be happy if they come to my place of rest.
  Psalms 95 [en]: 11 vv, 1s
    Psalms 96:1
      שִׁירוּ לַיהוָה שִׁיר חָדָשׁ שִׁירוּ לַיהוָה כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → Sing to the LORD, a new song! Sing to the LORD, all the earth.
    Psalms 96:2
      שִׁירוּ לַיהוָה בָּרֲכוּ שְׁמוֹ בַּשְּׂרוּ מִיּֽוֹם־לְיוֹם יְשׁוּעָתֽוֹ׃
    → Praise Jehovah, bless His name, from day to day, for His salvation.
    Psalms 96:3
      סַפְּרוּ בַגּוֹיִם כְּבוֹדוֹ בְּכָל־הָֽעַמִּים נִפְלְאוֹתָֽיו׃
    → Let them be praised in all nations, among all peoples. May their glory spread far and wide.
    Psalms 96:4
      כִּי גָדוֹל יְהוָה וּמְהֻלָּל מְאֹד נוֹרָא הוּא עַל־כָּל־אֱלֹהִֽים׃
    → For Jehovah is great and glorious in all places; He is exalted above all gods.
    Psalms 96:5
      כִּי ׀ כָּל־אֱלֹהֵי הָעַמִּים אֱלִילִים וַֽיהוָה שָׁמַיִם עָשָֽׂה׃
    → For all the gods of the nations are idols, and Jehovah has created the heavens.
    Psalms 96:6
      הוֹד־וְהָדָר לְפָנָיו עֹז וְתִפְאֶרֶת בְּמִקְדָּשֽׁוֹ׃
    → He has strength and glory before him in his sanctuary.
    Psalms 96:7
      הָבוּ לַיהוָה מִשְׁפְּחוֹת עַמִּים הָבוּ לַיהוָה כָּבוֹד וָעֹֽז׃
    → Let there be honor and glory for Jehovah among the nations.
    Psalms 96:8
      הָבוּ לַיהוָה כְּבוֹד שְׁמוֹ שְׂאֽוּ־מִנְחָה וּבֹאוּ לְחַצְרוֹתָֽיו׃
    → They went to Jehovah with reverence, in honor of His name. They came to His courts.
    Psalms 96:9
      הִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לַיהוָה בְּהַדְרַת־קֹדֶשׁ חִילוּ מִפָּנָיו כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → Hallow Jehovah in holiness; let all the earth worship Him.
    Psalms 96:10
      אִמְרוּ בַגּוֹיִם ׀ יְהוָה מָלָךְ אַף־תִּכּוֹן תֵּבֵל בַּל־תִּמּוֹט יָדִין עַמִּים בְּמֵישָׁרִֽים׃
    → Say in the nations, “The LORD is the king. Even if Egypt is strong, it will not be able to defeat them.” Nations will be defeated by those who are righteous.
    Psalms 96:11
      יִשְׂמְחוּ הַשָּׁמַיִם וְתָגֵל הָאָרֶץ יִֽרְעַם הַיָּם וּמְלֹאֽוֹ׃
    → May the heavens rejoice, and may the earth tremble. May the sea rage, and fill it with its waves.
    Psalms 96:12
      יַעֲלֹז שָׂדַי וְכָל־אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ אָז יְרַנְּנוּ כָּל־עֲצֵי־יָֽעַר׃
    → All the trees in the forest will be lush and green again.
    Psalms 96:13
      לִפְנֵי יְהוָה ׀ כִּי בָא כִּי בָא לִשְׁפֹּט הָאָרֶץ יִשְׁפֹּֽט־תֵּבֵל בְּצֶדֶק וְעַמִּים בֶּאֱמוּנָתֽוֹ׃
    → Before Jehovah, for He has come to judge the earth. He will judge Constantinople justly, and nations with righteousness.
  Psalms 96 [en]: 13 vv, 2s
    Psalms 97:1
      יְהוָה מָלָךְ תָּגֵל הָאָרֶץ יִשְׂמְחוּ אִיִּים רַבִּֽים׃
    → The LORD, the king, will make the earth shine; many nations will rejoice.
    Psalms 97:2
      עָנָן וַעֲרָפֶל סְבִיבָיו צֶדֶק וּמִשְׁפָּט מְכוֹן כִּסְאֽוֹ׃
    → The clouds and darkness around him represent righteousness and justice. They serve as a foundation for his throne.
    Psalms 97:3
      אֵשׁ לְפָנָיו תֵּלֵךְ וּתְלַהֵט סָבִיב צָרָֽיו׃
    → Fire will go before him, and it will burn around his feet.
    Psalms 97:4
      הֵאִירוּ בְרָקָיו תֵּבֵל רָאֲתָה וַתָּחֵל הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → Their lamps shone in Egypt. She saw it, and the earth began to shine.
    Psalms 97:5
      הָרִים כַּדּוֹנַג נָמַסּוּ מִלִּפְנֵי יְהוָה מִלִּפְנֵי אֲדוֹן כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → The mountains of Kadoan were destroyed before Jehovah’s eyes, before Adonai, throughout all the land.
    Psalms 97:6
      הִגִּידוּ הַשָּׁמַיִם צִדְקוֹ וְרָאוּ כָל־הָעַמִּים כְּבוֹדֽוֹ׃
    → May the heavens speak righteousness, and may all nations see its glory.
    Psalms 97:7
      יֵבֹשׁוּ ׀ כָּל־עֹבְדֵי פֶסֶל הַמִּֽתְהַלְלִים בָּאֱלִילִים הִשְׁתַּחֲווּ־לוֹ כָּל־אֱלֹהִֽים׃
    → May all those who worship the idols be cursed! May all the gods be disgraced.
    Psalms 97:8
      שָׁמְעָה וַתִּשְׂמַח ׀ צִיּוֹן וַתָּגֵלְנָה בְּנוֹת יְהוּדָה לְמַעַן מִשְׁפָּטֶיךָ יְהוָֽה׃
    → She heard and was glad; Zion rejoiced, and the daughters of Judah praised you for your judgments, O LORD.
    Psalms 97:9
      כִּֽי־אַתָּה יְהוָה עֶלְיוֹן עַל־כָּל־הָאָרֶץ מְאֹד נַעֲלֵיתָ עַל־כָּל־אֱלֹהִֽים׃
    → For you, LORD, are exalted above all nations; you have been honored above all gods.
    Psalms 97:10
      אֹהֲבֵי יְהוָה שִׂנְאוּ רָע שֹׁמֵר נַפְשׁוֹת חֲסִידָיו מִיַּד רְשָׁעִים יַצִּילֵֽם׃
    → The lovers of Jehovah hate evil. They protect the lives of their faithful people from the hands of the wicked. They save them.
    Psalms 97:11
      אוֹר זָרֻעַ לַצַּדִּיק וּֽלְיִשְׁרֵי־לֵב שִׂמְחָֽה׃
    → Light for the righteous and for those with a pure heart, who will be joyful.
    Psalms 97:12
      שִׂמְחוּ צַדִּיקִים בַּֽיהוָה וְהוֹדוּ לְזֵכֶר קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃
    → Rejoice, righteous people, in the Lord! Praise Him, so that His holiness may be remembered.
  Psalms 97 [en]: 12 vv, 2s
    Psalms 98:1
      מִזְמוֹר שִׁירוּ לַֽיהוָה ׀ שִׁיר חָדָשׁ כִּֽי־נִפְלָאוֹת עָשָׂה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה־לּוֹ יְמִינוֹ וּזְרוֹעַ קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃
    → A song for Jehovah, a new song. It was created by His mercy; His right hand and His holy one have made it possible.
    Psalms 98:2
      הוֹדִיעַ יְהוָה יְשׁוּעָתוֹ לְעֵינֵי הַגּוֹיִם גִּלָּה צִדְקָתֽוֹ׃
    → The LORD revealed His salvation to the eyes of the nations, thereby showing His righteousness.
    Psalms 98:3
      זָכַר חַסְדּוֹ ׀ וֶֽאֱֽמוּנָתוֹ לְבֵית יִשְׂרָאֵל רָאוּ כָל־אַפְסֵי־אָרֶץ אֵת יְשׁוּעַת אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃
    → They remembered His kindness and mercy toward the house of Israel. All the people of the earth saw the salvation that our God brought.
    Psalms 98:4
      הָרִיעוּ לַֽיהוָה כָּל־הָאָרֶץ פִּצְחוּ וְרַנְּנוּ וְזַמֵּֽרוּ׃
    → All the nations praised the LORD; they sang and rejoiced.
    Psalms 98:5
      זַמְּרוּ לַיהוָה בְּכִנּוֹר בְּכִנּוֹר וְקוֹל זִמְרָֽה׃
    → Sing to Jehovah with instruments and songs.
    Psalms 98:6
      בַּחֲצֹצְרוֹת וְקוֹל שׁוֹפָר הָרִיעוּ לִפְנֵי ׀ הַמֶּלֶךְ יְהוָֽה׃
    → In the courts and with loud voices, they praised before the king, Jehovah.
    Psalms 98:7
      יִרְעַם הַיָּם וּמְלֹאוֹ תֵּבֵל וְיֹשְׁבֵי בָֽהּ׃
    → The sea will rage, and the Mediterranean will be filled with waves. And those who live there will be destroyed.
    Psalms 98:8
      נְהָרוֹת יִמְחֲאוּ־כָף יַחַד הָרִים יְרַנֵּֽנוּ׃
    → The rivers wash away the stones together; they nourish us along the mountains.
    Psalms 98:9
      לִֽפְֽנֵי־יְהוָה כִּי בָא לִשְׁפֹּט הָאָרֶץ יִשְׁפֹּֽט־תֵּבֵל בְּצֶדֶק וְעַמִּים בְּמֵישָׁרִֽים׃
    → Before the LORD, for He will come to judge the earth. He will judge Tiberias with righteousness, and nations with fairness.
  Psalms 98 [en]: 9 vv, 1s
    Psalms 99:1
      יְהוָה מָלָךְ יִרְגְּזוּ עַמִּים יֹשֵׁב כְּרוּבִים תָּנוּט הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → The LORD, the king, will punish those nations who dwell in their own lands. The earth will be filled with destruction.
    Psalms 99:2
      יְהוָה בְּצִיּוֹן גָּדוֹל וְרָם הוּא עַל־כָּל־הָֽעַמִּֽים׃
    → YHWH is great and mighty; He rules over all nations.
    Psalms 99:3
      יוֹדוּ שִׁמְךָ גָּדוֹל וְנוֹרָא קָדוֹשׁ הֽוּא׃
    → May your name be great and holy.
    Psalms 99:4
      וְעֹז מֶלֶךְ מִשְׁפָּט אָהֵב אַתָּה כּוֹנַנְתָּ מֵישָׁרִים מִשְׁפָּט וּצְדָקָה בְּיַעֲקֹב ׀ אַתָּה עָשִֽׂיתָ׃
    → And you, King of Justice, you love righteousness and fairness. You are the one who creates justice and righteousness in Jacob. You have done so.
    Psalms 99:5
      רֽוֹמְמוּ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ וְֽהִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לַהֲדֹם רַגְלָיו קָדוֹשׁ הֽוּא׃
    → May the Lord our God have mercy on us, and may we humble ourselves before His holy feet.
    Psalms 99:6
      מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן ׀ בְּֽכֹהֲנָיו וּשְׁמוּאֵל בְּקֹרְאֵי שְׁמוֹ קֹרִאים אֶל־יְהוָה וְהוּא יַעֲנֵֽם׃
    → Moses and Aaron, along with their priests, and Samuel, when they call out His name, will be answered by Jehovah.
    Psalms 99:7
      בְּעַמּוּד עָנָן יְדַבֵּר אֲלֵיהֶם שָׁמְרוּ עֵדֹתָיו וְחֹק נָֽתַן־לָֽמוֹ׃
    → In the image of clouds, He will speak to them. They shall keep His commandments and laws.
    Psalms 99:8
      יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ אַתָּה עֲנִיתָם אֵל נֹשֵׂא הָיִיתָ לָהֶם וְנֹקֵם עַל־עֲלִילוֹתָֽם׃
    → YHWH, our God, you are the one who will answer them. You will avenge them against their accusers.
    Psalms 99:9
      רֽוֹמְמוּ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲווּ לְהַר קָדְשׁוֹ כִּֽי־קָדוֹשׁ יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃
    → May the Lord our God rejoice, and may they worship His Holy Mountain, for the Lord our God is indeed holy.
  Psalms 99 [en]: 9 vv, 1s
    Psalms 100:1
      מִזְמוֹר לְתוֹדָה הָרִיעוּ לַיהוָה כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → A prayer for the Lord; all the earth rejoices in Him.
    Psalms 100:2
      עִבְדוּ אֶת־יְהוָה בְּשִׂמְחָה בֹּאוּ לְפָנָיו בִּרְנָנָֽה׃
    → Serve the LORD with joy, and come before Him with songs of praise.
    Psalms 100:3
      דְּעוּ כִּֽי־יְהוָה הוּא אֱלֹהִים הֽוּא־עָשָׂנוּ וְלוֹ אֲנַחְנוּ עַמּוֹ וְצֹאן מַרְעִיתֽוֹ׃
    → Know that Jehovah is the God who created us. To Him we belong, and to Him we will return.
    Psalms 100:4
      בֹּאוּ שְׁעָרָיו ׀ בְּתוֹדָה חֲצֵרֹתָיו בִּתְהִלָּה הֽוֹדוּ־לוֹ בָּרֲכוּ שְׁמֽוֹ׃
    → Let them enter his gates, let them enter the streets of his city. Praise his name!
    Psalms 100:5
      כִּי־טוֹב יְהֹוָה לְעוֹלָם חַסְדּוֹ וְעַד־דֹּר וָדֹר אֱמוּנָתֽוֹ׃
    → For it is good for Jehovah to have his kindness forever; his truth will last from generation to generation.
  Psalms 100 [en]: 5 vv, 1s
    Psalms 101:1
      לְדָוִד מִזְמוֹר חֶֽסֶד־וּמִשְׁפָּט אָשִׁירָה לְךָ יְהוָה אֲזַמֵּֽרָה׃
    → To David, a song of grace and justice: The LORD has spoken to you.
    Psalms 101:2
      אַשְׂכִּילָה ׀ בְּדֶרֶךְ תָּמִים מָתַי תָּבוֹא אֵלָי אֶתְהַלֵּךְ בְּתָם־לְבָבִי בְּקֶרֶב בֵּיתִֽי׃
    → Be humble in your ways, so that you may come before me. Walk in my presence, in the midst of my house.
    Psalms 101:3
      לֹֽא־אָשִׁית ׀ לְנֶגֶד עֵינַי דְּֽבַר־בְּלִיָּעַל עֲשֹֽׂה־סֵטִים שָׂנֵאתִי לֹא יִדְבַּק בִּֽי׃
    → I will not do anything that goes against my own eyes. I will not make any decisions that I dislike.
    Psalms 101:4
      לֵבָב עִקֵּשׁ יָסוּר מִמֶּנִּי רָע לֹא אֵדָֽע׃
    → My heart is upset; it’s better for it to be away from me. I don’t know.
    Psalms 101:5
      מְלָשְׁנִי בַסֵּתֶר ׀ רֵעֵהוּ אוֹתוֹ אַצְמִית גְּֽבַהּ־עֵינַיִם וּרְחַב לֵבָב אֹתוֹ לֹא אוּכָֽל׃
    → I tried to open the box, but no one could get inside it. Its eyes were wide open, and its heart was full of kindness. But I couldn’t open it at all.
    Psalms 101:6
      עֵינַי ׀ בְּנֶֽאֶמְנֵי־אֶרֶץ לָשֶׁבֶת עִמָּדִי הֹלֵךְ בְּדֶרֶךְ תָּמִים הוּא יְשָׁרְתֵֽנִי׃
    → My eyes see the truth of the earth; I stand before you. I walk along a path of righteousness. He will guide me.
    Psalms 101:7
      לֹֽא־יֵשֵׁב ׀ בְּקֶרֶב בֵּיתִי עֹשֵׂה רְמִיָּה דֹּבֵר שְׁקָרִים לֹֽא־יִכּוֹן לְנֶגֶד עֵינָֽי׃
    → He shall not sit near my house. He will speak lies, and his words are false. He shall not be allowed to stand before my eyes.
    Psalms 101:8
      לַבְּקָרִים אַצְמִית כָּל־רִשְׁעֵי־אָרֶץ לְהַכְרִית מֵֽעִיר־יְהוָה כָּל־פֹּעֲלֵי אָֽוֶן׃
    → Let all the wicked of the earth be destroyed from the city of Jehovah. Let all those who do evil be removed from there.
  Psalms 101 [en]: 8 vv, 1s
    Psalms 102:1
      תְּפִלָּה לְעָנִי כִֽי־יַעֲטֹף וְלִפְנֵי יְהוָה יִשְׁפֹּךְ שִׂיחֽוֹ׃
    → Prayer for the poor, that they may be covered, and before Jehovah, their sin may be forgiven.
    Psalms 102:2
      יְהוָה שִׁמְעָה תְפִלָּתִי וְשַׁוְעָתִי אֵלֶיךָ תָבֽוֹא׃
    → May the LORD hear my prayers and my pleas. May His mercy be upon me.
    Psalms 102:3
      אַל־תַּסְתֵּר פָּנֶיךָ ׀ מִמֶּנִּי בְּיוֹם צַר לִי הַטֵּֽה־אֵלַי אָזְנֶךָ בְּיוֹם אֶקְרָא מַהֵר עֲנֵֽנִי׃
    → Do not hide your face from me on the day of my distress. Listen to me on that day when I call out to you.
    Psalms 102:4
      כִּֽי־כָלוּ בְעָשָׁן יָמָי וְעַצְמוֹתַי כְּמוֹ־קֵד נִחָֽרוּ׃
    → For all my days have passed in vain, and my own actions are like ashes that have been scattered away.
    Psalms 102:5
      הוּכָּֽה־כָעֵשֶׂב וַיִּבַשׁ לִבִּי כִּֽי־שָׁכַחְתִּי מֵאֲכֹל לַחְמִֽי׃
    → Oh, how I’m sad! My heart is filled with sorrow, as if I’ve forgotten to eat bread.
    Psalms 102:6
      מִקּוֹל אַנְחָתִי דָּבְקָה עַצְמִי לִבְשָׂרִֽי׃
    → From the sound of my sighs, I tried to control my speech.
    Psalms 102:7
      דָּמִיתִי לִקְאַת מִדְבָּר הָיִיתִי כְּכוֹס חֳרָבֽוֹת׃
    → I was like a victim of disaster; I was like a wrecked ship.
    Psalms 102:8
      שָׁקַדְתִּי וָאֶֽהְיֶה כְּצִפּוֹר בּוֹדֵד עַל־גָּֽג׃
    → I have suffered, and now I am like a butterfly, flying away from its cocoon.
    Psalms 102:9
      כָּל־הַיּוֹם חֵרְפוּנִי אוֹיְבָי מְהוֹלָלַי בִּי נִשְׁבָּֽעוּ׃
    → Today, my enemies and those who harm me have humiliated me. They have brought me disgrace.
    Psalms 102:10
      כִּי־אֵפֶר כַּלֶּחֶם אָכָלְתִּי וְשִׁקֻּוַי בִּבְכִי מָסָֽכְתִּי׃
    → For I have eaten every last bit of it; my mouth is filled with its flavor.
    Psalms 102:11
      מִפְּנֵֽי־זַֽעַמְךָ וְקִצְפֶּךָ כִּי נְשָׂאתַנִי וַתַּשְׁלִיכֵֽנִי׃
    → Because of your anger and fury, for you took me and threw me away.
    Psalms 102:12
      יָמַי כְּצֵל נָטוּי וַאֲנִי כָּעֵשֶׂב אִיבָֽשׁ׃
    → My days are like a shadow that shifts constantly; I am like a plant that grows and withers away.
    Psalms 102:13
      וְאַתָּה יְהוָה לְעוֹלָם תֵּשֵׁב וְזִכְרְךָ לְדֹר וָדֹֽר׃
    → And you, LORD, will reign forever. Your memory will be remembered from generation to generation.
    Psalms 102:14
      אַתָּה תָקוּם תְּרַחֵם צִיּוֹן כִּי־עֵת לְחֶֽנְנָהּ כִּי־בָא מוֹעֵֽד׃
    → You shall show compassion to Zion, for it is time for her to be saved. For a savior has come.
    Psalms 102:15
      כִּֽי־רָצוּ עֲבָדֶיךָ אֶת־אֲבָנֶיהָ וְֽאֶת־עֲפָרָהּ יְחֹנֵֽנוּ׃
    → For they desire to serve your stones and your sand.
    Psalms 102:16
      וְיִֽירְאוּ גוֹיִם אֶת־שֵׁם יְהוָה וְֽכָל־מַלְכֵי הָאָרֶץ אֶת־כְּבוֹדֶֽךָ׃
    → And nations will fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth will be under your authority.
    Psalms 102:17
      כִּֽי־בָנָה יְהוָה צִיּוֹן נִרְאָה בִּכְבוֹדֽוֹ׃
    → For Jehovah has created Zion in His glory.
    Psalms 102:18
      פָּנָה אֶל־תְּפִלַּת הָעַרְעָר וְלֹֽא־בָזָה אֶת־תְּפִלָּתָֽם׃
    → They turned away from the prayer of the harasser, and did not pray along with them.
    Psalms 102:19
      תִּכָּתֶב זֹאת לְדוֹר אַחֲרוֹן וְעַם נִבְרָא יְהַלֶּל־יָֽהּ׃
    → Write this down for future generations. May the people who are born after them praise it.
    Psalms 102:20
      כִּֽי־הִשְׁקִיף מִמְּרוֹם קָדְשׁוֹ יְהוָה מִשָּׁמַיִם ׀ אֶל־אֶרֶץ הִבִּֽיט׃
    → For from His holy voice, Jehovah, He looked down from heaven upon the earth.
    Psalms 102:21
      לִשְׁמֹעַ אֶנְקַת אָסִיר לְפַתֵּחַ בְּנֵי תְמוּתָֽה׃
    → To hear the cry of the prisoner, so that the children of Tamu’ah may be freed.
    Psalms 102:22
      לְסַפֵּר בְּצִיּוֹן שֵׁם יְהוָה וּתְהִלָּתוֹ בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃
    → To record in Zion the name of the LORD, and His songs in Jerusalem.
    Psalms 102:23
      בְּהִקָּבֵץ עַמִּים יַחְדָּו וּמַמְלָכוֹת לַעֲבֹד אֶת־יְהוָֽה׃
    → In unity, nations and kings shall serve Jehovah together.
    Psalms 102:24
      עִנָּה בַדֶּרֶךְ כֹּחִי קִצַּר יָמָֽי׃
    → I suffered in my limited strength during these short days.
    Psalms 102:25
      אֹמַר אֵלִי אַֽל־תַּעֲלֵנִי בַּחֲצִי יָמָי בְּדוֹר דּוֹרִים שְׁנוֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → He said to me, “Help me during the half month of your days, in those years that you will live.”
    Psalms 102:26
      לְפָנִים הָאָרֶץ יָסַדְתָּ וּֽמַעֲשֵׂה יָדֶיךָ שָׁמָֽיִם׃
    → In the beginning, you created the heavens and the earth. Your hands were the instruments through which you created everything in heaven and on earth.
    Psalms 102:27
      הֵמָּה ׀ יֹאבֵדוּ וְאַתָּה תַעֲמֹד וְכֻלָּם כַּבֶּגֶד יִבְלוּ כַּלְּבוּשׁ תַּחֲלִיפֵם וְֽיַחֲלֹֽפוּ׃
    → Many will be destroyed, and you will stand alone. They will all be like rags; they will be replaced by something else.
    Psalms 102:28
      וְאַתָּה־הוּא וּשְׁנוֹתֶיךָ לֹא יִתָּֽמּוּ׃
    → And you are that one; and your children will never be destroyed.
    Psalms 102:29
      בְּנֵֽי־עֲבָדֶיךָ יִשְׁכּוֹנוּ וְזַרְעָם לְפָנֶיךָ יִכּֽוֹן׃
    → Your servants will lie down, and their offspring will also lie down before you.
  Psalms 102 [en]: 29 vv, 4s
    Psalms 103:1
      לְדָוִד ׀ בָּרֲכִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהוָה וְכָל־קְרָבַי אֶת־שֵׁם קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃
    → To David, I bless my soul with the name of Jehovah. And to all my followers, I give them His holy name.
    Psalms 103:2
      בָּרֲכִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהוָה וְאַל־תִּשְׁכְּחִי כָּל־גְּמוּלָֽיו׃
    → I bless my soul to the Lord, and I will not forget all His commandments.
    Psalms 103:3
      הַסֹּלֵחַ לְכָל־עֲוֺנֵכִי הָרֹפֵא לְכָל־תַּחֲלֻאָֽיְכִי׃
    → The healer for all my enemies, the one who cures all my illnesses.
    Psalms 103:4
      הַגּוֹאֵל מִשַּׁחַת חַיָּיְכִי הַֽמְעַטְּרֵכִי חֶסֶד וְרַחֲמִֽים׃
    → The redeemer from the bondage of my own life, who surrounds me with kindness and compassion.
    Psalms 103:5
      הַמַּשְׂבִּיַע בַּטּוֹב עֶדְיֵךְ תִּתְחַדֵּשׁ כַּנֶּשֶׁר נְעוּרָֽיְכִי׃
    → The good things will be restored to you, as your days of youth are renewed.
    Psalms 103:6
      עֹשֵׂה צְדָקוֹת יְהוָה וּמִשְׁפָּטִים לְכָל־עֲשׁוּקִֽים׃
    → He performs righteousness and judgments for all people.
    Psalms 103:7
      יוֹדִיעַ דְּרָכָיו לְמֹשֶׁה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֲלִילֽוֹתָיו׃
    → He shows Moses the ways of Israel’s children along with their laws.
    Psalms 103:8
      רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן יְהוָה אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חָֽסֶד׃
    → May Jehovah’s kindness and compassion extend over us forever, and may His mercy be abundant.
    Psalms 103:9
      לֹֽא־לָנֶצַח יָרִיב וְלֹא לְעוֹלָם יִטּֽוֹר׃
    → He shall not contend forever, nor shall he endure evermore.
    Psalms 103:10
      לֹא כַחֲטָאֵינוּ עָשָׂה לָנוּ וְלֹא כַעֲוֺנֹתֵינוּ גָּמַל עָלֵֽינוּ׃
    → It wasn’t because of our sins that He did these things to us, nor was it because of our faults that He dealt with us in such a manner.
    Psalms 103:11
      כִּי כִגְבֹהַּ שָׁמַיִם עַל־הָאָרֶץ גָּבַר חַסְדּוֹ עַל־יְרֵאָֽיו׃
    → For as the heavens cover the earth, so also His kindness covers those who fear Him.
    Psalms 103:12
      כִּרְחֹק מִזְרָח מִֽמַּֽעֲרָב הִֽרְחִיק מִמֶּנּוּ אֶת־פְּשָׁעֵֽינוּ׃
    → As he moves away from the east, from the place of evil, so does he take away our sins from us.
    Psalms 103:13
      כְּרַחֵם אָב עַל־בָּנִים רִחַם יְהוָה עַל־יְרֵאָֽיו׃
    → May the Lord have mercy on his children, as he has mercy on those who fear him.
    Psalms 103:14
      כִּי־הוּא יָדַע יִצְרֵנוּ זָכוּר כִּי־עָפָר אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃
    → For he knew our creations; he remembered that we were indeed created by him.
    Psalms 103:15
      אֱנוֹשׁ כֶּחָצִיר יָמָיו כְּצִיץ הַשָּׂדֶה כֵּן יָצִֽיץ׃
    → A man is like a bird that spends his days like a falcon in the field; thus, he also flies.
    Psalms 103:16
      כִּי רוּחַ עָֽבְרָה־בּוֹ וְאֵינֶנּוּ וְלֹא־יַכִּירֶנּוּ עוֹד מְקוֹמֽוֹ׃
    → For the spirit has passed through it, and it is not yet known where it will go. It still does not know its own place.
    Psalms 103:17
      וְחֶסֶד יְהוָה ׀ מֵעוֹלָם וְעַד־עוֹלָם עַל־יְרֵאָיו וְצִדְקָתוֹ לִבְנֵי בָנִֽים׃
    → And the mercy of the LORD shall be upon him forevermore, for his faithfulness and righteousness will be passed down to his descendants.
    Psalms 103:18
      לְשֹׁמְרֵי בְרִיתוֹ וּלְזֹכְרֵי פִקֻּדָיו לַעֲשׂוֹתָֽם׃
    → To keep his covenant and to remember his commands, so that they may be carried out.
    Psalms 103:19
      יְֽהוָה בַּשָּׁמַיִם הֵכִין כִּסְאוֹ וּמַלְכוּתוֹ בַּכֹּל מָשָֽׁלָה׃
    → YHWH in the heavens has prepared His throne and His kingdom over all things.
    Psalms 103:20
      בָּרֲכוּ יְהוָה מַלְאָכָיו גִּבֹּרֵי כֹחַ עֹשֵׂי דְבָרוֹ לִשְׁמֹעַ בְּקוֹל דְּבָרֽוֹ׃
    → May the LORD bless His servants, those who carry out His commands, and those who listen to His voice.
    Psalms 103:21
      בָּרֲכוּ יְהוָה כָּל־צְבָאָיו מְשָׁרְתָיו עֹשֵׂי רְצוֹנֽוֹ׃
    → May the Lord bless all His servants and those who serve Him.
    Psalms 103:22
      בָּרֲכוּ יְהוָה ׀ כָּֽל־מַעֲשָׂיו בְּכָל־מְקֹמוֹת מֶמְשַׁלְתּוֹ בָּרֲכִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהוָֽה׃
    → May Jehovah bless all His works, in every place where He rules. I bless Jehovah with my heart.
  Psalms 103 [en]: 22 vv, 3s
    Psalms 104:1
      בָּרֲכִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהוָה יְהוָה אֱלֹהַי גָּדַלְתָּ מְּאֹד הוֹד וְהָדָר לָבָֽשְׁתָּ׃
    → Praise my soul to the LORD, Jehovah, my God! You have been exalted above all other gods. Praise and honor be to you!
    Psalms 104:2
      עֹֽטֶה־אוֹר כַּשַּׂלְמָה נוֹטֶה שָׁמַיִם כַּיְרִיעָֽה׃
    → The light of the sun is like a rainbow that spreads across the sky.
    Psalms 104:3
      הַמְקָרֶֽה בַמַּיִם עֲֽלִיּוֹתָיו הַשָּׂם־עָבִים רְכוּבוֹ הַֽמְהַלֵּךְ עַל־כַּנְפֵי־רֽוּחַ׃
    → The creature that lives in the water, with its thick skin, walks on wings made of air.
    Psalms 104:4
      עֹשֶׂה מַלְאָכָיו רוּחוֹת מְשָׁרְתָיו אֵשׁ לֹהֵֽט׃
    → He makes his servants into spirits who serve him; fire that burns.
    Psalms 104:5
      יָֽסַד־אֶרֶץ עַל־מְכוֹנֶיהָ בַּל־תִּמּוֹט עוֹלָם וָעֶֽד׃
    → He established the earth on its proper foundations, forever and ever.
    Psalms 104:6
      תְּהוֹם כַּלְּבוּשׁ כִּסִּיתוֹ עַל־הָרִים יַֽעַמְדוּ־מָֽיִם׃
    → The sun will be like a lamp, shining upon the mountains. The seas will stand still.
    Psalms 104:7
      מִן־גַּעֲרָתְךָ יְנוּסוּן מִן־קוֹל רַֽעַמְךָ יֵחָפֵזֽוּן׃
    → From your anger, they will be freed; from the sound of your voice, they will be rescued.
    Psalms 104:8
      יַעֲלוּ הָרִים יֵרְדוּ בְקָעוֹת אֶל־מְקוֹם זֶה ׀ יָסַדְתָּ לָהֶֽם׃
    → They will climb the mountains, descend into the valleys, and settle in this place. You have established them there.
    Psalms 104:9
      גְּֽבוּל־שַׂמְתָּ בַּל־יַֽעֲבֹרוּן בַּל־יְשׁוּבוּן לְכַסּוֹת הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → The boundaries of Samtah are beyond those of Yayavorun and Yishuvun; they serve to enclose the land.
    Psalms 104:10
      הַֽמְשַׁלֵּחַ מַעְיָנִים בַּנְּחָלִים בֵּין הָרִים יְהַלֵּכֽוּן׃
    → The ruler leads the people along the streams between the mountains.
    Psalms 104:11
      יַשְׁקוּ כָּל־חַיְתוֹ שָׂדָי יִשְׁבְּרוּ פְרָאִים צְמָאָֽם׃
    → May all his days be filled with suffering; may his crops be destroyed and his plants wither away.
    Psalms 104:12
      עֲלֵיהֶם עוֹף־הַשָּׁמַיִם יִשְׁכּוֹן מִבֵּין עֳפָאיִם יִתְּנוּ־קֽוֹל׃
    → Above them, in the heavens, they will be placed among the clouds. They will give forth their voices.
    Psalms 104:13
      מַשְׁקֶה הָרִים מֵעֲלִיּוֹתָיו מִפְּרִי מַעֲשֶׂיךָ תִּשְׂבַּע הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → May the mountains be filled with your fruits from your works; may the earth rejoice.
    Psalms 104:14
      מַצְמִיחַ חָצִיר ׀ לַבְּהֵמָה וְעֵשֶׂב לַעֲבֹדַת הָאָדָם לְהוֹצִיא לֶחֶם מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → They plant fields of grass for the use of cattle, and plants for human purposes, so that they can obtain bread from the earth.
    Psalms 104:15
      וְיַיִן ׀ יְשַׂמַּח לְֽבַב־אֱנוֹשׁ לְהַצְהִיל פָּנִים מִשָּׁמֶן וְלֶחֶם לְֽבַב־אֱנוֹשׁ יִסְעָֽד׃
    → And the human heart shall rejoice, to see its faces shine from the smoke; and bread shall fill the human heart.
    Psalms 104:16
      יִשְׂבְּעוּ עֲצֵי יְהוָה אַֽרְזֵי לְבָנוֹן אֲשֶׁר נָטָֽע׃
    → May the trees of Jehovah be blessed, those that are planted in Lebanon.
    Psalms 104:17
      אֲשֶׁר־שָׁם צִפֳּרִים יְקַנֵּנוּ חֲסִידָה בְּרוֹשִׁים בֵּיתָֽהּ׃
    → There, birds will provide us with protection and safety in their homes.
    Psalms 104:18
      הָרִים הַגְּבֹהִים לַיְּעֵלִים סְלָעִים מַחְסֶה לַֽשְׁפַנִּֽים׃
    → The high mountains provide rocks that can be used as shelter for the sheep.
    Psalms 104:19
      עָשָׂה יָרֵחַ לְמוֹעֲדִים שֶׁמֶשׁ יָדַע מְבוֹאֽוֹ׃
    → He created a bird that knew when to fly.
    Psalms 104:20
      תָּֽשֶׁת־חֹשֶׁךְ וִיהִי לָיְלָה בּֽוֹ־תִרְמֹשׂ כָּל־חַיְתוֹ־יָֽעַר׃
    → It became dark, and in that darkness, all living things in the forest died.
    Psalms 104:21
      הַכְּפִירִים שֹׁאֲגִים לַטָּרֶף וּלְבַקֵּשׁ מֵאֵל אָכְלָֽם׃
    → The wicked cry out for help and seek refuge in God’s hands.
    Psalms 104:22
      תִּזְרַח הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ יֵאָסֵפוּן וְאֶל־מְעוֹנֹתָם יִרְבָּצֽוּן׃
    → When the sun rises, they will be gathered together; and to their destinies they will be brought.
    Psalms 104:23
      יֵצֵא אָדָם לְפָעֳלוֹ וְֽלַעֲבֹדָתוֹ עֲדֵי־עָֽרֶב׃
    → Man goes out to work and to serve until evening.
    Psalms 104:24
      מָֽה־רַבּוּ מַעֲשֶׂיךָ ׀ יְֽהוָה כֻּלָּם בְּחָכְמָה עָשִׂיתָ מָלְאָה הָאָרֶץ קִנְיָנֶֽךָ׃
    → How many wonderful things you have done, O LORD! You have created everything with great wisdom. The earth is full of your creations.
    Psalms 104:25
      זֶה ׀ הַיָּם גָּדוֹל וּרְחַב יָדָיִם שָֽׁם־רֶמֶשׂ וְאֵין מִסְפָּר חַיּוֹת קְטַנּוֹת עִם־גְּדֹלֽוֹת׃
    → That’s a vast and wide ocean. There are countless tiny creatures living there, along with those that are larger in size.
    Psalms 104:26
      שָׁם אֳנִיּוֹת יְהַלֵּכוּן לִוְיָתָן זֶֽה־יָצַרְתָּ לְשַֽׂחֶק־בּֽוֹ׃
    → There, they will walk towards that place where you created them to play.
    Psalms 104:27
      כֻּלָּם אֵלֶיךָ יְשַׂבֵּרוּן לָתֵת אָכְלָם בְּעִתּֽוֹ׃
    → They all will be fulfilled, so that they can eat at that time.
    Psalms 104:28
      תִּתֵּן לָהֶם יִלְקֹטוּן תִּפְתַּח יָֽדְךָ יִשְׂבְּעוּן טֽוֹב׃
    → Give them them; let them open their hands. May they be blessed.
    Psalms 104:29
      תַּסְתִּיר פָּנֶיךָ יִֽבָּהֵלוּן תֹּסֵף רוּחָם יִגְוָעוּן וְֽאֶל־עֲפָרָם יְשׁוּבֽוּן׃
    → Your faces will be hidden from sight; their hearts will be filled with fear. They will return to their dust.
    Psalms 104:30
      תְּשַׁלַּח רוּחֲךָ יִבָּרֵאוּן וּתְחַדֵּשׁ פְּנֵי אֲדָמָֽה׃
    → “Send your breath, and it will bring forth crops; and you will renew the face of the land.”
    Psalms 104:31
      יְהִי כְבוֹד יְהוָה לְעוֹלָם יִשְׂמַח יְהוָה בְּמַעֲשָֽׂיו׃
    → May the glory of the LORD be forever; may the LORD rejoice in His works.
    Psalms 104:32
      הַמַּבִּיט לָאָרֶץ וַתִּרְעָד יִגַּע בֶּהָרִים וְֽיֶעֱשָֽׁנוּ׃
    → He looked down at the earth, and it trembled. He stepped onto the mountains, and they became our home.
    Psalms 104:33
      אָשִׁירָה לַיהוָה בְּחַיָּי אֲזַמְּרָה לֵאלֹהַי בְּעוֹדִֽי׃
    → I will sing to the LORD with all my heart, and I will praise the LORD before my enemies.
    Psalms 104:34
      יֶעֱרַב עָלָיו שִׂיחִי אָנֹכִי אֶשְׂמַח בַּיהוָֽה׃
    → My vines will cover it; I will rejoice in Him.
    Psalms 104:35
      יִתַּמּוּ חַטָּאִים ׀ מִן־הָאָרֶץ וּרְשָׁעִים ׀ עוֹד אֵינָם בָּרֲכִי נַפְשִׁי אֶת־יְהוָה הַֽלְלוּ־יָֽהּ׃
    → The sins of the people will be removed from the earth. But the wicked still won’t be blessed by Jehovah.
  Psalms 104 [en]: 35 vv, 4s
    Psalms 105:1
      הוֹדוּ לַיהוָה קִרְאוּ בִּשְׁמוֹ הוֹדִיעוּ בָעַמִּים עֲלִילוֹתָֽיו׃
    → Praise the LORD! Call upon His name. Let people everywhere know of His greatness.
    Psalms 105:2
      שִֽׁירוּ־לוֹ זַמְּרוּ־לוֹ שִׂיחוּ בְּכָל־נִפְלְאוֹתָֽיו׃
    → Sing to him, chant praises to him; praise him in all his wonders.
    Psalms 105:3
      הִֽתְהַלְלוּ בְּשֵׁם קָדְשׁוֹ יִשְׂמַח לֵב ׀ מְבַקְשֵׁי יְהוָֽה׃
    → They praised in His holy name; He will rejoice those who seek Him.
    Psalms 105:4
      דִּרְשׁוּ יְהוָה וְעֻזּוֹ בַּקְּשׁוּ פָנָיו תָּמִֽיד׃
    → He will demand it from them, and their faces will always be turned towards Him.
    Psalms 105:5
      זִכְרוּ נִפְלְאוֹתָיו אֲשֶׁר־עָשָׂה מֹפְתָיו וּמִשְׁפְּטֵי־פִֽיו׃
    → Remember his miracles that he performed, and the judgments of his mouth.
