      עַֽל־עֲרָבִים בְּתוֹכָהּ תָּלִינוּ כִּנֹּרוֹתֵֽינוּ׃
    → On the rocks within it, we hung our water containers.
    Psalms 137:3
      כִּי שָׁם שְֽׁאֵלוּנוּ שׁוֹבֵינוּ דִּבְרֵי־שִׁיר וְתוֹלָלֵינוּ שִׂמְחָה שִׁירוּ לָנוּ מִשִּׁיר צִיּֽוֹן׃
    → For there, our songs are once again words of joy; our praises are songs that bring us happiness from the singing of Zion.
    Psalms 137:4
      אֵיךְ נָשִׁיר אֶת־שִׁיר־יְהוָה עַל אַדְמַת נֵכָֽר׃
    → How shall we sing the LORD’s song on the land of Nebuchadnezzar?
    Psalms 137:5
      אִֽם־אֶשְׁכָּחֵךְ יְֽרוּשָׁלִָם תִּשְׁכַּח יְמִינִֽי׃
    → If I forget about Jerusalem, then my right hand will also forget.
    Psalms 137:6
      תִּדְבַּק־לְשׁוֹנִי ׀ לְחִכִּי אִם־לֹא אֶזְכְּרֵכִי אִם־לֹא אַעֲלֶה אֶת־יְרוּשָׁלִַם עַל רֹאשׁ שִׂמְחָתִֽי׃
    → I will wait for the right time. If you don’t remember me, or if I don’t take Jerusalem back from those who are against it, then I won’t do anything.
    Psalms 137:7
      זְכֹר יְהוָה ׀ לִבְנֵי אֱדוֹם אֵת יוֹם יְֽרוּשָׁלִָם הָאֹמְרִים עָרוּ ׀ עָרוּ עַד הַיְסוֹד בָּֽהּ׃
    → Remember the day when Jehovah remembered the children of Adam. It was the day of Jerusalem, when people cried out in joy until the end.
    Psalms 137:8
      בַּת־בָּבֶל הַשְּׁדוּדָה אַשְׁרֵי שֶׁיְשַׁלֶּם־לָךְ אֶת־גְּמוּלֵךְ שֶׁגָּמַלְתְּ לָֽנוּ׃
    → The daughter of Babylon, the murderer, you shall be punished for the shameful things you have done. You have made us shameful.
    Psalms 137:9
      אַשְׁרֵי ׀ שֶׁיֹּאחֵז וְנִפֵּץ אֶֽת־עֹלָלַיִךְ אֶל־הַסָּֽלַע׃
    → May he hold it and break your idols into pieces.
  Psalms 137 [en]: 9 vv, 1s
    Psalms 138:1
      לְדָוִד ׀ אוֹדְךָ בְכָל־לִבִּי נֶגֶד אֱלֹהִים אֲזַמְּרֶֽךָּ׃
    → To David, I sing your praises with all my heart, in the face of God.
    Psalms 138:2
      אֶשְׁתַּחֲוֶה אֶל־הֵיכַל קָדְשְׁךָ וְאוֹדֶה אֶת־שְׁמֶךָ עַל־חַסְדְּךָ וְעַל־אֲמִתֶּךָ כִּֽי־הִגְדַּלְתָּ עַל־כָּל־שִׁמְךָ אִמְרָתֶֽךָ׃
    → I will bow down before your holy temple, and I will praise your name for your kindness and truth. For you have exalted your name above all others.
    Psalms 138:3
      בְּיוֹם קָרָֽאתִי וַֽתַּעֲנֵנִי תַּרְהִבֵנִי בְנַפְשִׁי עֹֽז׃
    → On that day, I cried out to God, and He answered me with a terrible response. My heart was filled with sorrow.
    Psalms 138:4
      יוֹדוּךָ יְהוָה כָּל־מַלְכֵי־אָרֶץ כִּי שָׁמְעוּ אִמְרֵי־פִֽיךָ׃
    → May the LORD be praised, O all the kings of the earth! For they have heard Your words.
    Psalms 138:5
      וְיָשִׁירוּ בְּדַרְכֵי יְהוָה כִּי גָדוֹל כְּבוֹד יְהוָֽה׃
    → And they will serve in the ways of Jehovah, for Jehovah’s glory is great.
    Psalms 138:6
      כִּי־רָם יְהוָה וְשָׁפָל יִרְאֶה וְגָבֹהַּ מִמֶּרְחָק יְיֵדָֽע׃
    → For Jehovah is exalted and humble at the same time; He is far away, yet His power is known.
    Psalms 138:7
      אִם־אֵלֵךְ ׀ בְּקֶרֶב צָרָה תְּחַיֵּנִי עַל אַף אֹיְבַי תִּשְׁלַח יָדֶךָ וְתוֹשִׁיעֵנִי יְמִינֶֽךָ׃
    → If I am in distress, may your right hand save me from my enemies. May your hand rescue me from all my troubles.
    Psalms 138:8
      יְהוָה יִגְמֹר בַּעֲדִי יְהוָה חַסְדְּךָ לְעוֹלָם מַעֲשֵׂי יָדֶיךָ אַל־תֶּֽרֶף׃
    → May the LORD finish what He has begun. May Your kindness last forever, O Lord. May Your works be done forever.
  Psalms 138 [en]: 8 vv, 1s
    Psalms 139:1
      לַמְנַצֵּחַ לְדָוִד מִזְמוֹר יְהוָה חֲקַרְתַּנִי וַתֵּדָֽע׃
    → May David be delivered! May the words of Jehovah be fulfilled. You have known me well.
    Psalms 139:2
      אַתָּה יָדַעְתָּ שִׁבְתִּי וְקוּמִי בַּנְתָּה לְרֵעִי מֵרָחֽוֹק׃
    → You know that I rest in sleep, but I rise to fight against my enemies from afar.
    Psalms 139:3
      אָרְחִי וְרִבְעִי זֵרִיתָ וְֽכָל־דְּרָכַי הִסְכַּֽנְתָּה׃
    → My hosts and my friends were all gone, and all my paths were blocked.
    Psalms 139:4
      כִּי אֵין מִלָּה בִּלְשׁוֹנִי הֵן יְהוָה יָדַעְתָּ כֻלָּֽהּ׃
    → For there is no difference between them; Jehovah knows all of them.
    Psalms 139:5
      אָחוֹר וָקֶדֶם צַרְתָּנִי וַתָּשֶׁת עָלַי כַּפֶּֽכָה׃
    → First and foremost, you afflicted me, and your burden weighed heavily on me.
    Psalms 139:6
      פְּלִיאָֽה דַעַת מִמֶּנִּי נִשְׂגְּבָה לֹא־אוּכַֽל לָֽהּ׃
    → My wisdom was shattered by this; it could no longer function.
    Psalms 139:7
      אָנָה אֵלֵךְ מֵרוּחֶךָ וְאָנָה מִפָּנֶיךָ אֶבְרָֽח׃
    → I will go away from your presence, and I will flee from your face.
    Psalms 139:8
      אִם־אֶסַּק שָׁמַיִם שָׁם אָתָּה וְאַצִּיעָה שְּׁאוֹל הִנֶּֽךָּ׃
    → If I ascend to heaven there, then you shall be with me, and I will offer sacrifices to you.
    Psalms 139:9
