    → And he said, “Let darkness cover me, but let light shine upon me at night.”
    Psalms 139:12
      גַּם־חֹשֶׁךְ לֹֽא־יַחְשִׁיךְ מִמֶּךָ וְלַיְלָה כַּיּוֹם יָאִיר כַּחֲשֵׁיכָה כָּאוֹרָֽה׃
    → Even darkness will not be able to hide you from me. And the night will shine like day, because of your light.
    Psalms 139:13
      כִּֽי־אַתָּה קָנִיתָ כִלְיֹתָי תְּסֻכֵּנִי בְּבֶטֶן אִמִּֽי׃
    → For you have purchased my goods; please help me carry them on your back.
    Psalms 139:14
      אֽוֹדְךָ עַל כִּי נוֹרָאוֹת נִפְלֵיתִי נִפְלָאִים מַעֲשֶׂיךָ וְנַפְשִׁי יֹדַעַת מְאֹֽד׃
    → O God, for the sake of your wonders, I fall down in worship. Your deeds are wonderful, and my soul knows this well.
    Psalms 139:15
