    → I will not be ashamed of you, for I have done what I did in the tomb. I was buried in the depths of the earth.
    Psalms 139:16
      גָּלְמִי ׀ רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וְעַֽל־סִפְרְךָ כֻּלָּם יִכָּתֵבוּ יָמִים יֻצָּרוּ וְלוֹ אֶחָד בָּהֶֽם׃
    → Galmi: Your eyes have seen it all. Everything written in your books has been recorded by days of creation. And among those days, there’s only one that matters.
    Psalms 139:17
      וְלִי מַה־יָּקְרוּ רֵעֶיךָ אֵל מֶה עָצְמוּ רָאשֵׁיהֶֽם׃
    → And what do your enemies value? What do their own leaders really value?
    Psalms 139:18
      אֶסְפְּרֵם מֵחוֹל יִרְבּוּן הֱקִיצֹתִי וְעוֹדִי עִמָּֽךְ׃
    → I have recorded them from the days of Yirban. I will still be with you.
    Psalms 139:19
      אִם־תִּקְטֹל אֱלוֹהַּ ׀ רָשָׁע וְאַנְשֵׁי דָמִים סוּרוּ מֶֽנִּי׃
    → If you kill the wicked and those who are evil, then let them be punished by me.
    Psalms 139:20
      אֲשֶׁר יֹאמְרֻךָ לִמְזִמָּה נָשֻׂא לַשָּׁוְא עָרֶֽיךָ׃
    → When you say it at the right time, it will bring you peace.
    Psalms 139:21
      הֲלֽוֹא־מְשַׂנְאֶיךָ יְהוָה ׀ אֶשְׂנָא וּבִתְקוֹמְמֶיךָ אֶתְקוֹטָֽט׃
    → May the LORD not reject you; may He not abandon you or destroy you.
    Psalms 139:22
      תַּכְלִית שִׂנְאָה שְׂנֵאתִים לְאוֹיְבִים הָיוּ לִֽי׃
    → I hated those who hated their enemies.
    Psalms 139:23
      חָקְרֵנִי אֵל וְדַע לְבָבִי בְּחָנֵנִי וְדַע שַׂרְעַפָּֽי׃
    → Know me well, and understand my heart through my actions.
    Psalms 139:24
      וּרְאֵה אִם־דֶּֽרֶךְ־עֹצֶב בִּי וּנְחֵנִי בְּדֶרֶךְ עוֹלָֽם׃
    → And see if there is a path of sorrow in me, and whether I will be left in a path of eternal darkness.
  Psalms 139 [en]: 24 vv, 3s
    Psalms 140:1
