    → By Solomon, son of David, king of Israel.
    Proverbs 1:2
      לָדַעַת חָכְמָה וּמוּסָר לְהָבִין אִמְרֵי בִינָֽה׃
    → To know wisdom and to understand the words of prophecy.
    Proverbs 1:3
      לָקַחַת מוּסַר הַשְׂכֵּל צֶדֶק וּמִשְׁפָּט וּמֵישָׁרִֽים׃
    → You have taken justice and fairness from those who are upright and honest.
    Proverbs 1:4
      לָתֵת לִפְתָאיִם עָרְמָה לְנַעַר דַּעַת וּמְזִמָּֽה׃
    → To suddenly give a young man knowledge and wisdom.
    Proverbs 1:5
      יִשְׁמַע חָכָם וְיוֹסֶף לֶקַח וְנָבוֹן תַּחְבֻּלוֹת יִקְנֶֽה׃
    → The wise man will listen, and he will take what is necessary. He will also gather up all the necessary items.
    Proverbs 1:6
      לְהָבִין מָשָׁל וּמְלִיצָה דִּבְרֵי חֲכָמִים וְחִידֹתָֽם׃
    → To understand the wisdom and teachings of the sages.
    Proverbs 1:7
      יִרְאַת יְהוָה רֵאשִׁית דָּעַת חָכְמָה וּמוּסָר אֱוִילִים בָּֽזוּ׃
    → Fear of Jehovah is the beginning of wisdom and knowledge. It also involves the proper handling of wild animals.
    Proverbs 1:8
      שְׁמַע בְּנִי מוּסַר אָבִיךָ וְאַל־תִּטֹּשׁ תּוֹרַת אִמֶּֽךָ׃
    → Listen, my son, to the teachings of your father. Do not break the laws of your mother.
    Proverbs 1:9
      כִּי ׀ לִוְיַת חֵן הֵם לְרֹאשֶׁךָ וַעֲנָקִים לְגַרְגְּרֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → For they are like cherubim for your head, and serpents for your horns.
    Proverbs 1:10
      בְּנִי אִם־יְפַתּוּךָ חַטָּאִים אַל־תֹּבֵֽא׃
    → Son, if you commit sins, do not bring them out into the light.
    Proverbs 1:11
      אִם־יֹאמְרוּ לְכָה אִתָּנוּ נֶאֶרְבָה לְדָם נִצְפְּנָה לְנָקִי חִנָּֽם׃
    → If they say to us, “Let us be destroyed by bloodshed,” then let us be purified through sacrifice.
    Proverbs 1:12
      נִבְלָעֵם כִּשְׁאוֹל חַיִּים וּתְמִימִים כְּיוֹרְדֵי בֽוֹר׃
    → They are swallowed up when they are alive and innocent, like branches that fall from a tree.
    Proverbs 1:13
      כָּל־הוֹן יָקָר נִמְצָא נְמַלֵּא בָתֵּינוּ שָׁלָֽל׃
    → All those treasures were found in our homes. They were filled with wealth.
    Proverbs 1:14
      גּוֹרָלְךָ תַּפִּיל בְּתוֹכֵנוּ כִּיס אֶחָד יִהְיֶה לְכֻלָּֽנוּ׃
    → Your glory will be shared among us, like a single bag. It will belong to all of us.
    Proverbs 1:15
      בְּנִי אַל־תֵּלֵךְ בְּדֶרֶךְ אִתָּם מְנַע רַגְלְךָ מִנְּתִיבָתָֽם׃
    → Son, do not walk in their ways. Let your feet not be led along by their path.
    Proverbs 1:16
      כִּי רַגְלֵיהֶם לָרַע יָרוּצוּ וִֽימַהֲרוּ לִשְׁפָּךְ־דָּֽם׃
    → For their feet desire evil, and they hurry to shed blood.
    Proverbs 1:17
      כִּֽי־חִנָּם מְזֹרָה הָרָשֶׁת בְּעֵינֵי כָל־בַּעַל כָּנָֽף׃
    → For their beauty, they were despised in the eyes of all men.
    Proverbs 1:18
      וְהֵם לְדָמָם יֶאֱרֹבוּ יִצְפְּנוּ לְנַפְשֹׁתָֽם׃
    → And they shall be filled with joy; they shall rejoice in their hearts.
    Proverbs 1:19
      כֵּן אָרְחוֹת כָּל־בֹּצֵֽעַ בָּצַע אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ בְּעָלָיו יִקָּֽח׃
    → So, every one who does evil deeds will be punished for his own actions.
    Proverbs 1:20
      חָכְמוֹת בַּחוּץ תָּרֹנָּה בָּרְחֹבוֹת תִּתֵּן קוֹלָֽהּ׃
    → The wise ones, who are far away, cry out in the wilderness.
    Proverbs 1:21
      בְּרֹאשׁ הֹמִיּוֹת תִּקְרָא בְּפִתְחֵי שְׁעָרִים בָּעִיר אֲמָרֶיהָ תֹאמֵֽר׃
    → At the entrance to the gates of the city, it shall be called in Hebrew.
    Proverbs 1:22
      עַד־מָתַי ׀ פְּתָיִם תְּֽאֵהֲבוּ פֶתִי וְלֵצִים לָצוֹן חָמְדוּ לָהֶם וּכְסִילִים יִשְׂנְאוּ־דָֽעַת׃
    → Until death, they will still love me. They will seek to please me and do what I command them. But the foolish will hate me for my knowledge.
    Proverbs 1:23
      תָּשׁוּבוּ לְֽתוֹכַחְתִּי הִנֵּה אַבִּיעָה לָכֶם רוּחִי אוֹדִיעָה דְבָרַי אֶתְכֶֽם׃
    → Return to my presence. Now, I send you my spirit as a message to you. I speak to you through this message.
    Proverbs 1:24
      יַעַן קָרָאתִי וַתְּמָאֵנוּ נָטִיתִי יָדִי וְאֵין מַקְשִֽׁיב׃
    → I called out, but no one heard me. I stretched out my hand, but no one responded.
    Proverbs 1:25
      וַתִּפְרְעוּ כָל־עֲצָתִי וְתוֹכַחְתִּי לֹא אֲבִיתֶֽם׃
    → And all my plans failed; I was left without any hope.
    Proverbs 1:26
      גַּם־אֲנִי בְּאֵידְכֶם אֶשְׂחָק אֶלְעַג בְּבֹא פַחְדְּכֶֽם׃
    → I too will laugh at you when you are in fear.
    Proverbs 1:27
      בְּבֹא כְשׁוֹאָה ׀ פַּחְדְּכֶם וְֽאֵידְכֶם כְּסוּפָה יֶאֱתֶה בְּבֹא עֲלֵיכֶם צָרָה וְצוּקָֽה׃
    → When fear and anxiety come upon you, it will bring suffering and distress upon you.
    Proverbs 1:28
      אָז יִקְרָאֻנְנִי וְלֹא אֶֽעֱנֶה יְשַׁחֲרֻנְנִי וְלֹא יִמְצָאֻֽנְנִי׃
    → Then he will call me, but I won’t answer. He will try to harm me, but I won’t be found.
    Proverbs 1:29
      תַּחַת כִּי־שָׂנְאוּ דָעַת וְיִרְאַת יְהֹוָה לֹא בָחָֽרוּ׃
    → For they did not choose to follow the knowledge and fear of Jehovah.
    Proverbs 1:30
      לֹא־אָבוּ לַעֲצָתִי נָאֲצוּ כָּל־תּוֹכַחְתִּֽי׃
    → Do not follow my advice; let all my efforts be in vain.
    Proverbs 1:31
      וְֽיֹאכְלוּ מִפְּרִי דַרְכָּם וּֽמִמֹּעֲצֹתֵיהֶם יִשְׂבָּֽעוּ׃
    → And they would eat from their own fruits, and they would rejoice with their own decisions.
    Proverbs 1:32
      כִּי מְשׁוּבַת פְּתָיִם תַּֽהַרְגֵם וְשַׁלְוַת כְּסִילִים תְּאַבְּדֵֽם׃
    → For the return of fools will kill them, and the foolishness of those who are stupid will destroy them.
    Proverbs 1:33
      וְשֹׁמֵעַֽ לִי יִשְׁכָּן־בֶּטַח וְשַׁאֲנַן מִפַּחַד רָעָֽה׃
    → And he who hears me will dwell in safety, and we will be free from fear.
  Proverbs 1 [en]: 33 vv, 4s
    Proverbs 2:1
      בְּנִי אִם־תִּקַּח אֲמָרָי וּמִצְוֺתַי תִּצְפֹּן אִתָּֽךְ׃
    → Son, if you take my words and my commands seriously, then you will be blessed.
    Proverbs 2:2
      לְהַקְשִׁיב לַֽחָכְמָה אָזְנֶךָ תַּטֶּה לִבְּךָ לַתְּבוּנָֽה׃
    → To listen to wisdom, your ears will become attentive, and your heart will be open to understanding.
    Proverbs 2:3
      כִּי אִם לַבִּינָה תִקְרָא לַתְּבוּנָה תִּתֵּן קוֹלֶֽךָ׃
    → For if understanding is called “understanding,” then your voice will be heard.
    Proverbs 2:4
      אִם־תְּבַקְשֶׁנָּה כַכָּסֶף וְֽכַמַּטְמוֹנִים תַּחְפְּשֶֽׂנָּה׃
    → If you ask for gold and other treasures, then search for them.
    Proverbs 2:5
      אָז תָּבִין יִרְאַת יְהוָה וְדַעַת אֱלֹהִים תִּמְצָֽא׃
    → Then you will find the fear of Jehovah and knowledge of God.
    Proverbs 2:6
      כִּֽי־יְהוָה יִתֵּן חָכְמָה מִפִּיו דַּעַת וּתְבוּנָֽה׃
    → For Jehovah will give wisdom from His mouth; knowledge and understanding will be given to him.
    Proverbs 2:7
      יִצְפֹּן לַיְשָׁרִים תּוּשִׁיָּה מָגֵן לְהֹלְכֵי תֹֽם׃
    → May they be protected by the Lord from those who go astray.
    Proverbs 2:8
      לִנְצֹר אָרְחוֹת מִשְׁפָּט וְדֶרֶךְ חֲסִידָיו יִשְׁמֹֽר׃
    → May the laws of justice and the path of those who are righteous be preserved.
    Proverbs 2:9
      אָז תָּבִין צֶדֶק וּמִשְׁפָּט וּמֵישָׁרִים כָּל־מַעְגַּל־טֽוֹב׃
    → Then you will understand justice and righteousness, and all that is good.
    Proverbs 2:10
      כִּֽי־תָבוֹא חָכְמָה בְלִבֶּךָ וְדַעַת לְֽנַפְשְׁךָ יִנְעָֽם׃
    → For if wisdom enters your heart and knowledge fills your soul, then everything will be fine.
    Proverbs 2:11
      מְזִמָּה תִּשְׁמֹר עָלֶיךָ תְּבוּנָה תִנְצְרֶֽכָּה׃
    → May the invitation be kept safe for you; it will be preserved.
    Proverbs 2:12
      לְהַצִּילְךָ מִדֶּרֶךְ רָע מֵאִישׁ מְדַבֵּר תַּהְפֻּכֽוֹת׃
    → To save you from a bad path, from someone who talks nonsense.
    Proverbs 2:13
      הַעֹזְבִים אָרְחוֹת יֹשֶׁר לָלֶכֶת בְּדַרְכֵי־חֹֽשֶׁךְ׃
    → They leave their homes to go along the dark paths.
    Proverbs 2:14
      הַשְּׂמֵחִים לַעֲשׂוֹת רָע יָגִילוּ בְּֽתַהְפֻּכוֹת רָֽע׃
    → Those who are happy to do evil will be punished in terrible ways.
    Proverbs 2:15
      אֲשֶׁר אָרְחֹתֵיהֶם עִקְּשִׁים וּנְלוֹזִים בְּמַעְגְּלוֹתָֽם׃
    → Their nests are stubborn and are stored in their corners.
    Proverbs 2:16
      לְהַצִּילְךָ מֵאִשָּׁה זָרָה מִנָּכְרִיָּה אֲמָרֶיהָ הֶחֱלִֽיקָה׃
    → To save you from a foreign woman from a foreign land, her words were “Hurry up!”
    Proverbs 2:17
      הַעֹזֶבֶת אַלּוּף נְעוּרֶיהָ וְאֶת־בְּרִית אֱלֹהֶיהָ שָׁכֵֽחָה׃
    → She abandoned her thousands of children, and also her covenant with God.
    Proverbs 2:18
      כִּי שָׁחָה אֶל־מָוֶת בֵּיתָהּ וְאֶל־רְפָאִים מַעְגְּלֹתֶֽיהָ׃
    → For her house has fallen into death, and her doctors are unable to cure her illnesses.
    Proverbs 2:19
      כָּל־בָּאֶיהָ לֹא יְשׁוּבוּן וְלֹֽא־יַשִּׂיגוּ אָרְחוֹת חַיִּֽים׃
    → All those who come there will not be able to return, nor will they find a place where they can live.
    Proverbs 2:20
      לְמַעַן תֵּלֵךְ בְּדֶרֶךְ טוֹבִים וְאָרְחוֹת צַדִּיקִים תִּשְׁמֹֽר׃
    → So that you may walk in a good path and maintain the friendships of the righteous.
    Proverbs 2:21
      כִּֽי־יְשָׁרִים יִשְׁכְּנוּ אָרֶץ וּתְמִימִים יִוָּתְרוּ בָֽהּ׃
    → For the righteous will dwell in the land, and the pure will be allowed to live there.
    Proverbs 2:22
      וּרְשָׁעִים מֵאֶרֶץ יִכָּרֵתוּ וּבוֹגְדִים יִסְּחוּ מִמֶּֽנָּה׃
    → And the wicked will be destroyed from the earth, and those who are treacherous will be driven away from there.
  Proverbs 2 [en]: 22 vv, 2s
    Proverbs 3:1
      בְּנִי תּוֹרָתִי אַל־תִּשְׁכָּח וּמִצְוֺתַי יִצֹּר לִבֶּֽךָ׃
    → Son, do not forget my teachings; and keep my commandments in your heart.
    Proverbs 3:2
      כִּי אֹרֶךְ יָמִים וּשְׁנוֹת חַיִּים וְשָׁלוֹם יוֹסִיפוּ לָֽךְ׃
    → For days and years of life will pass by, and peace will continue to be with you.
    Proverbs 3:3
      חֶסֶד וֶאֱמֶת אַֽל־יַעַזְבֻךָ קָשְׁרֵם עַל־גַּרְגְּרוֹתֶיךָ כָּתְבֵם עַל־לוּחַ לִבֶּֽךָ׃
    → Mercy and truth will keep you safe from harm. They will protect your children, as they are written on your heart.
    Proverbs 3:4
      וּמְצָא־חֵן וְשֵֽׂכֶל־טוֹב בְּעֵינֵי אֱלֹהִים וְאָדָֽם׃
    → And he found grace and good judgment in the eyes of God and man.
    Proverbs 3:5
      בְּטַח אֶל־יְהוָה בְּכָל־לִבֶּךָ וְאֶל־בִּֽינָתְךָ אַל־תִּשָּׁעֵֽן׃
    → With all your heart, and with all your soul, you must adore the LORD. Do not forget to do this.
    Proverbs 3:6
      בְּכָל־דְּרָכֶיךָ דָעֵהוּ וְהוּא יְיַשֵּׁר אֹֽרְחֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → In all your ways, know him; and he will make your lodging comfortable.
    Proverbs 3:7
      אַל־תְּהִי חָכָם בְּעֵינֶיךָ יְרָא אֶת־יְהוָה וְסוּר מֵרָֽע׃
    → Do not be wise in your own eyes. Fear the LORD and do what is right.
    Proverbs 3:8
      רִפְאוּת תְּהִי לְשָׁרֶּךָ וְשִׁקּוּי לְעַצְמוֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → May healing be upon you, and may you be restored to your former state.
    Proverbs 3:9
      כַּבֵּד אֶת־יְהוָה מֵהוֹנֶךָ וּמֵרֵאשִׁית כָּל־תְּבוּאָתֶֽךָ׃
    → I will hate You, O LORD, from now on, and from the beginning of all Your reigns.
    Proverbs 3:10
      וְיִמָּלְאוּ אֲסָמֶיךָ שָׂבָע וְתִירוֹשׁ יְקָבֶיךָ יִפְרֹֽצוּ׃
    → And their camps will be filled with thousands; your inheritance will be divided among you.
    Proverbs 3:11
      מוּסַר יְהוָה בְּנִי אַל־תִּמְאָס וְאַל־תָּקֹץ בְּתוֹכַחְתּֽוֹ׃
    → May the LORD protect me from being destroyed or lost in my own thoughts.
    Proverbs 3:12
      כִּי אֶת אֲשֶׁר יֶאֱהַב יְהוָה יוֹכִיחַ וּכְאָב אֶת־בֵּן יִרְצֶֽה׃
    → For He will protect those whom He loves, and He will cause no harm to His children.
    Proverbs 3:13
      אַשְׁרֵי אָדָם מָצָא חָכְמָה וְאָדָם יָפִיק תְּבוּנָֽה׃
    → When a man finds wisdom, he will build a structure.
    Proverbs 3:14
      כִּי טוֹב סַחְרָהּ מִסְּחַר־כָּסֶף וּמֵחָרוּץ תְּבוּאָתָֽהּ׃
    → For it is better to trade in silver and to come out from the trade of selling.
    Proverbs 3:15
      יְקָרָה הִיא מִפְּנִינִים וְכָל־חֲפָצֶיךָ לֹא יִֽשְׁווּ־בָֽהּ׃
    → She is precious; her treasures and all your desires cannot be compared to her.
    Proverbs 3:16
      אֹרֶךְ יָמִים בִּֽימִינָהּ בִּשְׂמֹאולָהּ עֹשֶׁר וְכָבֽוֹד׃
    → It will last for many days in her hand, in Shemoyloh. It will be prosperous and abundant.
    Proverbs 3:17
      דְּרָכֶיהָ דַרְכֵי־נֹעַם וְֽכָל־נְתִיבוֹתֶיהָ שָׁלֽוֹם׃
    → Her paths are paths of sorrow, and all her ways lead to destruction.
    Proverbs 3:18
      עֵץ־חַיִּים הִיא לַמַּחֲזִיקִים בָּהּ וְֽתֹמְכֶיהָ מְאֻשָּֽׁר׃
    → A “Tree of Life” is something that those who possess it can use for their own benefit.
    Proverbs 3:19
      יְֽהוָה בְּחָכְמָה יָֽסַד־אָרֶץ כּוֹנֵן שָׁמַיִם בִּתְבוּנָֽה׃
    → YHWH, in His wisdom, created the earth and arranged the heavens in order.
    Proverbs 3:20
      בְּדַעְתּוֹ תְּהוֹמוֹת נִבְקָעוּ וּשְׁחָקִים יִרְעֲפוּ־טָֽל׃
    → In his knowledge, those who were lost will be brought back, and those who were scattered will be gathered together.
    Proverbs 3:21
      בְּנִי אַל־יָלֻזוּ מֵעֵינֶיךָ נְצֹר תֻּשִׁיָּה וּמְזִמָּֽה׃
    → My son, Al-Yaluzu, from your eyes, a creation of Tushiya and Mizma.
    Proverbs 3:22
      וְיִֽהְיוּ חַיִּים לְנַפְשֶׁךָ וְחֵן לְגַרְגְּרֹתֶֽיךָ׃
    → And they shall be living for your soul, and bring glory to your flocks.
    Proverbs 3:23
      אָז תֵּלֵךְ לָבֶטַח דַּרְכֶּךָ וְרַגְלְךָ לֹא תִגּֽוֹף׃
    → Then you shall walk in your path with confidence, and your feet shall not stumble.
    Proverbs 3:24
      אִם־תִּשְׁכַּב לֹֽא־תִפְחָד וְשָׁכַבְתָּ וְֽעָרְבָה שְׁנָתֶֽךָ׃
    → If you lie down without fear, and you sleep through the night.
    Proverbs 3:25
      אַל־תִּירָא מִפַּחַד פִּתְאֹם וּמִשֹּׁאַת רְשָׁעִים כִּי תָבֹֽא׃
    → Do not be afraid of sudden fear or the schemes of the wicked, when you go out.
    Proverbs 3:26
      כִּֽי־יְהוָה יִהְיֶה בְכִסְלֶךָ וְשָׁמַר רַגְלְךָ מִלָּֽכֶד׃
    → For Jehovah will be in your midst, and He will protect your feet from harm.
    Proverbs 3:27
      אַל־תִּמְנַע־טוֹב מִבְּעָלָיו בִּהְיוֹת לְאֵל יָדְךָ לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃
    → Do not hesitate to do what is right, since you are the one who has the power to do it.
    Proverbs 3:28
      אַל־תֹּאמַר לְרֵֽעֲךָ ׀ לֵךְ וָשׁוּב וּמָחָר אֶתֵּן וְיֵשׁ אִתָּֽךְ׃
    → Do not say to your friend, “Go back later; I will give it to you then.” There will be something with you already.
    Proverbs 3:29
      אַל־תַּחֲרֹשׁ עַל־רֵעֲךָ רָעָה וְהֽוּא־יוֹשֵׁב לָבֶטַח אִתָּֽךְ׃
    → Do not do any harm to your brother. He will surely take care of you.
    Proverbs 3:30
      אַל־תָּרִיב עִם־אָדָם חִנָּם אִם־לֹא גְמָלְךָ רָעָֽה׃
    → Do not quarrel with a man who is innocent. If he has not done you any harm, then do not blame him.
    Proverbs 3:31
      אַל־תְּקַנֵּא בְּאִישׁ חָמָס וְאַל־תִּבְחַר בְּכָל־דְּרָכָֽיו׃
    → Do not be jealous of a man who is rich, and do not follow all his ways.
    Proverbs 3:32
      כִּי תוֹעֲבַת יְהוָה נָלוֹז וְֽאֶת־יְשָׁרִים סוֹדֽוֹ׃
    → For the LORD’s anger is stored up against the righteous.
    Proverbs 3:33
      מְאֵרַת יְהוָה בְּבֵית רָשָׁע וּנְוֵה צַדִּיקִים יְבָרֵֽךְ׃
    → May the Lord’s word be blessed in the house of the wicked, while the righteous are blessed.
    Proverbs 3:34
      אִם־לַלֵּצִים הֽוּא־יָלִיץ וְלַעֲנָוִים יִתֶּן־חֵֽן׃
    → If they ask for help, He will provide them with sustenance. And those who are in need will be given what they deserve.
    Proverbs 3:35
      כָּבוֹד חֲכָמִים יִנְחָלוּ וּכְסִילִים מֵרִים קָלֽוֹן׃
    → Glory shall be given to the wise, while fools will be brought down to earth.
  Proverbs 3 [en]: 35 vv, 4s
    Proverbs 4:1
      שִׁמְעוּ בָנִים מוּסַר אָב וְהַקְשִׁיבוּ לָדַעַת בִּינָֽה׃
    → Hear, children, what your father has said; and listen carefully to gain understanding.
    Proverbs 4:2
      כִּי לֶקַח טוֹב נָתַתִּי לָכֶם תּֽוֹרָתִי אַֽל־תַּעֲזֹֽבוּ׃
    → For I have given you My Torah as good. Do not take away it from you.
    Proverbs 4:3
      כִּי־בֵן הָיִיתִי לְאָבִי רַךְ וְיָחִיד לִפְנֵי אִמִּֽי׃
    → For I was the only son of my father, and I was his sole child before my mother.
    Proverbs 4:4
      וַיֹּרֵנִי וַיֹּאמֶר לִי יִֽתְמָךְ־דְּבָרַי לִבֶּךָ שְׁמֹר מִצְוֺתַי וֶֽחְיֵֽה׃
    → And he questioned me, saying to me, “O my son, hear my words. Obey my commands and live.”
    Proverbs 4:5
      קְנֵה חָכְמָה קְנֵה בִינָה אַל־תִּשְׁכַּח וְאַל־תֵּט מֵֽאִמְרֵי־פִֽי׃
    → Buy wisdom; buy understanding. Do not forget it, and do not lose the words that come from your mouth.
    Proverbs 4:6
      אַל־תַּעַזְבֶהָ וְתִשְׁמְרֶךָּ אֱהָבֶהָ וְתִצְּרֶֽךָּ׃
    → Do not leave her; keep her in your love and care.
    Proverbs 4:7
      רֵאשִׁית חָכְמָה קְנֵה חָכְמָה וּבְכָל־קִנְיָנְךָ קְנֵה בִינָֽה׃
    → At the beginning, wisdom was given to him; and in all that he acquired, he also received wisdom.
    Proverbs 4:8
      סַלְסְלֶהָ וּֽתְרוֹמְמֶךָּ תְּכַבֵּדְךָ כִּי תְחַבְּקֶֽנָּה׃
    → Salsela and Trommekha will delight you, for they are our beloved ones.
    Proverbs 4:9
      תִּתֵּן לְרֹאשְׁךָ לִוְיַת־חֵן עֲטֶרֶת תִּפְאֶרֶת תְּמַגְּנֶֽךָּ׃
    → Give your head the grace of beauty and adornment.
    Proverbs 4:10
      שְׁמַע בְּנִי וְקַח אֲמָרָי וְיִרְבּוּ לְךָ שְׁנוֹת חַיִּֽים׃
    → Listen, my son, and take my words to heart. May they bring you many years of life.
    Proverbs 4:11
      בְּדֶרֶךְ חָכְמָה הֹרֵתִיךָ הִדְרַכְתִּיךָ בְּמַעְגְּלֵי־יֹֽשֶׁר׃
    → In wisdom, you have guided me along the paths of righteousness.
    Proverbs 4:12
      בְּֽלֶכְתְּךָ לֹא־יֵצַר צַעֲדֶךָ וְאִם־תָּרוּץ לֹא תִכָּשֵֽׁל׃
    → When you go, your steps will not be hindered; and if you run, you will not stumble.
    Proverbs 4:13
      הַחֲזֵק בַּמּוּסָר אַל־תֶּרֶף נִצְּרֶהָ כִּי־הִיא חַיֶּֽיךָ׃
    → The strength in the process of creation is not to be destroyed, for it is eternal.
    Proverbs 4:14
      בְּאֹרַח רְשָׁעִים אַל־תָּבֹא וְאַל־תְּאַשֵּׁר בְּדֶרֶךְ רָעִֽים׃
    → Do not enter the house of the wicked, and do not walk in their paths.
    Proverbs 4:15
      פְּרָעֵהוּ אַל־תַּעֲבָר־בּוֹ שְׂטֵה מֵעָלָיו וַעֲבֽוֹר׃
    → May not there be any dirt or filth on it.
    Proverbs 4:16
      כִּי לֹא יִֽשְׁנוּ אִם־לֹא יָרֵעוּ וְֽנִגְזְלָה שְׁנָתָם אִם־לֹא יַכְשִֽׁילוּ׃
    → For they will not be able to change their ways unless they repent. Their years will be wasted if they do not change their behavior.
    Proverbs 4:17
      כִּי לָחֲמוּ לֶחֶם רֶשַׁע וְיֵין חֲמָסִים יִשְׁתּֽוּ׃
    → For evil bread and bad wine will cause people to become drunk.
    Proverbs 4:18
      וְאֹרַח צַדִּיקִים כְּאוֹר נֹגַהּ הוֹלֵךְ וָאוֹר עַד־נְכוֹן הַיּֽוֹם׃
    → And the light of the righteous will shine like the light of a lamp that continues to burn until the end of the day.
    Proverbs 4:19
      דֶּרֶךְ רְשָׁעִים כָּֽאֲפֵלָה לֹא יָדְעוּ בַּמֶּה יִכָּשֵֽׁלוּ׃
    → The path of the wicked is like darkness; they will never know what awaits them.
    Proverbs 4:20
      בְּנִי לִדְבָרַי הַקְשִׁיבָה לַאֲמָרַי הַט־אָזְנֶֽךָ׃
    → Son, listen to my words. Pay attention to what I say.
    Proverbs 4:21
      אַל־יַלִּיזוּ מֵעֵינֶיךָ שָׁמְרֵם בְּתוֹךְ לְבָבֶֽךָ׃
    → Do not let them be hidden from your eyes; they are kept within your heart.
    Proverbs 4:22
      כִּֽי־חַיִּים הֵם לְמֹצְאֵיהֶם וּֽלְכָל־בְּשָׂרוֹ מַרְפֵּֽא׃
    → For they are alive, and their words bring healing to all who hear them.
    Proverbs 4:23
      מִֽכָּל־מִשְׁמָר נְצֹר לִבֶּךָ כִּֽי־מִמֶּנּוּ תּוֹצְאוֹת חַיִּֽים׃
    → From every corner of the world, let your heart be filled with hope, for from there will come life.
    Proverbs 4:24
      הָסֵר מִמְּךָ עִקְּשׁוּת פֶּה וּלְזוּת שְׂפָתַיִם הַרְחֵק מִמֶּֽךָּ׃
    → May the stubbornness of your heart be removed from you, and may your words be kept away from you.
    Proverbs 4:25
      עֵינֶיךָ לְנֹכַח יַבִּיטוּ וְעַפְעַפֶּיךָ יַיְשִׁרוּ נֶגְדֶּֽךָ׃
    → Your eyes shall watch over us, and your eyelids shall be turned away from you.
    Proverbs 4:26
      פַּלֵּס מַעְגַּל רַגְלֶךָ וְֽכָל־דְּרָכֶיךָ יִכֹּֽנוּ׃
    → May your feet be bound, and all your paths be blocked.
    Proverbs 4:27
      אַֽל־תֵּט־יָמִין וּשְׂמֹאול הָסֵר רַגְלְךָ מֵרָֽע׃
    → Do not let Al-Tet-Yamim and Shemoel take your feet away from evil.
  Proverbs 4 [en]: 27 vv, 3s
    Proverbs 5:1
      בְּנִי לְחָכְמָתִי הַקְשִׁיבָה לִתְבוּנָתִי הַט־אָזְנֶֽךָ׃
    → My son, by my wisdom, listen to my words; your ears should be attentive.
    Proverbs 5:2
      לִשְׁמֹר מְזִמּוֹת וְדַעַת שְׂפָתֶיךָ יִנְצֹֽרוּ׃
    → Be careful to keep your words and thoughts in check.
    Proverbs 5:3
      כִּי נֹפֶת תִּטֹּפְנָה שִׂפְתֵי זָרָה וְחָלָק מִשֶּׁמֶן חִכָּֽהּ׃
    → For those who are foreign to God’s ways, their lips will be closed, and part of their breath will be held back.
    Proverbs 5:4
      וְֽאַחֲרִיתָהּ מָרָה כַֽלַּעֲנָה חַדָּה כְּחֶרֶב פִּיּֽוֹת׃
    → And after that, it became like a burning fire, as if it were a terrible disaster.
    Proverbs 5:5
      רַגְלֶיהָ יֹרְדוֹת מָוֶת שְׁאוֹל צְעָדֶיהָ יִתְמֹֽכוּ׃
    → Her feet descend from death; her steps are still moving forward.
    Proverbs 5:6
      אֹרַח חַיִּים פֶּן־תְּפַלֵּס נָעוּ מַעְגְּלֹתֶיהָ לֹא תֵדָֽע׃
    → Let them live in peace; let them not be destroyed by their own mistakes. You will not know what will happen.
    Proverbs 5:7
      וְעַתָּה בָנִים שִׁמְעוּ־לִי וְאַל־תָּסוּרוּ מֵאִמְרֵי־פִֽי׃
    → And now, sons, listen to me. Do not ignore what I say.
    Proverbs 5:8
      הַרְחֵק מֵעָלֶיהָ דַרְכֶּךָ וְאַל־תִּקְרַב אֶל־פֶּתַח בֵּיתָֽהּ׃
    → Stay away from her. Do not approach the door of her house.
    Proverbs 5:9
      פֶּן־תִּתֵּן לַאֲחֵרִים הוֹדֶךָ וּשְׁנֹתֶיךָ לְאַכְזָרִֽי׃
    → Do not give your honor and your love to the wicked.
    Proverbs 5:10
      פֶּֽן־יִשְׂבְּעוּ זָרִים כֹּחֶךָ וַעֲצָבֶיךָ בְּבֵית נָכְרִֽי׃
    → May the foreigners praise your strength and your beauty in a foreign land.
    Proverbs 5:11
      וְנָהַמְתָּ בְאַחֲרִיתֶךָ בִּכְלוֹת בְּשָׂרְךָ וּשְׁאֵרֶֽךָ׃
    → And you will die in your later years, with your tongue and your remaining body also.
    Proverbs 5:12
      וְֽאָמַרְתָּ אֵיךְ שָׂנֵאתִי מוּסָר וְתוֹכַחַת נָאַץ לִבִּֽי׃
    → And you said, “How I love Musar… Please let my heart be at peace.”
    Proverbs 5:13
      וְֽלֹא־שָׁמַעְתִּי בְּקוֹל מוֹרָי וְלִֽמְלַמְּדַי לֹא־הִטִּיתִי אָזְנִֽי׃
    → And I did not hear the voice of the Lord; I did not pay attention to His teachings.
    Proverbs 5:14
      כִּמְעַט הָיִיתִי בְכָל־רָע בְּתוֹךְ קָהָל וְעֵדָֽה׃
    → Although I was in all kinds of trouble among a crowd and a council.
    Proverbs 5:15
      שְׁתֵה־מַיִם מִבּוֹרֶךָ וְנֹזְלִים מִתּוֹךְ בְּאֵרֶֽךָ׃
    → Fill your vessels with water, and let them be filled with water throughout your journey.
    Proverbs 5:16
      יָפוּצוּ מַעְיְנֹתֶיךָ חוּצָה בָּרְחֹבוֹת פַּלְגֵי־מָֽיִם׃
    → They will be freed from your bonds; they will be released into the vast depths of the oceans.
    Proverbs 5:17
      יִֽהְיוּ־לְךָ לְבַדֶּךָ וְאֵין לְזָרִים אִתָּֽךְ׃
    → It shall be yours alone; no one else shall have it.
    Proverbs 5:18
      יְהִֽי־מְקוֹרְךָ בָרוּךְ וּשְׂמַח מֵאֵשֶׁת נְעוּרֶֽךָ׃
