    → In his arms, He will hold the wicked; from Jehovah, all judgments will come.
  Proverbs 16 [en]: 33 vv, 4s
    Proverbs 17:1
      טוֹב פַּת חֲרֵבָה וְשַׁלְוָה־בָהּ מִבַּיִת מָלֵא זִבְחֵי־רִֽיב׃
    → It is good to be poor and humble; it brings peace from the house filled with idols of Rib.
    Proverbs 17:2
      עֶֽבֶד־מַשְׂכִּיל יִמְשֹׁל בְּבֵן מֵבִישׁ וּבְתוֹךְ אַחִים יַחֲלֹק נַחֲלָֽה׃
    → A wise servant will rule over his son, and among his brothers, he will divide the inheritance.
    Proverbs 17:3
      מַצְרֵף לַכֶּסֶף וְכוּר לַזָּהָב וּבֹחֵן לִבּוֹת יְהוָֽה׃
    → It is used to make coins and jewelry from gold, and also for making ornaments for the Lord’s temples.
    Proverbs 17:4
      מֵרַע מַקְשִׁיב עַל־שְׂפַת־אָוֶן שֶׁקֶר מֵזִין עַל־לְשׁוֹן הַוֺּֽת׃
    → May evil listen to the words of a false prophet who lies on the lips of those who are worthy.
    Proverbs 17:5
      לֹעֵג לָרָשׁ חֵרֵף עֹשֵׂהוּ שָׂמֵחַ לְאֵיד לֹא יִנָּקֶֽה׃
    → Let not the ruler be harsh; he who is harsh will never be happy.
    Proverbs 17:6
      עֲטֶרֶת זְקֵנִים בְּנֵי בָנִים וְתִפְאֶרֶת בָּנִים אֲבוֹתָֽם׃
    → They honor the elderly with sons, and they adorn their sons with the honors of their fathers.
    Proverbs 17:7
      לֹא־נָאוָה לְנָבָל שְׂפַת־יֶתֶר אַף כִּֽי־לְנָדִיב שְׂפַת־שָֽׁקֶר׃
    → It’s not pleasing to the tongue of those who speak lies, even if they are kind-hearted people who speak truth.
    Proverbs 17:8
      אֶֽבֶן־חֵן הַשֹּׁחַד בְּעֵינֵי בְעָלָיו אֶֽל־כָּל־אֲשֶׁר יִפְנֶה יַשְׂכִּֽיל׃
    → Eben-Han, who causes destruction in the eyes of his master, to all those who turn towards him.
    Proverbs 17:9
      מְֽכַסֶּה־פֶּשַׁע מְבַקֵּשׁ אַהֲבָה וְשֹׁנֶה בְדָבָר מַפְרִיד אַלּֽוּף׃
    → Hiding one’s sins, seeking love and reconciliation through words that can divide people.
    Proverbs 17:10
      תֵּחַת גְּעָרָה בְמֵבִין מֵהַכּוֹת כְּסִיל מֵאָֽה׃
    → Under the anger of those who understand nothing, like a fool.
    Proverbs 17:11
      אַךְ־מְרִי יְבַקֶּשׁ־רָע וּמַלְאָךְ אַכְזָרִי יְשֻׁלַּח־בּֽוֹ׃
    → But the wicked will seek evil, and the cruel rulers will send it.
    Proverbs 17:12
      פָּגוֹשׁ דֹּב שַׁכּוּל בְּאִישׁ וְאַל־כְּסִיל בְּאִוַּלְתּֽוֹ׃
    → Pagoosh Dov Shakul in a man, and Al-Kesil in a woman.
    Proverbs 17:13
      מֵשִׁיב רָעָה תַּחַת טוֹבָה לֹא־תָמוּשׁ רָעָה מִבֵּיתֽוֹ׃
    → May evil be replaced by good. Do not let evil remain in your home.
    Proverbs 17:14
      פּוֹטֵֽר מַיִם רֵאשִׁית מָדוֹן וְלִפְנֵי הִתְגַּלַּע הָרִיב נְטֽוֹשׁ׃
    → The waters were first divided from each other, before the conflict began.
    Proverbs 17:15
      מַצְדִּיק רָשָׁע וּמַרְשִׁיעַ צַדִּיק תּוֹעֲבַת יְהוָה גַּם־שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃
    → The righteous can also be wicked, and the wicked can also be righteous. Both can cause harm to Jehovah’s laws.
    Proverbs 17:16
      לָמָּה־זֶּה מְחִיר בְּיַד־כְּסִיל לִקְנוֹת חָכְמָה וְלֶב־אָֽיִן׃
    → Why does a fool try to acquire wisdom and a wise heart?
    Proverbs 17:17
      בְּכָל־עֵת אֹהֵב הָרֵעַ וְאָח לְצָרָה יִוָּלֵֽד׃
    → At all times, the enemy loves his enemy; and he lives in harm.
    Proverbs 17:18
      אָדָם חֲסַר־לֵב תּוֹקֵעַ כָּף עֹרֵב עֲרֻבָּה לִפְנֵי רֵעֵֽהוּ׃
    → A heartless man will always be at a disadvantage before his enemy.
    Proverbs 17:19
      אֹהֵֽב פֶּשַׁע אֹהֵב מַצָּה מַגְבִּיהַּ פִּתְחוֹ מְבַקֶּשׁ־שָֽׁבֶר׃
    → He loves sin; he loves evil. He opens his mouth to speak lies.
    Proverbs 17:20
      עִקֶּשׁ־לֵב לֹא יִמְצָא־טוֹב וְנֶהְפָּךְ בִּלְשׁוֹנוֹ יִפּוֹל בְּרָעָֽה׃
    → A stubborn heart will never find what’s good; it will instead turn into something bad.
    Proverbs 17:21
      יֹלֵד כְּסִיל לְתוּגָה לוֹ וְלֹֽא־יִשְׂמַח אֲבִי נָבָֽל׃
    → A fool will be born, but he will not be happy. His father will be a wicked man.
    Proverbs 17:22
      לֵב שָׂמֵחַ יֵיטִב גֵּהָה וְרוּחַ נְכֵאָה תְּיַבֶּשׁ־גָּֽרֶם׃
    → A happy heart is a blessing; a sad spirit will be destroyed.
    Proverbs 17:23
      שֹׁחַד מֵחֵיק רָשָׁע יִקָּח לְהַטּוֹת אָרְחוֹת מִשְׁפָּֽט׃
    → The righteous shall take away from the wicked their places in judgment.
    Proverbs 17:24
      אֶת־פְּנֵי מֵבִין חָכְמָה וְעֵינֵי כְסִיל בִּקְצֵה־אָֽרֶץ׃
    → The eyes of the wise are like those of a fool, who is located at the edge of the earth.
    Proverbs 17:25
      כַּעַס לְאָבִיו בֵּן כְּסִיל וּמֶמֶר לְיוֹלַדְתּֽוֹ׃
    → Anger at his father, a child of ignorance and foolishness.
    Proverbs 17:26
      גַּם עֲנוֹשׁ לַצַּדִּיק לֹא־טוֹב לְהַכּוֹת נְדִיבִים עַל־יֹֽשֶׁר׃
    → It is also not good for the righteous to punish those who are generous.
    Proverbs 17:27
      חוֹשֵׂךְ אֲמָרָיו יוֹדֵעַ דָּעַת יְקַר־רוּחַ אִישׁ תְּבוּנָֽה׃
    → He who hears his words knows the wisdom of a person with noble heart.
    Proverbs 17:28
      גַּם אֱוִיל מַחֲרִישׁ חָכָם יֵחָשֵׁב אֹטֵם שְׂפָתָיו נָבֽוֹן׃
    → Even a wise fox will think carefully before speaking.
  Proverbs 17 [en]: 28 vv, 4s
    Proverbs 18:1
      לְֽתַאֲוָה יְבַקֵּשׁ נִפְרָד בְּכָל־תּוּשִׁיָּה יִתְגַּלָּֽע׃
    → In desperation, he will seek to be separated from all his possessions.
    Proverbs 18:2
      לֹֽא־יַחְפֹּץ כְּסִיל בִּתְבוּנָה כִּי אִֽם־בְּהִתְגַּלּוֹת לִבּֽוֹ׃
    → He will not run away like a fool in the midst of confusion, when his heart is revealed.
    Proverbs 18:3
      בְּֽבוֹא־רָשָׁע בָּא גַם־בּוּז וְֽעִם־קָלוֹן חֶרְפָּֽה׃
    → When the wicked come in, they also bring shame and disgrace with them.
    Proverbs 18:4
      מַיִם עֲמֻקִּים דִּבְרֵי פִי־אִישׁ נַחַל נֹבֵעַ מְקוֹר חָכְמָֽה׃
    → Deep waters; words spoken by a man’s mouth. A stream that flows away from the wisdom of a wise person.
    Proverbs 18:5
      שְׂאֵת פְּנֵי־רָשָׁע לֹא־טוֹב לְהַטּוֹת צַדִּיק בַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃
    → It is not good to turn the face of the wicked towards the righteous in judgment.
    Proverbs 18:6
      שִׂפְתֵי כְסִיל יָבֹאֽוּ בְרִיב וּפִיו לְֽמַהֲלֻמוֹת יִקְרָֽא׃
    → The lips of the fool will bring forth words of strife, and his mouth will speak lies.
    Proverbs 18:7
      פִּֽי־כְסִיל מְחִתָּה־לוֹ וּשְׂפָתָיו מוֹקֵשׁ נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃
    → His mouth is dumb, and his lips are heavy with sorrow.
    Proverbs 18:8
      דִּבְרֵי נִרְגָּן כְּמִֽתְלַהֲמִים וְהֵם יָרְדוּ חַדְרֵי־בָֽטֶן׃
    → The words of Nirgan were like flames; they descended into the depths of darkness.
    Proverbs 18:9
      גַּם מִתְרַפֶּה בִמְלַאכְתּוֹ אָח הוּא לְבַעַל מַשְׁחִֽית׃
    → And in his work, he also becomes a destroyer. He is indeed a man of destruction.
    Proverbs 18:10
      מִגְדַּל־עֹז שֵׁם יְהוָה בּֽוֹ־יָרוּץ צַדִּיק וְנִשְׂגָּֽב׃
    → From the mountain of God’s name, there will rise a righteous man who is blessed.
    Proverbs 18:11
      הוֹן עָשִׁיר קִרְיַת עֻזּוֹ וּכְחוֹמָה נִשְׂגָּבָה בְּמַשְׂכִּיתֽוֹ׃
    → Hon is rich, but his strength and power have been weakened by his own actions.
    Proverbs 18:12
      לִפְנֵי־שֶׁבֶר יִגְבַּהּ לֵב־אִישׁ וְלִפְנֵי כָבוֹד עֲנָוָֽה׃
    → Before honor, it becomes a source of pride for a person; but before shame, it becomes a source of humiliation.
    Proverbs 18:13
      מֵשִׁיב דָּבָר בְּטֶרֶם יִשְׁמָע אִוֶּלֶת הִיא־לוֹ וּכְלִמָּֽה׃
    → It is said that a word should be spoken before it can be heard by him.
    Proverbs 18:14
      רֽוּחַ־אִישׁ יְכַלְכֵּל מַחֲלֵהוּ וְרוּחַ נְכֵאָה מִי יִשָּׂאֶֽנָּה׃
    → A person’s spirit can cure their illness; but whose spirit can be carried away?
    Proverbs 18:15
      לֵב נָבוֹן יִקְנֶה־דָּעַת וְאֹזֶן חֲכָמִים תְּבַקֶּשׁ־דָּֽעַת׃
    → A foolish heart will gain knowledge; and with the ears of wise men, one can seek wisdom.
    Proverbs 18:16
      מַתָּן אָדָם יַרְחִיב לוֹ וְלִפְנֵי גְדֹלִים יַנְחֶֽנּוּ׃
    → May God make him grow larger, and may he be honored before the great ones.
    Proverbs 18:17
      צַדִּיק הָרִאשׁוֹן בְּרִיבוֹ וּבָֽא־רֵעֵהוּ וַחֲקָרֽוֹ׃
    → The first righteous person is one who fights against his enemies and also seeks to help them.
    Proverbs 18:18
      מִדְיָנִים יַשְׁבִּית הַגּוֹרָל וּבֵין עֲצוּמִים יַפְרִֽיד׃
    → From Midian will come the punishment for the wicked, and among the trees, it will be separated.
    Proverbs 18:19
      אָח נִפְשָׁע מִקִּרְיַת־עֹז וּמִדְיָנִים כִּבְרִיחַ אַרְמֽוֹן׃
    → My brother is a sinner, born of evil and wickedness; he is like a fugitive from Armon.
    Proverbs 18:20
      מִפְּרִי פִי־אִישׁ תִּשְׂבַּע בִּטְנוֹ תְּבוּאַת שְׂפָתָיו יִשְׂבָּֽע׃
    → From the fruit of a man’s mouth, his belly shall rejoice; the sound of his words shall be pleasing to him.
    Proverbs 18:21
      מָוֶת וְחַיִּים בְּיַד־לָשׁוֹן וְאֹהֲבֶיהָ יֹאכַל פִּרְיָֽהּ׃
    → Death and life are in the hands of the serpent, and her love will be consumed by her own fruit.
    Proverbs 18:22
      מָצָא אִשָּׁה מָצָא טוֹב וַיָּפֶק רָצוֹן מֵיְהוָֽה׃
    → He found a wife; he found what was good. Then he fulfilled Jehovah’s desires.
    Proverbs 18:23
      תַּחֲנוּנִים יְדַבֶּר־רָשׁ וְעָשִׁיר יַעֲנֶה עַזּֽוֹת׃
    → The rich man will answer, and the poor man will be honored.
    Proverbs 18:24
      אִישׁ רֵעִים לְהִתְרֹעֵעַ וְיֵשׁ אֹהֵב דָּבֵק מֵאָֽח׃
    → A man who is hostile to others, and there’s also someone who loves his brother dearly.
  Proverbs 18 [en]: 24 vv, 3s
    Proverbs 19:1
      טֽוֹב־רָשׁ הוֹלֵךְ בְּתֻמּוֹ מֵעִקֵּשׁ שְׂפָתָיו וְהוּא כְסִֽיל׃
    → Tov-Rash walks with his lips parted, and he is ignorant.
    Proverbs 19:2
      גַּם בְּלֹא־דַעַת נֶפֶשׁ לֹא־טוֹב וְאָץ בְּרַגְלַיִם חוֹטֵֽא׃
    → Even without knowledge of the soul, one cannot live well; their feet are also in a state of decay.
    Proverbs 19:3
      אִוֶּלֶת אָדָם תְּסַלֵּף דַּרְכּוֹ וְעַל־יְהוָה יִזְעַף לִבּֽוֹ׃
    → May man’s ways be corrected, and may his heart be filled with hatred toward Jehovah.
    Proverbs 19:4
      הוֹן יֹסִיף רֵעִים רַבִּים וְדָל מֵרֵעהוּ יִפָּרֵֽד׃
    → He will have many enemies, but he will be defeated by his enemies.
    Proverbs 19:5
      עֵד שְׁקָרִים לֹא יִנָּקֶה וְיָפִיחַ כְּזָבִים לֹא יִמָּלֵֽט׃
    → False witnesses will not be accepted; they will be treated as liars. They will not be believed at all.
    Proverbs 19:6
      רַבִּים יְחַלּוּ פְנֵֽי־נָדִיב וְכָל־הָרֵעַ לְאִישׁ מַתָּֽן׃
    → Many will turn away from the generous person, and all his enemies will give him up to someone else.
    Proverbs 19:7
      כָּל אֲחֵי־רָשׁ ׀ שְֽׂנֵאֻהוּ אַף כִּי מְרֵעֵהוּ רָחֲקוּ מִמֶּנּוּ מְרַדֵּף אֲמָרִים לוֹ־הֵֽמָּה׃
    → All those who hated Rosh, even though they were his enemies, still kept away from him. They said to him, “Where is he?”
    Proverbs 19:8
      קֹֽנֶה־לֵּב אֹהֵב נַפְשׁוֹ שֹׁמֵר תְּבוּנָה לִמְצֹא־טֽוֹב׃
    → A person with a kind heart loves those who keep their promises and strive to find what’s good.
    Proverbs 19:9
      עֵד שְׁקָרִים לֹא יִנָּקֶה וְיָפִיחַ כְּזָבִים יֹאבֵֽד׃
    → False witnesses will not be forgiven; they will be destroyed, just like lies.
    Proverbs 19:10
      לֹֽא־נָאוֶה לִכְסִיל תַּעֲנוּג אַף כִּֽי־לְעֶבֶד ׀ מְשֹׁל בְּשָׂרִֽים׃
    → Do not be pleased with fools; they will not be satisfied, even if they serve those who are wise.
    Proverbs 19:11
      שֵׂכֶל אָדָם הֶאֱרִיךְ אַפּוֹ וְתִפאַרְתּוֹ עֲבֹר עַל־פָּֽשַׁע׃
    → A person’s intelligence and pride are more important than their sins.
    Proverbs 19:12
      נַהַם כַּכְּפִיר זַעַף מֶלֶךְ וּכְטַל עַל־עֵשֶׂב רְצוֹנֽוֹ׃
    → Naham Kafir Zaeph Maelk, and he laid waste to the land they desired.
    Proverbs 19:13
      הַוֺּת לְאָבִיו בֵּן כְּסִיל וְדֶלֶף טֹרֵד מִדְיְנֵי אִשָּֽׁה׃
    → He became a son of his father, but he was foolish and worthless. He was driven away from the house of his mother.
    Proverbs 19:14
      בַּיִת וָהוֹן נַחֲלַת אָבוֹת וּמֵיְהוָה אִשָּׁה מַשְׂכָּֽלֶת׃
    → The house and the land belong to the ancestors. And from Jehovah, a woman who is wise was born.
    Proverbs 19:15
