    → He walks in purity and righteousness; his ways are pure.
    Proverbs 28:19
      עֹבֵד אַדְמָתוֹ יִֽשְׂבַּֽע־לָחֶם וּמְרַדֵּף רֵקִים יִֽשְׂבַּֽע־רִֽישׁ׃
    → He serves his land with diligence and effort; he also pursues his goals with determination.
    Proverbs 28:20
      אִישׁ אֱמוּנוֹת רַב־בְּרָכוֹת וְאָץ לְהַעֲשִׁיר לֹא יִנָּקֶֽה׃
    → May he be a man of great blessings and riches; let him not be deprived of wealth.
    Proverbs 28:21
      הַֽכֵּר־פָּנִים לֹא־טוֹב וְעַל־פַּת־לֶחֶם יִפְשַׁע־גָּֽבֶר׃
    → A person who is ugly in appearance is not good; and one who breaks the law regarding bread is also a sinner.
    Proverbs 28:22
      נִֽבֳהָל לַהוֹן אִישׁ רַע עָיִן וְלֹֽא־יֵדַע כִּי־חֶסֶר יְבֹאֶֽנּוּ׃
    → One person will be frightened and in a state of panic, and they won’t know that we are going to be missing.
    Proverbs 28:23
      מוֹכִיחַ אָדָם אַחֲרַי חֵן יִמְצָא מִֽמַּחֲלִיק לָשֽׁוֹן׃
    → May someone who follows me find grace from the Lord.
    Proverbs 28:24
      גּוֹזֵל ׀ אָבִיו וְאִמּוֹ וְאֹמֵר אֵֽין־פָּשַׁע חָבֵר הוּא לְאִישׁ מַשְׁחִֽית׃
    → He killed his father and mother, and said, “There is no sinmer who is worthy of being associated with a destroyer.”
