    → Goodness is filled in the palm of one’s hand, from the filling of hard work and evil thoughts.
    Ecclesiastes 4:7
      וְשַׁבְתִּי אֲנִי וָאֶרְאֶה הֶבֶל תַּחַת הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃
    → And I sat down and saw the darkness under the sun.
    Ecclesiastes 4:8
      יֵשׁ אֶחָד וְאֵין שֵׁנִי גַּם בֵּן וָאָח אֵֽין־לוֹ וְאֵין קֵץ לְכָל־עֲמָלוֹ גַּם־עֵינוֹ לֹא־תִשְׂבַּע עֹשֶׁר וּלְמִי ׀ אֲנִי עָמֵל וּמְחַסֵּר אֶת־נַפְשִׁי מִטּוֹבָה גַּם־זֶה הֶבֶל וְעִנְיַן רָע הֽוּא׃
    → There is only one person, and there is no second one. There is no son or brother either. There’s no end to all his efforts. His eyes also won’t rest in peace. I work hard, but I’m still deprived of true happiness. It’s all just suffering and hardship.
    Ecclesiastes 4:9
      טוֹבִים הַשְּׁנַיִם מִן־הָאֶחָד אֲשֶׁר יֵשׁ־לָהֶם שָׂכָר טוֹב בַּעֲמָלָֽם׃
    → The two who are better than the one who has a good reward for their labor.
    Ecclesiastes 4:10
      כִּי אִם־יִפֹּלוּ הָאֶחָד יָקִים אֶת־חֲבֵרוֹ וְאִילוֹ הָֽאֶחָד שֶׁיִּפּוֹל וְאֵין שֵׁנִי לַהֲקִימֽוֹ׃
    → For if one of them falls, he will build up his companion. And if the one who falls has no other to help him in building up.
    Ecclesiastes 4:11
      גַּם אִם־יִשְׁכְּבוּ שְׁנַיִם וְחַם לָהֶם וּלְאֶחָד אֵיךְ יֵחָֽם׃
    → Even if two people lie down together, and it’s hot for them, how can one of them not feel hot?
    Ecclesiastes 4:12
      וְאִֽם־יִתְקְפוֹ הָאֶחָד הַשְּׁנַיִם יַעַמְדוּ נֶגְדּוֹ וְהַחוּט הַֽמְשֻׁלָּשׁ לֹא בִמְהֵרָה יִנָּתֵֽק׃
    → And if one of them attacks, the other two will stand against him. And the three-pronged spear won’t be used quickly enough to defeat him.
    Ecclesiastes 4:13
      טוֹב יֶלֶד מִסְכֵּן וְחָכָם מִמֶּלֶךְ זָקֵן וּכְסִיל אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַע לְהִזָּהֵר עֽוֹד׃
    → A good child comes from a dangerous parent, and a wise person comes from an old and foolish king. But a fool is someone who doesn’t know how to be careful anymore.
    Ecclesiastes 4:14
      כִּֽי־מִבֵּית הָסוּרִים יָצָא לִמְלֹךְ כִּי גַּם בְּמַלְכוּתוֹ נוֹלַד רָֽשׁ׃
    → For from the house of the prisoners, a king was born. Also during his reign, a new ruler was born.
    Ecclesiastes 4:15
      רָאִיתִי אֶת־כָּל־הַחַיִּים הַֽמְהַלְּכִים תַּחַת הַשָּׁמֶשׁ עִם הַיֶּלֶד הַשֵּׁנִי אֲשֶׁר יַעֲמֹד תַּחְתָּֽיו׃
    → I saw all the living creatures moving under the sun, along with the second child who stood beneath them.
    Ecclesiastes 4:16
      אֵֽין־קֵץ לְכָל־הָעָם לְכֹל אֲשֶׁר־הָיָה לִפְנֵיהֶם גַּם הָאַחֲרוֹנִים לֹא יִשְׂמְחוּ־בוֹ כִּֽי־גַם־זֶה הֶבֶל וְרַעְיוֹן רֽוּחַ׃
    → There is no hope for all people; even those who came before them did not rejoice over it. For it is still darkness and sorrow.
    Ecclesiastes 4:17
      שְׁמֹר רַגְלְךָ כַּאֲשֶׁר תֵּלֵךְ אֶל־בֵּית הָאֱלֹהִים וְקָרוֹב לִשְׁמֹעַ מִתֵּת הַכְּסִילִים זָבַח כִּֽי־אֵינָם יוֹדְעִים לַעֲשׂוֹת רָֽע׃
    → Keep your feet steady as you go to the house of God. Do not listen to the foolish people who worship those who do not know how to do what is right.
  Ecclesiastes 4 [en]: 17 vv, 3s
    Ecclesiastes 5:1
      אַל־תְּבַהֵל עַל־פִּיךָ וְלִבְּךָ אַל־יְמַהֵר לְהוֹצִיא דָבָר לִפְנֵי הָאֱלֹהִים כִּי הָאֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַיִם וְאַתָּה עַל־הָאָרֶץ עַֽל־כֵּן יִהְיוּ דְבָרֶיךָ מְעַטִּֽים׃
    → Do not be frightened in your heart. Do not rush to say something before God. For God is in heaven, and you are on earth. Therefore, your words will be weak.
    Ecclesiastes 5:2
      כִּי בָּא הַחֲלוֹם בְּרֹב עִנְיָן וְקוֹל כְּסִיל בְּרֹב דְּבָרִֽים׃
    → For the dream came with great difficulties, and its voice was like that of a fool who said many foolish things.
    Ecclesiastes 5:3
      כַּאֲשֶׁר תִּדֹּר נֶדֶר לֵֽאלֹהִים אַל־תְּאַחֵר לְשַׁלְּמוֹ כִּי אֵין חֵפֶץ בַּכְּסִילִים אֵת אֲשֶׁר־תִּדֹּר שַׁלֵּֽם׃
    → When you seek to please God, do not focus on your own desires. For the foolish do not have any desire to please Him at all.
    Ecclesiastes 5:4
      טוֹב אֲשֶׁר לֹֽא־תִדֹּר מִשֶׁתִּדּוֹר וְלֹא תְשַׁלֵּֽם׃
    → It is good that you do not stay in one place for too long, and do not be burdened by it.
    Ecclesiastes 5:5
      אַל־תִּתֵּן אֶת־פִּיךָ לַחֲטִיא אֶת־בְּשָׂרֶךָ וְאַל־תֹּאמַר לִפְנֵי הַמַּלְאָךְ כִּי שְׁגָגָה הִיא לָמָּה יִקְצֹף הָֽאֱלֹהִים עַל־קוֹלֶךָ וְחִבֵּל אֶת־מַעֲשֵׂה יָדֶֽיךָ׃
    → Do not give in to temptation and do not speak before the priest that it is a mistake. Why should God be angry at your words and disapprove of your actions?
    Ecclesiastes 5:6
      כִּי בְרֹב חֲלֹמוֹת וַהֲבָלִים וּדְבָרִים הַרְבֵּה כִּי אֶת־הָאֱלֹהִים יְרָֽא׃
    → For in many dreams and illusions, and with many things, one still fears God.
    Ecclesiastes 5:7
      אִם־עֹשֶׁק רָשׁ וְגֵזֶל מִשְׁפָּט וָצֶדֶק תִּרְאֶה בַמְּדִינָה אַל־תִּתְמַהּ עַל־הַחֵפֶץ כִּי גָבֹהַּ מֵעַל גָּבֹהַ שֹׁמֵר וּגְבֹהִים עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃
    → If a person is unjust and deceitful, and acts in accordance with injustice and wickedness, then you will see that in that country: do not be deceived by it. For its heights are higher than those of the mountains and hills.
    Ecclesiastes 5:8
      וְיִתְרוֹן אֶרֶץ בַּכֹּל הוּא מֶלֶךְ לְשָׂדֶה נֶעֱבָֽד׃
    → And the land will be filled with all kinds of crops; it will be a land used for farming.
    Ecclesiastes 5:9
      אֹהֵב כֶּסֶף לֹא־יִשְׂבַּע כֶּסֶף וּמִֽי־אֹהֵב בֶּהָמוֹן לֹא תְבוּאָה גַּם־זֶה הָֽבֶל׃
    → He loves money, but it cannot be satisfied by money. And he doesn’t love those who are like him at all. Even then, the darkness still remains.
    Ecclesiastes 5:10
      בִּרְבוֹת הַטּוֹבָה רַבּוּ אוֹכְלֶיהָ וּמַה־כִּשְׁרוֹן לִבְעָלֶיהָ כִּי אִם־רְאוּת עֵינָֽיו׃
    → In abundance of good things, her enjoyment increases; and what is most pleasing to her husband is, indeed, what his eyes see.
    Ecclesiastes 5:11
      מְתוּקָה שְׁנַת הָעֹבֵד אִם־מְעַט וְאִם־הַרְבֵּה יֹאכֵל וְהַשָּׂבָע לֶֽעָשִׁיר אֵינֶנּוּ מַנִּיחַֽ לוֹ לִישֽׁוֹן׃
    → Whether the servant has worked hard or not, and whether he has eaten enough or not, if he has spent all his money, then it’s not right for him to be allowed to rest.
    Ecclesiastes 5:12
      יֵשׁ רָעָה חוֹלָה רָאִיתִי תַּחַת הַשָּׁמֶשׁ עֹשֶׁר שָׁמוּר לִבְעָלָיו לְרָעָתֽוֹ׃
    → I saw a disease under the sun. For a hundred nights, it afflicted its owner with illness.
    Ecclesiastes 5:13
      וְאָבַד הָעֹשֶׁר הַהוּא בְּעִנְיַן רָע וְהוֹלִיד בֵּן וְאֵין בְּיָדוֹ מְאֽוּמָה׃
    → And that hundred was lost in a bad situation. He had a son, but he didn’t have anything to give him.
    Ecclesiastes 5:14
      כַּאֲשֶׁר יָצָא מִבֶּטֶן אִמּוֹ עָרוֹם יָשׁוּב לָלֶכֶת כְּשֶׁבָּא וּמְאוּמָה לֹא־יִשָּׂא בַעֲמָלוֹ שֶׁיֹּלֵךְ בְּיָדֽוֹ׃
    → As he left his mother’s house, the evil spirit returned to him. He was afraid that he wouldn’t be able to carry the burden on his own shoulders.
    Ecclesiastes 5:15
      וְגַם־זֹה רָעָה חוֹלָה כָּל־עֻמַּת שֶׁבָּא כֵּן יֵלֵךְ וּמַה־יִּתְרוֹן לוֹ שֶֽׁיַּעֲמֹל לָרֽוּחַ׃
    → And also, this is a bad disease. It will spread throughout everything that comes into contact with it. What can be done to stop its spread?
    Ecclesiastes 5:16
      גַּם כָּל־יָמָיו בַּחֹשֶׁךְ יֹאכֵל וְכָעַס הַרְבֵּה וְחָלְיוֹ וָקָֽצֶף׃
    → And all his days he would eat in darkness; he would also get very angry, and he would suffer from illness and pain.
    Ecclesiastes 5:17
      הִנֵּה אֲשֶׁר־רָאִיתִי אָנִי טוֹב אֲשֶׁר־יָפֶה לֶֽאֶכוֹל־וְלִשְׁתּוֹת וְלִרְאוֹת טוֹבָה בְּכָל־עֲמָלוֹ ׀ שֶׁיַּעֲמֹל תַּֽחַת־הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ מִסְפַּר יְמֵי־חַיָּיו אֲשֶׁר־נָֽתַן־לוֹ הָאֱלֹהִים כִּי־הוּא חֶלְקֽוֹ׃
    → Now, since I have seen that he is good, and that he is beautiful in all his actions and looks. He works under the sun for the days of his life, which God has given him as part of his destiny.
    Ecclesiastes 5:18
      גַּם כָּֽל־הָאָדָם אֲשֶׁר נָֽתַן־לוֹ הָאֱלֹהִים עֹשֶׁר וּנְכָסִים וְהִשְׁלִיטוֹ לֶאֱכֹל מִמֶּנּוּ וְלָשֵׂאת אֶת־חֶלְקוֹ וְלִשְׂמֹחַ בַּעֲמָלוֹ זֹה מַתַּת אֱלֹהִים הִֽיא׃
    → And all those people who were given wealth and possessions by God, and who were allowed to eat from it, to take their share, and to rejoice in their labor… these people also died as a punishment from God.
    Ecclesiastes 5:19
      כִּי לֹא הַרְבֵּה יִזְכֹּר אֶת־יְמֵי חַיָּיו כִּי הָאֱלֹהִים מַעֲנֶה בְּשִׂמְחַת לִבּֽוֹ׃
    → For he doesn’t remember his own days very much, because God delights in him.
  Ecclesiastes 5 [en]: 19 vv, 3s
    Ecclesiastes 6:1
      יֵשׁ רָעָה אֲשֶׁר רָאִיתִי תַּחַת הַשָּׁמֶשׁ וְרַבָּה הִיא עַל־הָאָדָֽם׃
    → There is a evil that I have seen under the sun; it is very severe upon people.
    Ecclesiastes 6:2
      אִישׁ אֲשֶׁר יִתֶּן־לוֹ הָאֱלֹהִים עֹשֶׁר וּנְכָסִים וְכָבוֹד וְֽאֵינֶנּוּ חָסֵר לְנַפְשׁוֹ ׀ מִכֹּל אֲשֶׁר־יִתְאַוֶּה וְלֹֽא־יַשְׁלִיטֶנּוּ הָֽאֱלֹהִים לֶאֱכֹל מִמֶּנּוּ כִּי אִישׁ נָכְרִי יֹֽאכֲלֶנּוּ זֶה הֶבֶל וָחֳלִי רָע הֽוּא׃
    → A man who is given by God wealth, possessions, and honor… yet he isn’t satisfied with all this. God doesn’t allow him to eat from these things. For a common person will surely eat him up; he’ll be consumed by hunger and disease.
    Ecclesiastes 6:3
      אִם־יוֹלִיד אִישׁ מֵאָה וְשָׁנִים רַבּוֹת יִֽחְיֶה וְרַב ׀ שֶׁיִּהְיוּ יְמֵֽי־שָׁנָיו וְנַפְשׁוֹ לֹא־תִשְׂבַּע מִן־הַטּוֹבָה וְגַם־קְבוּרָה לֹא־הָיְתָה לּוֹ אָמַרְתִּי טוֹב מִמֶּנּוּ הַנָּֽפֶל׃
    → If a man lives for a hundred years or more, and his years become longer, yet his soul does not grow more virtuous, and he also lacks wisdom, then I say that he is worse off than those who die young.
    Ecclesiastes 6:4
      כִּֽי־בַהֶבֶל בָּא וּבַחֹשֶׁךְ יֵלֵךְ וּבַחֹשֶׁךְ שְׁמוֹ יְכֻסֶּֽה׃
    → For darkness will come, and in the darkness it will go; and in the darkness its name will be forgotten.
    Ecclesiastes 6:5
      גַּם־שֶׁמֶשׁ לֹא־רָאָה וְלֹא יָדָע נַחַת לָזֶה מִזֶּֽה׃
    → Even the sun cannot see or know about this. It’s beyond his understanding.
    Ecclesiastes 6:6
      וְאִלּוּ חָיָה אֶלֶף שָׁנִים פַּעֲמַיִם וְטוֹבָה לֹא רָאָה הֲלֹא אֶל־מָקוֹם אֶחָד הַכֹּל הוֹלֵֽךְ׃
    → And if he lived a thousand years, and still never saw even one single place where everything would be in order.
    Ecclesiastes 6:7
      כָּל־עֲמַל הָאָדָם לְפִיהוּ וְגַם־הַנֶּפֶשׁ לֹא תִמָּלֵֽא׃
    → All the man’s efforts are in vain; even his soul will not be satisfied.
    Ecclesiastes 6:8
      כִּי מַה־יּוֹתֵר לֶחָכָם מִֽן־הַכְּסִיל מַה־לֶּעָנִי יוֹדֵעַ לַהֲלֹךְ נֶגֶד הַחַיִּֽים׃
    → For what can be better for a wise man than the foolish? What can be better for a poor man than knowing how to walk in the direction of life?
    Ecclesiastes 6:9
      טוֹב מַרְאֵה עֵינַיִם מֵֽהֲלָךְ־נָפֶשׁ גַּם־זֶה הֶבֶל וּרְעוּת רֽוּחַ׃
    → Good looks is pleasing to the eyes, but it also brings sorrow and evil thoughts.
    Ecclesiastes 6:10
      מַה־שֶּֽׁהָיָה כְּבָר נִקְרָא שְׁמוֹ וְנוֹדָע אֲשֶׁר־הוּא אָדָם וְלֹא־יוּכַל לָדִין עִם שֶׁתַּקִּיף מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃
    → What would have happened long ago if his name had been known, and people knew who he was? Then he wouldn’t have been able to do anything against us.
    Ecclesiastes 6:11
      כִּי יֵשׁ־דְּבָרִים הַרְבֵּה מַרְבִּים הָבֶל מַה־יֹּתֵר לָאָדָֽם׃
    → For there are many things that are far too difficult for a person to understand.
    Ecclesiastes 6:12
      כִּי מִֽי־יוֹדֵעַ מַה־טּוֹב לָֽאָדָם בַּֽחַיִּים מִסְפַּר יְמֵי־חַיֵּי הֶבְלוֹ וְיַעֲשֵׂם כַּצֵּל אֲשֶׁר מִֽי־יַגִּיד לָֽאָדָם מַה־יִּהְיֶה אַחֲרָיו תַּחַת הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃
    → For who can know what is good for a person during the days of their life? They will do things that are like a shadow—something that no one can predict what will happen to them under the sun.
  Ecclesiastes 6 [en]: 12 vv, 2s
    Ecclesiastes 7:1
      טוֹב שֵׁם מִשֶּׁמֶן טוֹב וְיוֹם הַמָּוֶת מִיּוֹם הִוָּלְדֽוֹ׃
    → A good name is better than bad. And the day of death is worse than the day of birth.
    Ecclesiastes 7:2
      טוֹב לָלֶכֶת אֶל־בֵּֽית־אֵבֶל מִלֶּכֶת אֶל־בֵּית מִשְׁתֶּה בַּאֲשֶׁר הוּא סוֹף כָּל־הָאָדָם וְהַחַי יִתֵּן אֶל־לִבּֽוֹ׃
    → It’s better to go to the house of sorrow than to the house of drinking, when that is the end of all people. And life will be given to their hearts.
    Ecclesiastes 7:3
      טוֹב כַּעַס מִשְּׂחֹק כִּֽי־בְרֹעַ פָּנִים יִיטַב לֵֽב׃
    → It’s better to get angry from playing games, rather than having a good relationship with others. It’s better for the heart to be happy.
    Ecclesiastes 7:4
      לֵב חֲכָמִים בְּבֵית אֵבֶל וְלֵב כְּסִילִים בְּבֵית שִׂמְחָֽה׃
    → The hearts of the wise are in the house of mourning, while the hearts of the foolish are in the house of joy.
    Ecclesiastes 7:5
      טוֹב לִשְׁמֹעַ גַּעֲרַת חָכָם מֵאִישׁ שֹׁמֵעַ שִׁיר כְּסִילִֽים׃
    → It is good to hear the complaints of a wise man from someone who only hears the songs of fools.
    Ecclesiastes 7:6
      כִּי כְקוֹל הַסִּירִים תַּחַת הַסִּיר כֵּן שְׂחֹק הַכְּסִיל וְגַם־זֶה הָֽבֶל׃
    → For just as the noise of those who are under the yoke is heard beneath it, so too does the foolish person laugh. And that is also a form of gloom.
    Ecclesiastes 7:7
      כִּי הָעֹשֶׁק יְהוֹלֵל חָכָם וִֽיאַבֵּד אֶת־לֵב מַתָּנָֽה׃
    → For the blind one will praise the wise, and he will destroy the heart of those who are foolish.
    Ecclesiastes 7:8
      טוֹב אַחֲרִית דָּבָר מֵֽרֵאשִׁיתוֹ טוֹב אֶֽרֶךְ־רוּחַ מִגְּבַהּ־רֽוּחַ׃
    → Good is that which comes from its beginning; good is something that lasts forever.
    Ecclesiastes 7:9
      אַל־תְּבַהֵל בְּרֽוּחֲךָ לִכְעוֹס כִּי כַעַס בְּחֵיק כְּסִילִים יָנֽוּחַ׃
    → Do not be upset in your heart, for anger is like a nest of fools.
    Ecclesiastes 7:10
      אַל־תֹּאמַר מֶה הָיָה שֶׁהַיָּמִים הָרִאשֹׁנִים הָיוּ טוֹבִים מֵאֵלֶּה כִּי לֹא מֵחָכְמָה שָׁאַלְתָּ עַל־זֶֽה׃
    → Don’t say that the days in the past were better than these. It’s not wise of you to ask about them.
    Ecclesiastes 7:11
      טוֹבָה חָכְמָה עִֽם־נַחֲלָה וְיֹתֵר לְרֹאֵי הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃
    → Goodness is wisdom, along with a generous heart; it is also more pleasing to those who see the heavens.
    Ecclesiastes 7:12
      כִּי בְּצֵל הַֽחָכְמָה בְּצֵל הַכָּסֶף וְיִתְרוֹן דַּעַת הַֽחָכְמָה תְּחַיֶּה בְעָלֶֽיהָ׃
    → For in the shadow of wisdom, in the shadow of gold, and as wisdom’s knowledge increases, so does its life.
