    → Also, I saw wisdom under the sun. It was truly great.
    Ecclesiastes 9:14
      עִיר קְטַנָּה וַאֲנָשִׁים בָּהּ מְעָט וּבָֽא־אֵלֶיהָ מֶלֶךְ גָּדוֹל וְסָבַב אֹתָהּ וּבָנָה עָלֶיהָ מְצוֹדִים גְּדֹלִֽים׃
    → It’s a small city, and there are only a few people living there. There’s a great king who rules over it. He built magnificent walls around the city.
    Ecclesiastes 9:15
      וּמָצָא בָהּ אִישׁ מִסְכֵּן חָכָם וּמִלַּט־הוּא אֶת־הָעִיר בְּחָכְמָתוֹ וְאָדָם לֹא זָכַר אֶת־הָאִישׁ הַמִּסְכֵּן הַהּֽוּא׃
    → And he found in her a wise and intelligent man. He ruled the city with his wisdom. No one remembered the wise man who had saved the city.
    Ecclesiastes 9:16
      וְאָמַרְתִּי אָנִי טוֹבָה חָכְמָה מִגְּבוּרָה וְחָכְמַת הַמִּסְכֵּן בְּזוּיָה וּדְבָרָיו אֵינָם נִשְׁמָעִֽים׃
    → And I said, “I am good and wise from a great distance. My wisdom is beyond measure, and my words are not heard.”
    Ecclesiastes 9:17
      דִּבְרֵי חֲכָמִים בְּנַחַת נִשְׁמָעִים מִזַּעֲקַת מוֹשֵׁל בַּכְּסִילִֽים׃
    → The words of the wise are heard with respect, out of the cries of those who are foolish.
    Ecclesiastes 9:18
      טוֹבָה חָכְמָה מִכְּלֵי קְרָב וְחוֹטֶא אֶחָד יְאַבֵּד טוֹבָה הַרְבֵּֽה׃
    → Better is wisdom than all kinds of sacrifices and evil deeds. One evil act destroys much good.
  Ecclesiastes 9 [en]: 18 vv, 3s
    Ecclesiastes 10:1
      זְבוּבֵי מָוֶת יַבְאִישׁ יַבִּיעַ שֶׁמֶן רוֹקֵחַ יָקָר מֵחָכְמָה מִכָּבוֹד סִכְלוּת מְעָֽט׃
    → The dead birds bring forth the scent of wisdom; they reveal something precious from the depths of intelligence. But it’s also a sign of foolishness.
    Ecclesiastes 10:2
