    → A wise heart is our strength, while a foolish heart leads us astray.
    Ecclesiastes 10:3
      וְגַם־בַּדֶּרֶךְ כְּשֶׁסָּכָל הֹלֵךְ לִבּוֹ חָסֵר וְאָמַר לַכֹּל סָכָל הֽוּא׃
    → And also, in the same way that a fool walks around with empty hands, and says to everyone, “He’s a fool.”
    Ecclesiastes 10:4
      אִם־רוּחַ הַמּוֹשֵׁל תַּעֲלֶה עָלֶיךָ מְקוֹמְךָ אַל־תַּנַּח כִּי מַרְפֵּא יַנִּיחַ חֲטָאִים גְּדוֹלִֽים׃
    → If the Spirit of healing rises up from your place, do not be discouraged. For the one who heals will also forgive great sins.
    Ecclesiastes 10:5
      יֵשׁ רָעָה רָאִיתִי תַּחַת הַשָּׁמֶשׁ כִּשְׁגָגָה שֶׁיֹּצָא מִלִּפְנֵי הַשַּׁלִּֽיט׃
    → I saw a light under the sky, as if it were a mirage that came from before the sun.
    Ecclesiastes 10:6
      נִתַּן הַסֶּכֶל בַּמְּרוֹמִים רַבִּים וַעֲשִׁירִים בַּשֵּׁפֶל יֵשֵֽׁבוּ׃
    → He gave knowledge in many ways; and those who are rich and powerful sat down in poverty.
    Ecclesiastes 10:7
      רָאִיתִי עֲבָדִים עַל־סוּסִים וְשָׂרִים הֹלְכִים כַּעֲבָדִים עַל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → I saw servants riding on horses and camels, going about as if they were servants on the earth.
    Ecclesiastes 10:8
      חֹפֵר גּוּמָּץ בּוֹ יִפּוֹל וּפֹרֵץ גָּדֵר יִשְּׁכֶנּוּ נָחָֽשׁ׃
    → The serpent digs holes in it; the scorpion and other reptiles also live there.
    Ecclesiastes 10:9
      מַסִּיעַ אֲבָנִים יֵעָצֵב בָּהֶם בּוֹקֵעַ עֵצִים יִסָּכֶן בָּֽם׃
    → He carries stones, which can be used to block paths; he cuts down trees, which can be used to harm others.
    Ecclesiastes 10:10
