      גַּם מִגָּבֹהַּ יִרָאוּ וְחַתְחַתִּים בַּדֶּרֶךְ וְיָנֵאץ הַשָּׁקֵד וְיִסְתַּבֵּל הֶֽחָגָב וְתָפֵר הָֽאֲבִיּוֹנָה כִּֽי־הֹלֵךְ הָאָדָם אֶל־בֵּית עוֹלָמוֹ וְסָבְבוּ בָשּׁוּק הַסֹּפְדִֽים׃
    → Also, from above, they will be seen and heard along the way. The seeds will be scattered, and the fruits will fall like ripe fruits. As people go back home, they will be surrounded by the fields of thorns.
    Ecclesiastes 12:6
      עַד אֲשֶׁר לֹֽא־יֵרָתֵק חֶבֶל הַכֶּסֶף וְתָרֻץ גֻּלַּת הַזָּהָב וְתִשָּׁבֶר כַּד עַל־הַמַּבּוּעַ וְנָרֹץ הַגַּלְגַּל אֶל־הַבּֽוֹר׃
    → Until the chain of gold is not tightened, and the gold floor remains loose. Then it will be fixed on its place, and the ring will be broken into pieces.
    Ecclesiastes 12:7
      וְיָשֹׁב הֶעָפָר עַל־הָאָרֶץ כְּשֶׁהָיָה וְהָרוּחַ תָּשׁוּב אֶל־הָאֱלֹהִים אֲשֶׁר נְתָנָֽהּ׃
    → And the sun will stand on the earth, just as it was before. And the wind will return to God who has given it to us.
    Ecclesiastes 12:8
      הֲבֵל הֲבָלִים אָמַר הַקּוֹהֶלֶת הַכֹּל הָֽבֶל׃
    → “Wastefulness and foolishness,” said the prophet. “All is wastefulness.”
    Ecclesiastes 12:9
      וְיֹתֵר שֶׁהָיָה קֹהֶלֶת חָכָם עוֹד לִמַּד־דַּעַת אֶת־הָעָם וְאִזֵּן וְחִקֵּר תִּקֵּן מְשָׁלִים הַרְבֵּֽה׃
    → And those who remained wise would still strive to understand the teachings of God. They would also observe and study the laws and regulations that govern human behavior.
    Ecclesiastes 12:10
      בִּקֵּשׁ קֹהֶלֶת לִמְצֹא דִּבְרֵי־חֵפֶץ וְכָתוּב יֹשֶׁר דִּבְרֵי אֱמֶֽת׃
    → I seek a congregation that can find words of truth, and let those who write down such words be recognized as true believers.
    Ecclesiastes 12:11
      דִּבְרֵי חֲכָמִים כַּדָּרְבֹנוֹת וּֽכְמַשְׂמְרוֹת נְטוּעִים בַּעֲלֵי אֲסֻפּוֹת נִתְּנוּ מֵרֹעֶה אֶחָֽד׃
    → The words of the wise men, as they were taught and preserved, were given to us by one who was wise.
    Ecclesiastes 12:12
      וְיֹתֵר מֵהֵמָּה בְּנִי הִזָּהֵר עֲשׂוֹת סְפָרִים הַרְבֵּה אֵין קֵץ וְלַהַג הַרְבֵּה יְגִעַת בָּשָֽׂר׃
    → And from those who are like them, my children, beware! They make many records. There’s no end to them. And their efforts will surely lead to failure.
    Ecclesiastes 12:13
      סוֹף דָּבָר הַכֹּל נִשְׁמָע אֶת־הָאֱלֹהִים יְרָא וְאֶת־מִצְוֺתָיו שְׁמוֹר כִּי־זֶה כָּל־הָאָדָֽם׃
    → At last, all these words were heard. Man feared God and obeyed His commands, for that is what every human being should do.
    Ecclesiastes 12:14
      כִּי אֶת־כָּל־מַֽעֲשֶׂה הָאֱלֹהִים יָבִא בְמִשְׁפָּט עַל כָּל־נֶעְלָם אִם־טוֹב וְאִם־רָֽע׃
    → For all that God does, He does it in accordance with justice, whether it is good or bad.
  Ecclesiastes 12 [en]: 14 vv, 2s
    Song of Songs 1:1
