    → And they fell as victims in the land, like wild animals and pests in its corners.
    Jeremiah 51:5
      כִּי לֹֽא־אַלְמָן יִשְׂרָאֵל וִֽיהוּדָה מֵֽאֱלֹהָיו מֵֽיְהוָה צְבָאוֹת כִּי אַרְצָם מָלְאָה אָשָׁם מִקְּדוֹשׁ יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃
    → For Israel and Judah have not obeyed their God, the Lord of hosts. Their land is filled with sins, because Israel has violated the laws of God.
    Jeremiah 51:6
      נֻסוּ ׀ מִתּוֹךְ בָּבֶל וּמַלְּטוּ אִישׁ נַפְשׁוֹ אַל־תִּדַּמּוּ בַּעֲוֺנָהּ כִּי עֵת נְקָמָה הִיא לַֽיהוָה גְּמוּל הוּא מְשַׁלֵּם לָֽהּ׃
    → They were rescued from Babylon. One man’s soul was saved from destruction. It shouldn’t be destroyed in the flames of war, for it is a time of vengeance for God. He will reward those who are worthy.
    Jeremiah 51:7
      כּוֹס־זָהָב בָּבֶל בְּיַד־יְהוָה מְשַׁכֶּרֶת כָּל־הָאָרֶץ מִיֵּינָהּ שָׁתוּ גוֹיִם עַל־כֵּן יִתְהֹלְלוּ גוֹיִֽם׃
    → A golden crown in Babylon, held by Jehovah. It commands all the earth. Because of it, nations will praise Him.
    Jeremiah 51:8
      פִּתְאֹם נָפְלָה בָבֶל וַתִּשָּׁבֵר הֵילִילוּ עָלֶיהָ קְחוּ צֳרִי לְמַכְאוֹבָהּ אוּלַי תֵּרָפֵֽא׃
    → Suddenly, Babel fell down. Her hair was torn apart. They took her clothes to wear as a shroud for her burial. But I will still be saved.
    Jeremiah 51:9
      רִפִּינוּ אֶת־בָּבֶל וְלֹא נִרְפָּתָה עִזְבוּהָ וְנֵלֵךְ אִישׁ לְאַרְצוֹ כִּֽי־נָגַע אֶל־הַשָּׁמַיִם מִשְׁפָּטָהּ וְנִשָּׂא עַד־שְׁחָקִֽים׃
    → We will destroy Babylon, and it will not be able to resist us. Then each person will go back to his own land. We will reach the heavens through judgment, and then we will be carried away to Shekhim.
    Jeremiah 51:10
      הוֹצִיא יְהוָה אֶת־צִדְקֹתֵינוּ בֹּאוּ וּנְסַפְּרָה בְצִיּוֹן אֶֽת־מַעֲשֵׂה יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃
    → May Jehovah bring forth our righteousnesses, so that they may be recorded in the books of heaven regarding the deeds of Jehovah, our God.
    Jeremiah 51:11
      הָבֵרוּ הַחִצִּים מִלְאוּ הַשְּׁלָטִים הֵעִיר יְהוָה אֶת־רוּחַ מַלְכֵי מָדַי כִּֽי־עַל־בָּבֶל מְזִמָּתוֹ לְהַשְׁחִיתָהּ כִּֽי־נִקְמַת יְהוָה הִיא נִקְמַת הֵיכָלֽוֹ׃
    → Let the gates be closed; let the rulers be filled with power. May Jehovah send a spirit from heaven upon the kings of Media, just as He did upon Babylon. This is an act of vengeance by Jehovah. It is a retribution for their sins.
    Jeremiah 51:12
      אֶל־חוֹמֹת בָּבֶל שְׂאוּ־נֵס הַחֲזִיקוּ הַמִּשְׁמָר הָקִימוּ שֹֽׁמְרִים הָכִינוּ הָאֹֽרְבִים כִּי גַּם־זָמַם יְהוָה גַּם־עָשָׂה אֵת אֲשֶׁר־דִּבֶּר אֶל־יֹשְׁבֵי בָבֶֽל׃
    → To the people of Babylon, Shau-Nes took hold of the throne. They established guards and prepared for battle. For they also knew that Jehovah would do as He had spoken to the rulers of Babylon.
    Jeremiah 51:13
      שֹׁכַנְתְּ עַל־מַיִם רַבִּים רַבַּת אֽוֹצָרֹת בָּא קִצֵּךְ אַמַּת בִּצְעֵֽךְ׃
    → You have dwelt on many waters; your wealth is great. But in the end, it will all be destroyed.
    Jeremiah 51:14
      נִשְׁבַּע יְהוָה צְבָאוֹת בְּנַפְשׁוֹ כִּי אִם־מִלֵּאתִיךְ אָדָם כַּיֶּלֶק וְעָנוּ עָלַיִךְ הֵידָֽד׃
    → May the Lord, in His glory, bless you with His power. For you have been filled with greatness, and people have turned to you for help.
    Jeremiah 51:15
      עֹשֵׂה אֶרֶץ בְּכֹחוֹ מֵכִין תֵּבֵל בְּחָכְמָתוֹ וּבִתְבוּנָתוֹ נָטָה שָׁמָֽיִם׃
    → He creates the earth with His power; He prepares the sea with His wisdom and planning. He turns the heavens towards Him.
    Jeremiah 51:16
      לְקוֹל תִּתּוֹ הֲמוֹן מַיִם בַּשָּׁמַיִם וַיַּעַל נְשִׂאִים מִקְצֵה־אָרֶץ בְּרָקִים לַמָּטָר עָשָׂה וַיֹּצֵא רוּחַ מֵאֹצְרֹתָֽיו׃
    → To the sound of his voice, the waters rose from the heavens. They rose from the edges of the earth in clouds, towards the sky. A wind was sent forth from his treasures.
    Jeremiah 51:17
      נִבְעַר כָּל־אָדָם מִדַּעַת הֹבִישׁ כָּל־צֹרֵף מִפָּסֶל כִּי שֶׁקֶר נִסְכּוֹ וְלֹא־רוּחַ בָּֽם׃
    → Everyone is ashamed of the knowledge of falsehood. Every person is disgusted by those who are deceitful. For they are full of lies, and have no true spirit at all.
    Jeremiah 51:18
      הֶבֶל הֵמָּה מַעֲשֵׂה תַּעְתֻּעִים בְּעֵת פְּקֻדָּתָם יֹאבֵֽדוּ׃
    → The wicked will be destroyed when they are punished. They will be consumed.
    Jeremiah 51:19
      לֹֽא־כְאֵלֶּה חֵלֶק יַעֲקוֹב כִּֽי־יוֹצֵר הַכֹּל הוּא וְשֵׁבֶט נַחֲלָתוֹ יְהוָה צְבָאוֹת שְׁמֽוֹ׃
    → It is not Jacob’s share that these things belong to him. He is the one who created everything. His inheritance belongs to Jehovah, the Almighty God.
    Jeremiah 51:20
      מַפֵּץ־אַתָּה לִי כְּלֵי מִלְחָמָה וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ גּוֹיִם וְהִשְׁחַתִּי בְךָ מַמְלָכֽוֹת׃
    → You have brought me all kinds of troubles in battle. I will be destroyed by you, and nations will be destroyed by you as well.
    Jeremiah 51:21
      וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ סוּס וְרֹֽכְבוֹ וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ רֶכֶב וְרֹכְבֽוֹ׃
    → And I will be broken in you, along with your horse and its rider. I will be destroyed in you, along with your chariot and its rider.
    Jeremiah 51:22
      וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ אִישׁ וְאִשָּׁה וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ זָקֵן וָנָעַר וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ בָּחוּר וּבְתוּלָֽה׃
    → And I will be destroyed in you, both man and woman. I will be destroyed in you, both the old and the young. I will be destroyed in you, both the married and the unmarried.
    Jeremiah 51:23
      וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ רֹעֶה וְעֶדְרוֹ וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ אִכָּר וְצִמְדּוֹ וְנִפַּצְתִּי בְךָ פַּחוֹת וּסְגָנִֽים׃
    → And I will be destroyed by you, both in body and soul. I will also be destroyed by you, along with all my possessions and treasures.
    Jeremiah 51:24
      וְשִׁלַּמְתִּי לְבָבֶל וּלְכֹל ׀ יוֹשְׁבֵי כַשְׂדִּים אֵת כָּל־רָעָתָם אֲשֶׁר־עָשׂוּ בְצִיּוֹן לְעֵֽינֵיכֶם נְאֻם יְהוָֽה׃
    → And I have destroyed Babylon and all those who dwell in Kashdim. I have punished them for all their evil deeds they committed against you, O LORD.
    Jeremiah 51:25
      הִנְנִי אֵלֶיךָ הַר הַמַּשְׁחִית נְאֻם־יְהוָה הַמַּשְׁחִית אֶת־כָּל־הָאָרֶץ וְנָטִיתִי אֶת־יָדִי עָלֶיךָ וְגִלְגַּלְתִּיךָ מִן־הַסְּלָעִים וּנְתַתִּיךָ לְהַר שְׂרֵפָֽה׃
    → I am your God, the destroyer. May Jehovah, the destroyer, destroy all the land. I will raise my hand over you, and you will be thrown down from the rocks. I will throw you into the burning mountain.
    Jeremiah 51:26
      וְלֹֽא־יִקְחוּ מִמְּךָ אֶבֶן לְפִנָּה וְאֶבֶן לְמֽוֹסָדוֹת כִּֽי־שִׁמְמוֹת עוֹלָם תִּֽהְיֶה נְאֻם־יְהוָֽה׃
    → And they shall not take any stones from you for foundations, for the foundations of the house will be eternal, says Jehovah.
    Jeremiah 51:27
      שְׂאוּ־נֵס בָּאָרֶץ תִּקְעוּ שׁוֹפָר בַּגּוֹיִם קַדְּשׁוּ עָלֶיהָ גּוֹיִם הַשְׁמִיעוּ עָלֶיהָ מַמְלְכוֹת אֲרָרַט מִנִּי וְאַשְׁכְּנָז פִּקְדוּ עָלֶיהָ טִפְסָר הַֽעֲלוּ־סוּס כְּיֶלֶק סָמָֽר׃
    → Shu-Nes came to this land. They set up altars in various nations. Nations listened to him. Kings of Aram and Ashkenaz worshipped him. Tefsar, the rider on the horse, was also there.
    Jeremiah 51:28
      קַדְּשׁוּ עָלֶיהָ גוֹיִם אֶת־מַלְכֵי מָדַי אֶת־פַּחוֹתֶיהָ וְאֶת־כָּל־סְגָנֶיהָ וְאֵת כָּל־אֶרֶץ מֶמְשַׁלְתּֽוֹ׃
    → Nations sanctified her; they honored the kings of Madai, their treasures, and all their possessions. They also ruled over all the lands under their control.
    Jeremiah 51:29
      וַתִּרְעַשׁ הָאָרֶץ וַתָּחֹל כִּי קָמָה עַל־בָּבֶל מַחְשְׁבוֹת יְהוָה לָשׂוּם אֶת־אֶרֶץ בָּבֶל לְשַׁמָּה מֵאֵין יוֹשֵֽׁב׃
    → The earth trembled and shook, because the thoughts of the LORD had been fulfilled: the land of Babylon was given over to chaos, with no one living there anymore.
    Jeremiah 51:30
      חָדְלוּ גִבּוֹרֵי בָבֶל לְהִלָּחֵם יָֽשְׁבוּ בַּמְּצָדוֹת נָשְׁתָה גְבוּרָתָם הָיוּ לְנָשִׁים הִצִּיתוּ מִשְׁכְּנֹתֶיהָ נִשְׁבְּרוּ בְרִיחֶֽיהָ׃
    → The rulers of Babylon stopped fighting. They sat down in their places. Their power became like that of women. They lit fires from their homes, and their smoke filled the air.
    Jeremiah 51:31
      רָץ לִקְרַאת־רָץ יָרוּץ וּמַגִּיד לִקְרַאת מַגִּיד לְהַגִּיד לְמֶלֶךְ בָּבֶל כִּֽי־נִלְכְּדָה עִירוֹ מִקָּצֶֽה׃
    → He ran to shout out his news. He told the king of Babylon that his city had been captured from him.
    Jeremiah 51:32
      וְהַמַּעְבָּרוֹת נִתְפָּשׂוּ וְאֶת־הָאֲגַמִּים שָׂרְפוּ בָאֵשׁ וְאַנְשֵׁי הַמִּלְחָמָה נִבְהָֽלוּ׃
    → And those who were captured were taken captive, and the trenches were burned with fire. The soldiers were terrified.
    Jeremiah 51:33
      כִּי כֹה אָמַר יְהוָה צְבָאוֹת אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בַּת־בָּבֶל כְּגֹרֶן עֵת הִדְרִיכָהּ עוֹד מְעַט וּבָאָה עֵֽת־הַקָּצִיר לָֽהּ׃
    → For as Jehovah, the army of Israel’s God, said in Babylon: “At the time of planting, it still remains in a state of growth; but when the time comes for harvesting, it is ready.”
    Jeremiah 51:34
      אֲכָלַנִי הֲמָמַנִי נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּר מֶלֶךְ בָּבֶל הִצִּיגַנִי כְּלִי רִיק בְּלָעַנִי כַּתַּנִּין מִלָּא כְרֵשׂוֹ מֵֽעֲדָנָי הֱדִיחָֽנִי׃
    → The king of Babylon, Nabuchadrezzar, ate me. He made me look like a hollow body; my stomach was full of worms. He devoured me from within.
    Jeremiah 51:35
      חֲמָסִי וּשְׁאֵרִי עַל־בָּבֶל תֹּאמַר יֹשֶׁבֶת צִיּוֹן וְדָמִי אֶל־יֹשְׁבֵי כַשְׂדִּים תֹּאמַר יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃
    → Hamasi and Sheri will say in Babylon, “You who rule over Zion, my blood will flow to those who rule over the cities.” They will also say, “Jerusalem!”
    Jeremiah 51:36
      לָכֵן כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה הִנְנִי־רָב אֶת־רִיבֵךְ וְנִקַּמְתִּי אֶת־נִקְמָתֵךְ וְהַחֲרַבְתִּי אֶת־יַמָּהּ וְהֹבַשְׁתִּי אֶת־מְקוֹרָֽהּ׃
    → Therefore, thus said Jehovah: “I will avenge your injuries. I will take revenge for your grievances. I will destroy her sea, and I will destroy her land.”
    Jeremiah 51:37
      וְהָיְתָה בָבֶל ׀ לְגַלִּים ׀ מְעוֹן־תַּנִּים שַׁמָּה וּשְׁרֵקָה מֵאֵין יוֹשֵֽׁב׃
    → And Babylon would become a place of chaos and destruction, with no one who could rule or govern it.
    Jeremiah 51:38
      יַחְדָּו כַּכְּפִרִים יִשְׁאָגוּ נָעֲרוּ כְּגוֹרֵי אֲרָיֽוֹת׃
    → Together, like wild beasts, they were driven away, like young animals in the wilderness.
    Jeremiah 51:39
      בְּחֻמָּם אָשִׁית אֶת־מִשְׁתֵּיהֶם וְהִשְׁכַּרְתִּים לְמַעַן יַעֲלֹזוּ וְיָשְׁנוּ שְׁנַת־עוֹלָם וְלֹא יָקִיצוּ נְאֻם יְהוָֽה׃
    → In their midst, I will destroy them; I will make them serve as a punishment for their sins. They will be destroyed forever, and they will never rise again. May the Lord have mercy on them.
    Jeremiah 51:40
      אֽוֹרִידֵם כְּכָרִים לִטְבוֹחַ כְּאֵילִים עִם־עַתּוּדִֽים׃
    → They were like cattle that were slaughtered, like sheep with their horns cut off.
    Jeremiah 51:41
      אֵיךְ נִלְכְּדָה שֵׁשַׁךְ וַתִּתָּפֵשׂ תְּהִלַּת כָּל־הָאָרֶץ אֵיךְ הָיְתָה לְשַׁמָּה בָּבֶל בַּגּוֹיִֽם׃
    → How was Shechem captured and its song destroyed? How did Samah Babel’s people end up in those lands?
    Jeremiah 51:42
      עָלָה עַל־בָּבֶל הַיָּם בַּהֲמוֹן גַּלָּיו נִכְסָֽתָה׃
    → The sea rose over Babylon in the stormy waves.
    Jeremiah 51:43
      הָיוּ עָרֶיהָ לְשַׁמָּה אֶרֶץ צִיָּה וַעֲרָבָה אֶרֶץ לֹֽא־יֵשֵׁב בָּהֵן כָּל־אִישׁ וְלֹֽא־יַעֲבֹר בָּהֵן בֶּן־אָדָֽם׃
    → Its cities were like ruins of land that had been destroyed. It was a land where no man could live, and no child could walk through it.
