    → They had enemies who were stronger than them. But Jehovah would judge them for their many sins. They were forced to submit to their enemies’ rule.
    Lamentations 1:6
      וַיֵּצֵא־מִבַּת־צִיּוֹן כָּל־הֲדָרָהּ הָיוּ שָׂרֶיהָ כְּאַיָּלִים לֹא־מָצְאוּ מִרְעֶה וַיֵּלְכוּ בְלֹא־כֹחַ לִפְנֵי רוֹדֵֽף׃
    → And from the house of Zion, all their land was covered with snow. They had no place to rest or sleep. They walked without any strength in front of the enemy.
    Lamentations 1:7
