    → Jerusalem committed a sin. As a result, all its treasures were lost. They saw its ugliness, and even she sighed and returned home.
    Lamentations 1:9
      טֻמְאָתָהּ בְּשׁוּלֶיהָ לֹא זָֽכְרָה אַחֲרִיתָהּ וַתֵּרֶד פְּלָאִים אֵין מְנַחֵם לָהּ רְאֵה יְהוָה אֶת־עָנְיִי כִּי הִגְדִּיל אוֹיֵֽב׃
    → She forgot her past in her sorrow; she went down into the depths of despair. There’s no comfort for her. Look, God, at my suffering! How great is my wretchedness!
    Lamentations 1:10
      יָדוֹ פָּרַשׂ צָר עַל כָּל־מַחֲמַדֶּיהָ כִּֽי־רָאֲתָה גוֹיִם בָּאוּ מִקְדָּשָׁהּ אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתָה לֹא־יָבֹאוּ בַקָּהָל לָֽךְ׃
    → Her hand spread a curse over all her offerings, because she saw nations coming from the holy place. She had ordered that they should not enter the temple.
