      לוֹא אֲלֵיכֶם כָּל־עֹבְרֵי דֶרֶךְ הַבִּיטוּ וּרְאוּ אִם־יֵשׁ מַכְאוֹב כְּמַכְאֹבִי אֲשֶׁר עוֹלַל לִי אֲשֶׁר הוֹגָה יְהוָה בְּיוֹם חֲרוֹן אַפּֽוֹ׃
    → If not for all the hardships along the way, may you see and understand whether there is any sorrow like mine. This sorrow was brought upon me by Jehovah on that day of judgment.
    Lamentations 1:13
      מִמָּרוֹם שָֽׁלַח־אֵשׁ בְּעַצְמֹתַי וַיִּרְדֶּנָּה פָּרַשׂ רֶשֶׁת לְרַגְלַי הֱשִׁיבַנִי אָחוֹר נְתָנַנִי שֹֽׁמֵמָה כָּל־הַיּוֹם דָּוָֽה׃
    → From the fire that was sent upon me, a veil fell over my feet. Then, I was restored to life again. All day long, I remained in that state.
    Lamentations 1:14
      נִשְׂקַד עֹל פְּשָׁעַי בְּיָדוֹ יִשְׂתָּֽרְגוּ עָלוּ עַל־צַוָּארִי הִכְשִׁיל כֹּחִי נְתָנַנִי אֲדֹנָי בִּידֵי לֹא־אוּכַל קֽוּם׃
    → He will punish my sins with his hands. He will humble me on my chest. He will weaken my strength. My Lord, he has given me into his hands; I cannot stand up anymore.
    Lamentations 1:15
      סִלָּה כָל־אַבִּירַי ׀ אֲדֹנָי בְּקִרְבִּי קָרָא עָלַי מוֹעֵד לִשְׁבֹּר בַּחוּרָי גַּת דָּרַךְ אֲדֹנָי לִבְתוּלַת בַּת־יְהוּדָֽה׃
    → All my lords and rulers, stand before me. I command you to be gathered together in one place. Go through the gates of Jerusalem, towards the Temple of God.
    Lamentations 1:16
      עַל־אֵלֶּה ׀ אֲנִי בוֹכִיָּה עֵינִי ׀ עֵינִי יֹרְדָה מַּיִם כִּֽי־רָחַק מִמֶּנִּי מְנַחֵם מֵשִׁיב נַפְשִׁי הָיוּ בָנַי שֽׁוֹמֵמִים כִּי גָבַר אוֹיֵֽב׃
    → For these reasons, my eyes weep. My eyes have been brought down from the sea, as if they are far away from me. My soul is filled with sorrow. My children were once happy, but now they are in pain.
    Lamentations 1:17
      פֵּֽרְשָׂה צִיּוֹן בְּיָדֶיהָ אֵין מְנַחֵם לָהּ צִוָּה יְהוָה לְיַעֲקֹב סְבִיבָיו צָרָיו הָיְתָה יְרוּשָׁלִַם לְנִדָּה בֵּינֵיהֶֽם׃
    → With the tablets in her hands, she found no comfort. Jehovah commanded Jacob to go around them. Jerusalem was among their surroundings.
    Lamentations 1:18
      צַדִּיק הוּא יְהוָה כִּי פִיהוּ מָרִיתִי שִׁמְעוּ־נָא כָל־הָֽעַמִּים וּרְאוּ מַכְאֹבִי בְּתוּלֹתַי וּבַחוּרַי הָלְכוּ בַשֶּֽׁבִי׃
    → The righteous is Jehovah, for he has redeemed me. May all nations hear this! May they see my suffering in my streets and in my homes. Then they will go away from me.
    Lamentations 1:19
      קָרָאתִי לַֽמְאַהֲבַי הֵמָּה רִמּוּנִי כֹּהֲנַי וּזְקֵנַי בָּעִיר גָּוָעוּ כִּֽי־בִקְשׁוּ אֹכֶל לָמוֹ וְיָשִׁיבוּ אֶת־נַפְשָֽׁם׃
    → I called to my lovers: “Oh, you scoundrels! You priests and elders in this city are crying out for food. They want to eat, and they want to settle their souls.”
    Lamentations 1:20
      רְאֵה יְהוָה כִּֽי־צַר־לִי מֵעַי חֳמַרְמָרוּ נֶהְפַּךְ לִבִּי בְּקִרְבִּי כִּי מָרוֹ מָרִיתִי מִחוּץ שִׁכְּלָה־חֶרֶב בַּבַּיִת כַּמָּֽוֶת׃
    → See, LORD, I am tired from all these hardships. My heart is broken because I have been separated from my loved ones. I am like a dead body in the house, without any hope.
    Lamentations 1:21
      שָׁמְעוּ כִּי נֶאֱנָחָה אָנִי אֵין מְנַחֵם לִי כָּל־אֹיְבַי שָׁמְעוּ רָֽעָתִי שָׂשׂוּ כִּי אַתָּה עָשִׂיתָ הֵבֵאתָ יוֹם־קָרָאתָ וְיִֽהְיוּ כָמֽוֹנִי׃
    → They heard that I was tired. There’s no comfort for me at all. All my enemies heard of my suffering. They were pleased because you brought about this day of judgment. It will be like yesterday.
    Lamentations 1:22
      תָּבֹא כָל־רָעָתָם לְפָנֶיךָ וְעוֹלֵל לָמוֹ כַּאֲשֶׁר עוֹלַלְתָּ לִי עַל כָּל־פְּשָׁעָי כִּֽי־רַבּוֹת אַנְחֹתַי וְלִבִּי דַוָּֽי׃
    → All their evil deeds will come before you. They will be punished just as you have punished me for all my sins. For my sorrows and my heart’s pain are too great.
  Lamentations 1 [en]: 22 vv, 4s
    Lamentations 2:1
      אֵיכָה יָעִיב בְּאַפּוֹ ׀ אֲדֹנָי אֶת־בַּת־צִיּוֹן הִשְׁלִיךְ מִשָּׁמַיִם אֶרֶץ תִּפְאֶרֶת יִשְׂרָאֵל וְלֹא־זָכַר הֲדֹם־רַגְלָיו בְּיוֹם אַפּֽוֹ׃
    → How painful it will be for Adonai to throw down Zion from heaven! A beautiful land will be given to Israel, but its blood will not be remembered on that day.
    Lamentations 2:2
      בִּלַּע אֲדֹנָי וְלֹא חָמַל אֵת כָּל־נְאוֹת יַעֲקֹב הָרַס בְּעֶבְרָתוֹ מִבְצְרֵי בַת־יְהוּדָה הִגִּיעַ לָאָרֶץ חִלֵּל מַמְלָכָה וְשָׂרֶֽיהָ׃
    → In his exile, Jacob’s desires were destroyed. He was taken away from the land of the Jews. He arrived in a land without a king or rulers.
    Lamentations 2:3
      גָּדַע בָּֽחֳרִי אַף כֹּל קֶרֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל הֵשִׁיב אָחוֹר יְמִינוֹ מִפְּנֵי אוֹיֵב וַיִּבְעַר בְּיַעֲקֹב כְּאֵשׁ לֶֽהָבָה אָכְלָה סָבִֽיב׃
    → He struck with his sword all the branches of Israel. He turned around to his right side, away from the enemy. And Jacob was like fire that burned brightly. It consumed everything around him.
    Lamentations 2:4
      דָּרַךְ קַשְׁתּוֹ כְּאוֹיֵב נִצָּב יְמִינוֹ כְּצָר וַֽיַּהֲרֹג כֹּל מַחֲמַדֵּי־עָיִן בְּאֹהֶל בַּת־צִיּוֹן שָׁפַךְ כָּאֵשׁ חֲמָתֽוֹ׃
    → His path was difficult; he stood there like a victim. All those who were eager to see him died in the tomb of Zion’s daughter. His fire consumed them all.
    Lamentations 2:5
      הָיָה אֲדֹנָי ׀ כְּאוֹיֵב בִּלַּע יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּלַּע כָּל־אַרְמְנוֹתֶיהָ שִׁחֵת מִבְצָרָיו וַיֶּרֶב בְּבַת־יְהוּדָה תַּאֲנִיָּה וַאֲנִיָּֽה׃
    → Adonai was like a destroyer who plundered Israel, destroying all its cities. He multiplied the sins of the Jews.
    Lamentations 2:6
      וַיַּחְמֹס כַּגַּן שֻׂכּוֹ שִׁחֵת מוֹעֲדוֹ שִׁכַּח יְהוָה ׀ בְּצִיּוֹן מוֹעֵד וְשַׁבָּת וַיִּנְאַץ בְּזַֽעַם־אַפּוֹ מֶלֶךְ וְכֹהֵֽן׃
    → And he neglected the gardens that were meant to be used for worship. He forgot about Jehovah during the festivals of Passover and Shavu’t. In his anger, he rebelled against the king and the priests.
    Lamentations 2:7
      זָנַח אֲדֹנָי ׀ מִזְבְּחוֹ נִאֵר מִקְדָּשׁוֹ הִסְגִּיר בְּיַד־אוֹיֵב חוֹמֹת אַרְמְנוֹתֶיהָ קוֹל נָתְנוּ בְּבֵית־יְהוָה כְּיוֹם מוֹעֵֽד׃
    → May Adonai be abandoned; may his holy place be desecrated. May its palaces be turned into ruins. May the voices of those who worshiped there be silenced in the house of Jehovah today.
    Lamentations 2:8
      חָשַׁב יְהוָה ׀ לְהַשְׁחִית חוֹמַת בַּת־צִיּוֹן נָטָה קָו לֹא־הֵשִׁיב יָדוֹ מִבַּלֵּעַ וַיַּֽאֲבֶל־חֵל וְחוֹמָה יַחְדָּו אֻמְלָֽלוּ׃
    → God thought of destroying the house of Zion. He refused to return his hand from the destruction. They wept together in sorrow.
    Lamentations 2:9
      טָבְעוּ בָאָרֶץ שְׁעָרֶיהָ אִבַּד וְשִׁבַּר בְּרִיחֶיהָ מַלְכָּהּ וְשָׂרֶיהָ בַגּוֹיִם אֵין תּוֹרָה גַּם־נְבִיאֶיהָ לֹא־מָצְאוּ חָזוֹן מֵיְהוָֽה׃
    → Their gates were destroyed on the earth; their palaces were broken apart. Their kings and queens were taken captive in other lands. There was no more any rule or prophet among them. They did not find any sign from Jehovah.
    Lamentations 2:10
      יֵשְׁבוּ לָאָרֶץ יִדְּמוּ זִקְנֵי בַת־צִיּוֹן הֶֽעֱלוּ עָפָר עַל־רֹאשָׁם חָגְרוּ שַׂקִּים הוֹרִידוּ לָאָרֶץ רֹאשָׁן בְּתוּלֹת יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃
    → They sat down on the ground. The elders of Zion rose up. They put sashes around their heads. Then they threw their heads back onto the ground, in Jerusalem.
    Lamentations 2:11
      כָּלוּ בַדְּמָעוֹת עֵינַי חֳמַרְמְרוּ מֵעַי נִשְׁפַּךְ לָאָרֶץ כְּבֵדִי עַל־שֶׁבֶר בַּת־עַמִּי בֵּֽעָטֵף עוֹלֵל וְיוֹנֵק בִּרְחֹבוֹת קִרְיָֽה׃
    → All my eyes are filled with tears; they flow down onto the earth. I am like a flower that has been trampled underfoot. My people’s daughter is covered in blood, and she lies there, bleeding profusely.
    Lamentations 2:12
      לְאִמֹּתָם יֹֽאמְרוּ אַיֵּה דָּגָן וָיָיִן בְּהִֽתְעַטְּפָם כֶּֽחָלָל בִּרְחֹבוֹת עִיר בְּהִשְׁתַּפֵּךְ נַפְשָׁם אֶל־חֵיק אִמֹּתָֽם׃
    → To their mothers, they would say, “Where are the fish and shrimps? They’re trapped in the chaos of the city streets. Their souls are lost in the chaos of the city.”
    Lamentations 2:13
      מָֽה־אֲעִידֵךְ מָה אֲדַמֶּה־לָּךְ הַבַּת יְרוּשָׁלִַם מָה אַשְׁוֶה־לָּךְ וַאֲנַֽחֲמֵךְ בְּתוּלַת בַּת־צִיּוֹן כִּֽי־גָדוֹל כַּיָּם שִׁבְרֵךְ מִי יִרְפָּא־לָֽךְ׃
    → What can I testify to you? You have gone to Jerusalem. You have gone to Zion. I comfort you in the place where the daughter of Zion is. She is like the sea that brings peace. Who can heal you?
    Lamentations 2:14
      נְבִיאַיִךְ חָזוּ לָךְ שָׁוְא וְתָפֵל וְלֹֽא־גִלּוּ עַל־עֲוֺנֵךְ לְהָשִׁיב שְׁבוּתֵךְ וַיֶּחֱזוּ לָךְ מַשְׂאוֹת שָׁוְא וּמַדּוּחִֽים׃
    → Your prophets have seen your suffering and cried out for help, but they did not give you any hope of recovery. They saw that you were in a state of despair.
    Lamentations 2:15
      סָֽפְקוּ עָלַיִךְ כַּפַּיִם כָּל־עֹבְרֵי דֶרֶךְ שָֽׁרְקוּ וַיָּנִעוּ רֹאשָׁם עַל־בַּת יְרוּשָׁלִָם הֲזֹאת הָעִיר שֶׁיֹּֽאמְרוּ כְּלִילַת יֹפִי מָשׂוֹשׂ לְכָל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃
    → They have taken over your shoulders. All those who were on the road have fled. Their heads are now in Jerusalem, this city that was said to be the most beautiful city in all of the world.
    Lamentations 2:16
      פָּצוּ עָלַיִךְ פִּיהֶם כָּל־אוֹיְבַיִךְ שָֽׁרְקוּ וַיַּֽחַרְקוּ־שֵׁן אָמְרוּ בִּלָּעְנוּ אַךְ זֶה הַיּוֹם שֶׁקִּוִּינֻהוּ מָצָאנוּ רָאִֽינוּ׃
    → Their mouths were full of your enemies. They howled and screamed. They said, “We will destroy you!” But today, we have found him. We have seen him.
    Lamentations 2:17
      עָשָׂה יְהוָה אֲשֶׁר זָמָם בִּצַּע אֶמְרָתוֹ אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה מִֽימֵי־קֶדֶם הָרַס וְלֹא חָמָל וַיְשַׂמַּח עָלַיִךְ אוֹיֵב הֵרִים קֶרֶן צָרָֽיִךְ׃
    → Yahweh did as He had promised. He destroyed those who obeyed His words from ancient times. He did not spare them, but He rejoiced over you. Oh, how great is Your glory!
    Lamentations 2:18
      צָעַק לִבָּם אֶל־אֲדֹנָי חוֹמַת בַּת־צִיּוֹן הוֹרִידִי כַנַּחַל דִּמְעָה יוֹמָם וָלַיְלָה אַֽל־תִּתְּנִי פוּגַת לָךְ אַל־תִּדֹּם בַּת־עֵינֵֽךְ׃
    → Their hearts cried out to the Lord of Hotham, daughter of Zion. May the river of tears flow day and night! Please do not let me suffer like this. Do not allow your eyes to weep.
    Lamentations 2:19
      קוּמִי ׀ רֹנִּי בַלַּיְלָה לְרֹאשׁ אַשְׁמֻרוֹת שִׁפְכִי כַמַּיִם לִבֵּךְ נֹכַח פְּנֵי אֲדֹנָי שְׂאִי אֵלָיו כַּפַּיִךְ עַל־נֶפֶשׁ עֽוֹלָלַיִךְ הָעֲטוּפִים בְּרָעָב בְּרֹאשׁ כָּל־חוּצֽוֹת׃
    → Get up in the night to carry out my commands. Let the waters flow down upon you. Be present before Adonai, with your hands raised over your broken spirit. They are covered in hunger, from head to toe.
    Lamentations 2:20
      רְאֵה יְהוָה וְֽהַבִּיטָה לְמִי עוֹלַלְתָּ כֹּה אִם־תֹּאכַלְנָה נָשִׁים פִּרְיָם עֹלֲלֵי טִפֻּחִים אִם־יֵהָרֵג בְּמִקְדַּשׁ אֲדֹנָי כֹּהֵן וְנָבִֽיא׃
    → Look, LORD! See whom you have sinned against. If women eat the fruit of these trees, they will be considered sinners. And if a priest or prophet is killed in the holy place, that too will be considered a sin.
    Lamentations 2:21
      שָׁכְבוּ לָאָרֶץ חוּצוֹת נַעַר וְזָקֵן בְּתוּלֹתַי וּבַחוּרַי נָפְלוּ בֶחָרֶב הָרַגְתָּ בְּיוֹם אַפֶּךָ טָבַחְתָּ לֹא חָמָֽלְתָּ׃
    → They lay down on the ground, young men and old women. They fell in the fields and in the ravines. You killed them on that day. You did not care at all.
    Lamentations 2:22
      תִּקְרָא כְיוֹם מוֹעֵד מְגוּרַי מִסָּבִיב וְלֹא הָיָה בְּיוֹם אַף־יְהוָה פָּלִיט וְשָׂרִיד אֲשֶׁר־טִפַּחְתִּי וְרִבִּיתִי אֹיְבִי כִלָּֽם׃
    → It will be called today, “The Day of the Exiles from All Around.” And it wasn’t in that day that Jehovah showed mercy and compassion towards those who were oppressed and suffered.
  Lamentations 2 [en]: 22 vv, 4s
    Lamentations 3:1
      אֲנִי הַגֶּבֶר רָאָה עֳנִי בְּשֵׁבֶט עֶבְרָתֽוֹ׃
    → I am the proud one who saw the poor in their miserable condition.
    Lamentations 3:2
      אוֹתִי נָהַג וַיֹּלַךְ חֹשֶׁךְ וְלֹא־אֽוֹר׃
    → I drove forward, and it became dark and silent.
    Lamentations 3:3
      אַךְ בִּי יָשֻׁב יַהֲפֹךְ יָדוֹ כָּל־הַיּֽוֹם׃
    → But in me, his hand will always be turned towards me.
    Lamentations 3:4
      בִּלָּה בְשָׂרִי וְעוֹרִי שִׁבַּר עַצְמוֹתָֽי׃
    → In my lips and in my mouth, my secrets are revealed.
    Lamentations 3:5
      בָּנָה עָלַי וַיַּקַּף רֹאשׁ וּתְלָאָֽה׃
    → He built me up, and I rose to my feet.
    Lamentations 3:6
      בְּמַחֲשַׁכִּים הוֹשִׁיבַנִי כְּמֵתֵי עוֹלָֽם׃
    → In their thoughts, they keep me captive like a dead body forever.
    Lamentations 3:7
      גָּדַר בַּעֲדִי וְלֹא אֵצֵא הִכְבִּיד נְחָשְׁתִּֽי׃
    → He has mocked me, and I cannot find any way to defend myself against him.
    Lamentations 3:8
      גַּם כִּי אֶזְעַק וַאֲשַׁוֵּעַ שָׂתַם תְּפִלָּתִֽי׃
    → Even though I cry and wail, your prayers still have power.
    Lamentations 3:9
      גָּדַר דְּרָכַי בְּגָזִית נְתִיבֹתַי עִוָּֽה׃
    → I have changed my path in dire ways.
    Lamentations 3:10
      דֹּב אֹרֵב הוּא לִי אֲרִי בְּמִסְתָּרִֽים׃
    → He walks around me in secret.
    Lamentations 3:11
      דְּרָכַי סוֹרֵר וַֽיְפַשְּׁחֵנִי שָׂמַנִי שֹׁמֵֽם׃
    → His ways are cruel, and he has opened my eyes to see clearly.
    Lamentations 3:12
      דָּרַךְ קַשְׁתוֹ וַיַּצִּיבֵנִי כַּמַּטָּרָא לַחֵֽץ׃
    → His path was difficult, but he set me up as a ladder to climb up.
    Lamentations 3:13
      הֵבִיא בְּכִלְיוֹתָי בְּנֵי אַשְׁפָּתֽוֹ׃
    → He brought with him the sons of Aspaht.
    Lamentations 3:14
      הָיִיתִי שְּׂחֹק לְכָל־עַמִּי נְגִינָתָם כָּל־הַיּֽוֹם׃
    → I would play music for all nations, every day.
    Lamentations 3:15
      הִשְׂבִּיעַנִי בַמְּרוֹרִים הִרְוַנִי לַעֲנָֽה׃
    → Help me in the midst of difficulties; guide me along the right path.
    Lamentations 3:16
      וַיַּגְרֵס בֶּֽחָצָץ שִׁנָּי הִכְפִּישַׁנִי בָּאֵֽפֶר׃
    → And he settled in the land of Shinar. He built his city there.
    Lamentations 3:17
      וַתִּזְנַח מִשָּׁלוֹם נַפְשִׁי נָשִׁיתִי טוֹבָֽה׃
    → And my soul was abandoned by its master; it was in a state of wretchedness.
    Lamentations 3:18
      וָאֹמַר אָבַד נִצְחִי וְתוֹחַלְתִּי מֵיְהוָֽה׃
    → And he said, “I am forever lost; I begin my journey from Jehovah.”
    Lamentations 3:19
      זְכָר־עָנְיִי וּמְרוּדִי לַעֲנָה וָרֹֽאשׁ׃
    → Remember my sorrows and my hardships.
    Lamentations 3:20
      זָכוֹר תִּזְכּוֹר וְתָשׁוֹחַ עָלַי נַפְשִֽׁי׃
    → Remember, and remember also; may my soul be comforted.
    Lamentations 3:21
      זֹאת אָשִׁיב אֶל־לִבִּי עַל־כֵּן אוֹחִֽיל׃
    → This is what I commit to my heart.
    Lamentations 3:22
      חַֽסְדֵי יְהוָה כִּי לֹא־תָמְנוּ כִּי לֹא־כָלוּ רַחֲמָֽיו׃
    → The mercy of Jehovah, for they did not stop, because His compassion was not shown to them.
    Lamentations 3:23
      חֲדָשִׁים לַבְּקָרִים רַבָּה אֱמוּנָתֶֽךָ׃
    → For those who are new to this, your truth is truly great.
    Lamentations 3:24
      חֶלְקִי יְהוָה אָמְרָה נַפְשִׁי עַל־כֵּן אוֹחִיל לֽוֹ׃
    → The parts of Jehovah said, “My soul shall be placed upon him.”
    Lamentations 3:25
      טוֹב יְהוָה לְקוָֹו לְנֶפֶשׁ תִּדְרְשֶֽׁנּוּ׃
    → May the Lord be good to Kovu, and may he guide us.
    Lamentations 3:26
      טוֹב וְיָחִיל וְדוּמָם לִתְשׁוּעַת יְהוָֽה׃
    → May they be good and righteous, and may their names be blessed by Jehovah.
    Lamentations 3:27
      טוֹב לַגֶּבֶר כִּֽי־יִשָּׂא עֹל בִּנְעוּרָֽיו׃
    → It is good for the shepherd to carry his lambs on his shoulders.
    Lamentations 3:28
      יֵשֵׁב בָּדָד וְיִדֹּם כִּי נָטַל עָלָֽיו׃
    → He sits alone and suffers because he has been taken away from him.
    Lamentations 3:29
      יִתֵּן בֶּֽעָפָר פִּיהוּ אוּלַי יֵשׁ תִּקְוָֽה׃
    → It will be given in the form of a gift, but there will still be a request.
    Lamentations 3:30
      יִתֵּן לְמַכֵּהוּ לֶחִי יִשְׂבַּע בְּחֶרְפָּֽה׃
    → He will give him life, and he will be rejoiced in his humiliation.
    Lamentations 3:31
      כִּי לֹא יִזְנַח לְעוֹלָם אֲדֹנָֽי׃
    → For he will not abandon his Lord forever.
    Lamentations 3:32
      כִּי אִם־הוֹגָה וְרִחַם כְּרֹב חֲסָדָֽיו׃
    → For he is merciful and full of his kindness.
    Lamentations 3:33
      כִּי לֹא עִנָּה מִלִּבּוֹ וַיַּגֶּה בְנֵי־אִֽישׁ׃
    → For he did not resist from his heart, and the sons of man were destroyed.
    Lamentations 3:34
      לְדַכֵּא תַּחַת רַגְלָיו כֹּל אֲסִירֵי אָֽרֶץ׃
    → To bring under his feet all the prisoners of the earth.
    Lamentations 3:35
      לְהַטּוֹת מִשְׁפַּט־גָּבֶר נֶגֶד פְּנֵי עֶלְיֽוֹן׃
    → To impose judgment upon Elion.
    Lamentations 3:36
      לְעַוֵּת אָדָם בְּרִיבוֹ אֲדֹנָי לֹא רָאָֽה׃
    → To avenge a man in a quarrel, Adonai did not see it.
    Lamentations 3:37
      מִי זֶה אָמַר וַתֶּהִי אֲדֹנָי לֹא צִוָּֽה׃
    → Who said this? And Adonai did not command it.
    Lamentations 3:38
      מִפִּי עֶלְיוֹן לֹא תֵצֵא הָרָעוֹת וְהַטּֽוֹב׃
    → From his mouth shall not come either evil or good.
    Lamentations 3:39
      מַה־יִּתְאוֹנֵן אָדָם חָי גֶּבֶר עַל־חֲטָאָֽיו׃
    → What does a living person desire more than his own sins?
    Lamentations 3:40
      נַחְפְּשָׂה דְרָכֵינוּ וְֽנַחְקֹרָה וְנָשׁוּבָה עַד־יְהוָֽה׃
    → We shall seek our paths again, and they will be discovered. Then we will return to Jehovah.
    Lamentations 3:41
      נִשָּׂא לְבָבֵנוּ אֶל־כַּפָּיִם אֶל־אֵל בַּשָּׁמָֽיִם׃
    → It was carried before our eyes, above the heavens.
    Lamentations 3:42
      נַחְנוּ פָשַׁעְנוּ וּמָרִינוּ אַתָּה לֹא סָלָֽחְתָּ׃
    → We have sinned and wronged others. You, however, did not forgive us.
    Lamentations 3:43
      סַכֹּתָה בָאַף וַֽתִּרְדְּפֵנוּ הָרַגְתָּ לֹא חָמָֽלְתָּ׃
    → They rushed at us with their swords; they attacked us without hesitation. You killed them, but you didn’t spare them at all.
    Lamentations 3:44
      סַכּוֹתָה בֶֽעָנָן לָךְ מֵעֲבוֹר תְּפִלָּֽה׃
    → May the heavens cry out to you from afar, from the depths of heaven.
    Lamentations 3:45
      סְחִי וּמָאוֹס תְּשִׂימֵנוּ בְּקֶרֶב הָעַמִּֽים׃
    → Sachi and Mamos will place us among the nations.
    Lamentations 3:46
      פָּצוּ עָלֵינוּ פִּיהֶם כָּל־אֹיְבֵֽינוּ׃
    → Their mouths have spoken all our evils against us.
    Lamentations 3:47
      פַּחַד וָפַחַת הָיָה לָנוּ הַשֵּׁאת וְהַשָּֽׁבֶר׃
    → Fear and dread were our companions throughout our journey.
    Lamentations 3:48
      פַּלְגֵי־מַיִם תֵּרַד עֵינִי עַל־שֶׁבֶר בַּת־עַמִּֽי׃
    → The tears of water rolled down from my eyes, as I looked at the daughter of my people.
    Lamentations 3:49
      עֵינִי נִגְּרָה וְלֹא תִדְמֶה מֵאֵין הֲפֻגֽוֹת׃
    → My eyes were closed, and I couldn’t see from where the light came from.
    Lamentations 3:50
      עַד־יַשְׁקִיף וְיֵרֶא יְהוָה מִשָּׁמָֽיִם׃
    → Until He looks down from heaven and sees.
    Lamentations 3:51
      עֵינִי עֽוֹלְלָה לְנַפְשִׁי מִכֹּל בְּנוֹת עִירִֽי׃
    → My eyes are blurred with tears for all the daughters of this city.
    Lamentations 3:52
      צוֹד צָדוּנִי כַּצִּפּוֹר אֹיְבַי חִנָּֽם׃
    → My enemy is like a spider that spins its webs to trap others.
    Lamentations 3:53
      צָֽמְתוּ בַבּוֹר חַיָּי וַיַּדּוּ־אֶבֶן בִּֽי׃
    → They were buried in the grave of their lives. Their hands were tied to the stones.
    Lamentations 3:54
      צָֽפוּ־מַיִם עַל־רֹאשִׁי אָמַרְתִּי נִגְזָֽרְתִּי׃
    → I said, “The waters cover my head; I am trapped.”
    Lamentations 3:55
      קָרָאתִי שִׁמְךָ יְהוָה מִבּוֹר תַּחְתִּיּֽוֹת׃
    → I have heard your name, O LORD, from beneath my feet.
    Lamentations 3:56
      קוֹלִי שָׁמָעְתָּ אַל־תַּעְלֵם אָזְנְךָ לְרַוְחָתִי לְשַׁוְעָתִֽי׃
    → Your voice I have heard; may your ears never be silent to my cries for help.
    Lamentations 3:57
      קָרַבְתָּ בְּיוֹם אֶקְרָאֶךָּ אָמַרְתָּ אַל־תִּירָֽא׃
    → You came on the day I called out to you. You said, “Do not be afraid.”
    Lamentations 3:58
      רַבְתָּ אֲדֹנָי רִיבֵי נַפְשִׁי גָּאַלְתָּ חַיָּֽי׃
    → Grace, Adonai, you have reconciled my soul. You have saved my life.
    Lamentations 3:59
      רָאִיתָה יְהוָה עַוָּתָתִי שָׁפְטָה מִשְׁפָּטִֽי׃
    → The LORD saw my suffering and judged it according to His laws.
    Lamentations 3:60
      רָאִיתָה כָּל־נִקְמָתָם כָּל־מַחְשְׁבֹתָם לִֽי׃
    → You have seen all their schemes and all their thoughts.
    Lamentations 3:61
      שָׁמַעְתָּ חֶרְפָּתָם יְהוָה כָּל־מַחְשְׁבֹתָם עָלָֽי׃
    → You have heard the disgrace they deserve, O LORD, for all their wicked plans.
    Lamentations 3:62
      שִׂפְתֵי קָמַי וְהֶגְיוֹנָם עָלַי כָּל־הַיּֽוֹם׃
    → My lips are closed, and they remain sealed upon me every day.
    Lamentations 3:63
      שִׁבְתָּם וְקִֽימָתָם הַבִּיטָה אֲנִי מַנְגִּינָתָֽם׃
    → When they sat down and stood up, I watched them play music.
    Lamentations 3:64
      תָּשִׁיב לָהֶם גְּמוּל יְהוָה כְּמַעֲשֵׂה יְדֵיהֶֽם׃
    → May the Lord restore them to their rightful place, as they deserve.
    Lamentations 3:65
      תִּתֵּן לָהֶם מְגִנַּת־לֵב תַּאֲלָֽתְךָ לָהֶֽם׃
    → Give them your protection and shelter from their evil deeds.
    Lamentations 3:66
      תִּרְדֹּף בְּאַף וְתַשְׁמִידֵם מִתַּחַת שְׁמֵי יְהוָֽה׃
    → He will destroy them with his arrows, and he will wipe them out from under the eyes of Jehovah.
  Lamentations 3 [en]: 66 vv, 7s
    Lamentations 4:1
      אֵיכָה יוּעַם זָהָב יִשְׁנֶא הַכֶּתֶם הַטּוֹב תִּשְׁתַּפֵּכְנָה אַבְנֵי־קֹדֶשׁ בְּרֹאשׁ כָּל־חוּצֽוֹת׃
    → How great is this gold! It makes the best ornaments. The precious stones are used to adorn everything.
    Lamentations 4:2
      בְּנֵי צִיּוֹן הַיְקָרִים הַמְסֻלָּאִים בַּפָּז אֵיכָה נֶחְשְׁבוּ לְנִבְלֵי־חֶרֶשׂ מַעֲשֵׂה יְדֵי יוֹצֵֽר׃
    → The precious children of Zion, who are so numerous, are considered to be creatures of creation, works of the Creator’s hands.
    Lamentations 4:3
      גַּם־תַּנִּים חָלְצוּ שַׁד הֵינִיקוּ גּוּרֵיהֶן בַּת־עַמִּי לְאַכְזָר כַּיְעֵנִים בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃
    → And they also took out the bodies of the slain. They buried them in my land, as a sign of their cruelty.
    Lamentations 4:4
      דָּבַק לְשׁוֹן יוֹנֵק אֶל־חכּוֹ בַּצָּמָא עֽוֹלָלִים שָׁאֲלוּ לֶחֶם פֹּרֵשׂ אֵין לָהֶֽם׃
    → They clung to their straw, hoping for bread during the night. But they had no bread to eat.
    Lamentations 4:5
      הָאֹֽכְלִים לְמַעֲדַנִּים נָשַׁמּוּ בַּחוּצוֹת הָאֱמֻנִים עֲלֵי תוֹלָע חִבְּקוּ אַשְׁפַּתּֽוֹת׃
    → The food for the travelers was stored in the corners of the houses, on top of piles of trash.
    Lamentations 4:6
      וַיִּגְדַּל עֲוֺן בַּת־עַמִּי מֵֽחַטַּאת סְדֹם הַֽהֲפוּכָה כְמוֹ־רָגַע וְלֹא־חָלוּ בָהּ יָדָֽיִם׃
    → And the punishment for my people became greater than the suffering of Sodom. It was a moment of great pain, and no one could heal them with their hands.
    Lamentations 4:7
      זַכּוּ נְזִירֶיהָ מִשֶּׁלֶג צַחוּ מֵחָלָב אָדְמוּ עֶצֶם מִפְּנִינִים סַפִּיר גִּזְרָתָֽם׃
    → May their monks be freed from the ice and snow; may they be freed from the bondage of earth. May their bodies be adorned with pearls.
    Lamentations 4:8
      חָשַׁךְ מִשְּׁחוֹר תָּֽאֳרָם לֹא נִכְּרוּ בַּחוּצוֹת צָפַד עוֹרָם עַל־עַצְמָם יָבֵשׁ הָיָה כָעֵֽץ׃
    → It was dark from the darkness of the night. They couldn’t be seen in the distance. Their bodies were covered with dust; they resembled trees.
    Lamentations 4:9
      טוֹבִים הָיוּ חַלְלֵי־חֶרֶב מֵֽחַלְלֵי רָעָב שֶׁהֵם יָזוּבוּ מְדֻקָּרִים מִתְּנוּבֹת שָׂדָֽי׃
    → The good were the spaces of darkness, compared to the spaces of hunger that were filled with filth from the dung in the fields.
    Lamentations 4:10
