    → You were like a vine that was planted in the field. You grew and multiplied, and I became great. But then, my enemies came against me. Your gates were broken down, and you became a ruin and a desolation.
    Ezekiel 16:8
      וָאֶעֱבֹר עָלַיִךְ וָאֶרְאֵךְ וְהִנֵּה עִתֵּךְ עֵת דֹּדִים וָאֶפְרֹשׂ כְּנָפִי עָלַיִךְ וָאֲכַסֶּה עֶרְוָתֵךְ וָאֶשָּׁבַֽע לָךְ וָאָבוֹא בִבְרִית אֹתָךְ נְאֻם אֲדֹנָי יְהוִה וַתִּהְיִי לִֽי׃
    → And I will pass over you, and I will look at you. Then, in that moment, I will spread my wings over you, and I will cover your shame with them. I will be your lover, and I will enter into a covenant with you. May the Lord say, “May you become mine.”
    Ezekiel 16:9
      וָאֶרְחָצֵךְ בַּמַּיִם וָאֶשְׁטֹף דָּמַיִךְ מֵֽעָלָיִךְ וָאֲסֻכֵךְ בַּשָּֽׁמֶן׃
    → And I will wash you with water, and I will wipe away your blood from you. And I will cover you with dust.
    Ezekiel 16:10
      וָאַלְבִּישֵׁךְ רִקְמָה וָאֶנְעֲלֵךְ תָּחַשׁ וָאֶחְבְּשֵׁךְ בַּשֵּׁשׁ וַאֲכַסֵּךְ מֶֽשִׁי׃
    → And I will sew you up, and I will wrap you in cloth. I will also bathe you in water, and I will cover you with cloth.
    Ezekiel 16:11
      וָאֶעְדֵּךְ עֶדִי וָאֶתְּנָה צְמִידִים עַל־יָדַיִךְ וְרָבִיד עַל־גְּרוֹנֵֽךְ׃
    → And I will bind you with ropes on your hands, and tie you tightly to your legs.
    Ezekiel 16:12
      וָאֶתֵּן נֶזֶם עַל־אַפֵּךְ וַעֲגִילִים עַל־אָזְנָיִךְ וַעֲטֶרֶת תִּפְאֶרֶת בְּרֹאשֵֽׁךְ׃
    → And I will put cloves on your lips, and perfumes on your ears. And I will adorn you with beauty on your head.
    Ezekiel 16:13
      וַתַּעְדִּי זָהָב וָכֶסֶף וּמַלְבּוּשֵׁךְ שֵׁשׁ וָמֶשִׁי וְרִקְמָה סֹלֶת וּדְבַשׁ וָשֶׁמֶן אָכָלְתְּ וַתִּיפִי בִּמְאֹד מְאֹד וַֽתִּצְלְחִי לִמְלוּכָֽה׃
    → And she used gold, silver, and other precious metals; she also used silk, cloth, and leather. She ate everything that was available to her. She became very rich and successful as a queen.
    Ezekiel 16:14
