    → And he went forth to you in your beauty, for it is all in my power. I have placed this curse upon you, O Lord Jehovah.
    Ezekiel 16:15
      וַתִּבְטְחִי בְיָפְיֵךְ וַתִּזְנִי עַל־שְׁמֵךְ וַתִּשְׁפְּכִי אֶת־תַּזְנוּתַיִךְ עַל־כָּל־עוֹבֵר לוֹ־יֶֽהִי׃
    → I will worship you with my whole heart, and I will pour out all my love upon you. I will give all my devotion to everyone who comes near you.
    Ezekiel 16:16
      וַתִּקְחִי מִבְּגָדַיִךְ וַתַּֽעֲשִׂי־לָךְ בָּמוֹת טְלֻאוֹת וַתִּזְנִי עֲלֵיהֶם לֹא בָאוֹת וְלֹא יִהְיֶֽה׃
    → And take some of your tears, and use them to make makeup for your eyes. Apply it on your eyelids, but do not let it get on your skin.
    Ezekiel 16:17
      וַתִּקְחִי כְּלֵי תִפְאַרְתֵּךְ מִזְּהָבִי וּמִכַּסְפִּי אֲשֶׁר נָתַתִּי לָךְ וַתַּעֲשִׂי־לָךְ צַלְמֵי זָכָר וַתִּזְנִי־בָֽם׃
    → And you shall take all your jewels from gold and silver, which I have given you. Then you shall make statues of them as memorials.
    Ezekiel 16:18
