    → And I went to the children of Egypt, your neighbors. I grew up among them, and I made my presence known in order to provoke you.
    Ezekiel 16:27
      וְהִנֵּה נָטִיתִי יָדִי עָלַיִךְ וָאֶגְרַע חֻקֵּךְ וָאֶתְּנֵךְ בְּנֶפֶשׁ שֹׂנְאוֹתַיִךְ בְּנוֹת פְּלִשְׁתִּים הַנִּכְלָמוֹת מִדַּרְכֵּךְ זִמָּֽה׃
    → And behold, I laid my hand on you, and I cut off your hair. I will also cast you away among your enemies, those daughters of Philistia who have gone astray from your path.
    Ezekiel 16:28
      וַתִּזְנִי אֶל־בְּנֵי אַשּׁוּר מִבִּלְתִּי שָׂבְעָתֵךְ וַתִּזְנִים וְגַם לֹא שָׂבָֽעַתְּ׃
    → And I spoke to the sons of Ashur, because you did not repent. And they also did not repent.
    Ezekiel 16:29
      וַתַּרְבִּי אֶת־תַּזְנוּתֵךְ אֶל־אֶרֶץ כְּנַעַן כַּשְׂדִּימָה וְגַם־בְּזֹאת לֹא שָׂבָֽעַתְּ׃
    → And he carried your baggage to the land of Canaan, as it was written. But even then, he did not rest.
    Ezekiel 16:30
      מָה אֲמֻלָה לִבָּתֵךְ נְאֻם אֲדֹנָי יְהוִה בַּעֲשׂוֹתֵךְ אֶת־כָּל־אֵלֶּה מַעֲשֵׂה אִשָּֽׁה־זוֹנָה שַׁלָּֽטֶת׃
    → What am I to say to your daughter? O Lord Jehovah, for all these deeds you have done, it’s like a wicked woman who is causing trouble.
    Ezekiel 16:31
