    → As for horses, they should be seen as such; and just as arrows are also seen as arrows.
    Joel 2:5
      כְּקוֹל מַרְכָּבוֹת עַל־רָאשֵׁי הֶֽהָרִים יְרַקֵּדוּן כְּקוֹל לַהַב אֵשׁ אֹכְלָה קָשׁ כְּעַם עָצוּם עֱרוּךְ מִלְחָמָֽה׃
    → Like the sound of horses galloping atop the mountains, they danced like the sound of fire burning through hard wood. They were like a people filled with anger and hatred, ready for battle.
    Joel 2:6
      מִפָּנָיו יָחִילוּ עַמִּים כָּל־פָּנִים קִבְּצוּ פָארֽוּר׃
    → From his side, nations of all kinds would gather together. They would form a great crowd.
