    → May the LORD hear your words and take notice of what you say. May you do good and evil in accordance with what the LORD desires. Who is this judge, if not the God of judgment?
  Malachi 2 [en]: 17 vv, 3s
    Malachi 3:1
      הִנְנִי שֹׁלֵחַ מַלְאָכִי וּפִנָּה־דֶרֶךְ לְפָנָי וּפִתְאֹם יָבוֹא אֶל־הֵיכָלוֹ הָאָדוֹן ׀ אֲשֶׁר־אַתֶּם מְבַקְשִׁים וּמַלְאַךְ הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר־אַתֶּם חֲפֵצִים הִנֵּה־בָא אָמַר יְהוָה צְבָאֽוֹת׃
    → I am sending my angel to guide me along the path before me. Suddenly, he will come to the house of the Lord, where you seek Him. And the angel of the covenant, whom you desire, will also be there. Now, say: “The Lord, the Almighty, says this.”
    Malachi 3:2
      וּמִי מְכַלְכֵּל אֶת־יוֹם בּוֹאוֹ וּמִי הָעֹמֵד בְּהֵרָֽאוֹתוֹ כִּֽי־הוּא כְּאֵשׁ מְצָרֵף וּכְבֹרִית מְכַבְּסִֽים׃
    → And who fills his days with activities? And who stands at his doorstep, as if he were fire that burns brightly and flames that burn fiercely?
    Malachi 3:3
